{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations","id":195976,"title":"Why would a solar ever use evocations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-12T21:02:27-07:00","id":195976,"title":"Why would a solar ever use evocations?","content":"I know that the devs have said that the solars will be the best at them, but wouldn't a solar be smarter to just invent a melee charm for whatever evocations their weapon might do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1174-the-lidless-eye-that-sees","name":"The Lidless Eye That Sees","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:24:38-07:00","id":196011,"title":"","content":"If a Solar wants to turn the ground into molten lava, he can't do that with his own charms. He can do it with Sorcery or an Evocation (or possibly a really weird Martial Art).<br /> <br /> One reason to pick up Evocations for the same reason you pick up Sorcery or Martial Arts. To do things you <i>can't</i> normally do with charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:34:22-07:00","id":196014,"title":"","content":"First an evocation might be easier to work with than creating a charm.<br /> <br /> Second, as I understand evocations, they might grant powers that aren't normally part of a purview for a solar. For example one of the powers of the artifact diaklave Volcano Cutter is called &quot;Pyroclastic Holocaust Judgement&quot; call me crazy but that sounds very much like a power that ends with a massive eruption of fire and molten rock. Which would very much be in line for a fire aspect dragon blood, but a solar doesn't normally have access to attacks that go off like a volcano.<br /> <br /> Third there's a level of pride in being able to access and use a weapon better than anyone else. I mean lets face it the honest pride in being able to use a weapon to the point where everything about it is open and available to use has gotta be good for the ego.<br /> <br /> Fourth, maybe it never occurred to the solar that a power like that could be done. The solar could make a melee charm too but they might have learned of the principles of it through using an evocation and then created a charm because its a really useful power and they want it even if the weapon is lost for some reason.<br /> <br /> Finally, who knows it might cost less to use evocations than charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:54:51-07:00","id":196024,"title":"","content":"Why use a daiklaive when you can use Glorious Solar Saber? Why wear armor when you can use Iron Kettle Body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/246-wretch","name":"Wretch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:55:45-07:00","id":196025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lidless Eye That Sees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations#post195976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the devs have said that the solars will be the best at them, but wouldn't a solar be smarter to just invent a melee charm for whatever evocations their weapon might do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know little enough about Evocations to say for sure, but some possible reasons include:<br /> <br /> (1) Evocations can allow for out-of-native-theme effects (can't be a Solar Charm; Solar Charms can't conjure magma, for example).<br /> (2) Evocations may be able to be bought from a separate XP pool than Charms. If Solar XP is implemented (it was mentioned previously and is listed on the 3e wiki) as a second pool to buy things aside from Solar native Charms, double your pleasure to increase your power. <br /> (3) Evocations may be always-on effects for the person who unlocked them. As in, no mote/Willpower costs. That's a definite advantage over a Charm.<br /> (4) Adding on to (3), Evocations may not have a Type, unlike Charms, so may provide bonuses to Combos that an otherwise-equal Charm could not because of Type rules for Combos (not being able to use 2 Simples at the same time, for example, or Supplementals only being able to be used to supplement the Simple in the Combo).<br /> (5) Coolness factor? Seems like 3e is taking the view that &quot;native Charms are not like techniques.&quot; Maybe Evocations are more like techniques (always work in a certain way, possibly flashy in a way that Solar Charms, as extensions of the inherent Awesomeness of the user, may not be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:56:44-07:00","id":196028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196011#post196011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason to pick up Evocations for the same reason you pick up Sorcery or Martial Arts. To do things you <i>can't</i> normally do with charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Case in point, while various tables' tastes may vary, I suspect most would be gobsmacked if someone tried to present homebrew Solar Melee Charms that did this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sample of Evocations: The daiklave called Stormcaller sleeps in its sheathe. When drawn, a hurricane begins to form overhead. Its Evocations both draw from the storm's ferocity, and add to it. The character must carefully draw down and disperse the storm before sheathing Stormcaller. Apex Evocation involves sheathing the weapon early to disperse the storm in a massive directional stormblast capable of flooring a behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>NOTE: The hurricane isn't a special effect. It is an actual hurricane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-13-2014, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:08:52-07:00","id":196033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wretch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196024#post196024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why use a daiklaive when you can use Glorious Solar Saber? Why wear armor when you can use Iron Kettle Body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Commitment costs, for one thing. GSS is overpriced compared to a solid metal weapon, and you can get comparable stats with a good MM pick and a harmonic adapter.<br /> <br /> Action economy for another. GSS is Simple, welp, there's your action and your Charm use, summoning your weapon. Same for IKB next round. Versus just wearing armor and carrying a weapon, which is not going to turn heads in a lot of places anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:13:02-07:00","id":196034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lidless Eye That Sees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations#post195976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the devs have said that the solars will be the best at them, but wouldn't a solar be smarter to just invent a melee charm for whatever evocations their weapon might do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because developing a Charm that makes my sword impossible to pick up unless you're true of heart (read: possessing my Exaltation shard) doesn't really make sense, but developing an evocation to do the same does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:43:31-07:00","id":196041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196034#post196034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because developing a Charm that makes my sword impossible to pick up unless you're true of heart (read: possessing my Exaltation shard) doesn't really make sense, but developing an evocation to do the same does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? that is a good Evocation for a Goremaul based on Thor's Hammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:56:35-07:00","id":196047,"title":"","content":"Once you have seen an Evocation, you will immediately understand why they cannot be replicated through native Solar Charms. They're just...totally two different dogs. One day is a master swordsman on the level of Zatoichi, Kenshin Himura, or Cloud Strife. The other dog goes woof and triggers a massive explosion of lava. That kind of dogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T23:04:18-07:00","id":196048,"title":"","content":"Solars use Evocations for the same reason Captain America uses his Shield or Thor uses his hammer. Sure, they're super soldiers/demi gods who can kick all kinds of ass in without it, but sometimes you just want to slam a large hunk of metal in to someone's face for that satisfying &quot;clang&quot;*, ya know?<br /> <br /> *Said clang may or may not involve conjuring up the primal fury of a hurricane or volcano, use at risk of the surrounding countryside/population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T23:22:27-07:00","id":196061,"title":"","content":"If evocations were like charms they would be called 'charms'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T01:09:28-07:00","id":196108,"title":"","content":"1: It's evocative of many stories that Exalted is inspired by. Items like Son Wukong's Staff, Mjolnir, Excalibur, maybe even Hercules' invulnerable lion king cloak are all items that can be recreated with evocations. Having a hero who carries around this legendary weapon with which he can cut mountains in half is absolutely something that is appropriate for a game like Exalted.<br /> <br /> 2: It makes the player interested in their weapon. Not to harp on D&amp;D or anything, but, for example, if my character wields a greatsword in D&amp;D that was given to him by his father in his dying breath, well in-character I have a reason to keep that weapon. But out of character, I will pick up a greatsword+1 as soon as possible, because it's mechanically more useful for me. Having Evocations makes your weapon scale with your character, in a sense, so that you have a mechanical reason to be attached to your weapon, if you want your character to be.<br /> <br /> 3: Having a sword that can turn the battlefield into a burning hellscape with a short chant and a couple of swings is something that makes sense as an evocation, but not as a charm.<br /> <br /> 4: It is really, really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T02:03:57-07:00","id":196153,"title":"","content":"In the 2e corebook there are a bunch of artifact weapons with unusual powers from the first age. It seems to me that evocations are a way of bringing that sort of theme into the forefront and making it standard operating procedure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:27:37-07:00","id":196185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196041#post196041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? that is a good Evocation for a Goremaul based on Thor's Hammer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:48:25-07:00","id":196191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196047#post196047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you have seen an Evocation, you will immediately understand why they cannot be replicated through native Solar Charms. They're just...totally two different dogs. One day is a master swordsman on the level of Zatoichi, Kenshin Himura, or Cloud Strife. The other dog goes woof and triggers a massive explosion of lava. That kind of dogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the best kind of dogs.<br /> <br /> Wait no. Second best. Forgot about puppies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T05:28:38-07:00","id":196202,"title":"","content":"I'm still trying to figure out what sort of evocation arrays, (trees? Templates?) to assign to Lightning Crystal, Obsidiium, Thousand Fold Steel, and Unicorn bone. The Heartwood is easy wounds that turn flesh to wood, entangling branches or roots grabbing your foe, or even thrusting you bade into the earth and having the nearby plants rise and walk on their roots as a battlegroup that serves you. <br /> <br /> I seriously wish I could see any MM info.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T05:53:26-07:00","id":196224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196202#post196202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still trying to figure out what sort of evocation arrays, (trees? Templates?) to assign to Lightning Crystal, Obsidiium, Thousand Fold Steel, and Unicorn bone. The Heartwood is easy wounds that turn flesh to wood, entangling branches or roots grabbing your foe, or even thrusting you bade into the earth and having the nearby plants rise and walk on their roots as a battlegroup that serves you.<br /> <br /> I seriously wish I could see any MM info.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the Evocations are completely dependent on the materials used in the created artifacts. It was already said that Magical Materials will get a whole slew of unique bonuses. Yeah, it makes sense if your sword was tempered in the blood of a volcano-god that it's abilities might be volcano-related, but that doesn't always have to be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T06:03:04-07:00","id":196227,"title":"","content":"Generally, magic weapons in fiction derive their abilities from three things: Construction (what they are made of/how they were made eg mijolnir), Things they've killed (some weapons go as far as picking up new abilities like Mega Man) and previous owners (the sword of a volcano god gets volcano based powers. This one kind of merges into the first a bit.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T06:18:24-07:00","id":196228,"title":"","content":"We have been told the the MM will be a contributing factor to Evocations. Either providing some of your array, or modifiers (bennies) to the Evocations that your artifact has. What exactly it is and how it works we don't exactly know yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T06:42:20-07:00","id":196235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196227#post196227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things they've killed (some weapons go as far as picking up new abilities like Mega Man)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's been hinted at that Volfer's insane daiklaive picked up Evocations from slaying a demon and becoming hell-tainted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T07:45:08-07:00","id":196273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196025#post196025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1) Evocations can allow for out-of-native-theme effects (can't be a Solar Charm; Solar Charms can't conjure magma, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh...I honestly hope that this is the <i>least</i> reason to use Evocations. But then, I despise Black Mirror Revelation and Primordial Principal Emulation and think that they never should have been written. I'm a bit hopeful in that regard, though, if only because it would be rather silly to par Eclipse charmsteal down to a vetted list and then turn around and say &quot;Solars can steal any theme and call it an evocation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","user":"Coik","date":". 07-13-2014, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T07:46:48-07:00","id":196294,"title":"","content":"Solar Melee Charms, don't traditionally make you just a master swordsman. They do give you essence wave strike attacks (a la Cloud Strife) and the Glorious Solar Saber, and more tentatively, the fan home brew GSS expansions that move into terrifying scale mass essence attacks. And the same with Solar Brawl, Archery, etc.<br /> <br /> (Obviously I'm not actually trying to tell folks here who know more about writing Charms this as if it's some amazing observation, but it's the jump off for my next para!).<br /> <br /> So I do wonder how much those, and the promise of those, will stay. Evocations still having plenty of appeal whether they stay or not.<br /> <br /> Like I assume that if you wanted to build up a custom GSS expansion Charm where you charge up your GSS, jam into the ground, it sinks in and then moments later the earth a radius around you explodes with damaging sunlight lasers (i.e. the classic &quot;Sky Dragon Slash&quot; move - <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OqNYlgtsVNQ\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OqNYlgtsVNQ</a>) you can still do that in Ex3e, and its not like, evocation-only, territory or anything.<br /> <br /> I do hope that evocations don't encourage weapon stealing by non-evocation users, to even the balance, or even between different evocation users. I'm not so keen on weapon stealing plots. I don't think those are particularly common in Exalted as is though, so it would seem unlikely evocations would make them more common.<br /> <br /> (Also, kind of strange that it occurs to me that Evocations seem like they could make Solars with appropriate elemental artefacts in a sense more &quot;airbender-y&quot; than DBs who wear their elemental might internally (which DBs doing I do totally approve of and all). And this enhances the case for DBs not to really depend on bending Charms to make them unique.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T08:00:46-07:00","id":196301,"title":"","content":"What I'm wondering, now that I think about it, is how magical materials will key into all this. Will the elemental effects be from jade weapons? I can easy see how evocations will work in those cases; big elemental effects like exploding in lava or causing storms to brew overhead are obvious and cool. The question then would be why a Dragon-Blooded would want to use a jade weapon, if it's just going to grant elemental effects like they can presumably already make.<br /> <br /> Similarly, what kind of evocations would orichalcum weapons get, and why would a Solar want to use them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T08:23:16-07:00","id":196309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196025#post196025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we know little enough about Evocations to say for sure, but some possible reasons include:<br /> <br /> (2) Evocations may be able to be bought from a separate XP pool than Charms. If Solar XP is implemented (it was mentioned previously and is listed on the 3e wiki) as a second pool to buy things aside from Solar native Charms, double your pleasure to increase your power.<br /> (3) Evocations may be always-on effects for the person who unlocked them. As in, no mote/Willpower costs. That's a definite advantage over a Charm.<br /> (4) Adding on to (3), Evocations may not have a Type, unlike Charms, so may provide bonuses to Combos that an otherwise-equal Charm could not because of Type rules for Combos (not being able to use 2 Simples at the same time, for example, or Supplementals only being able to be used to supplement the Simple in the Combo).</div> </div> </div> </div>On these 2-4, none of these are *bad*, but they do feel like &quot;Use these because there is an arbitrary rule that incentivizes you to&quot; kind of bonuses.<br /> <br /> They don't just come from the nature of evocations as distinct from Charms in a deep, elegant and simple way*, unlike evocations specifically being able to do what Charms can't, or look cool in a certain way doing it even when they can.<br /> <br /> Having two pools of Charms that feed off separate exp / resource and separate activations *would* encourage you to use both. But would that actually be interesting design?<br /> <br /> *I think of deep, simple and elegant as when you look at a thing and think &quot;Could it really be any other way?&quot; and at the same time its full of interesting possibilities and combinations. And you don't think &quot;Aha. That's a button to make me use / do ...&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196273#post196273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh...I honestly hope that this is the <i>least</i> reason to use Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it is that a Solar couldn't really have the &quot;Daiklaive of Generic Siderealness and power of Fate&quot; that gives him access to all these generic Sidereal effects over Fate.<br /> <br /> He could have Daiklaive of Endings that has its own specific aesthetics beyond that which allows him to use certain powers over Endings that aren't the same as or better than those in the Sidereal set (no matter how far he branches down his evocation tree).<br /> <br /> But that's not the same as being a Sidereal and having the ability they have to mix Endings with all their Endings Caste abilities, and access to Astrology (which should hopefully be actually good) and all their other Sidereal trees, MA, a certain relationship with Heaven and other Sidereal Exalted, a certain attitude... <br /> <br /> And its not really the same as having power over the Fate of Endings in your soul, either.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe there would be a lot more overlap if a Solar picked up tons of Sidereal bling, but I'm hoping it won't really be like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T08:44:28-07:00","id":196313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196273#post196273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh...I honestly hope that this is the <i>least</i> reason to use Evocations. But then, I despise Black Mirror Revelation and Primordial Principal Emulation and think that they never should have been written. I'm a bit hopeful in that regard, though, if only because it would be rather silly to par Eclipse charmsteal down to a vetted list and then turn around and say &quot;Solars can steal any theme and call it an evocation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocations are not Solar-only, no more than Sorcery or Martial Arts are.<br /> <br /> And let me flip it around and put it like this: It is bad to say &quot;you cannot create an artifact to do X&quot;, &quot;you cannot create a spell to do X&quot; or &quot;you cannot create a martial art to do X&quot; simply because an unrelated splatbook on the other end of the gameline also has a take on X. This is because a <i>theme</i> (as it applies to types of Exalted) is more than just one charm or one power or one aspect of your flavor; it's the overarching narrative behind the whole subject in question. Volcano Cutter presumably does fiery things, but to pretend that that makes Fire Aspects obsolete is to ignore everything that makes Dragon-Blooded what they are and (probably) everything that makes Volcano Cutter what it is.<br /> <br /> The Eclipse charmshare was turned into a vetted list primarily for balance and design reasons (specifically, it sucks to have to design every charm around the possibility that Solars will get it), plus perhaps some thematic concerns over what it implies about what charms really are, in-setting. But Solars continue to be the most straightforward exemplar of all sorts of 'human' heroes, and this includes, say, being a hero who is primarily defined as master of a legendary sword that can master fire, or one what can reflect visions of the future along the mirrored edge of its blade. Such artifacts will have unique and distinct stories, which means not directly and completely overlapping with someone else's overarching story -- a daiklave called &quot;LunarExalt&quot; which gives you all the powers of a Lunar Exalt is obviously dumb.<br /> <br /> But the purpose of playing (for instance) a Sidereal is to explore the Sidereal narrative. That overarching narrative should be unique to them, and the game should avoid things that would actually damage it (eg. revealing someone who is flatly better at SMA than Sidereals, or giving powerful future-predictive powers to nearly everyone so mastering it no longer has any special meaning.) But that doesn't require saying &quot;only Sidereals can predict the future&quot; or anything like that, and making that statement would be bad for the game (because there are many angles to explore predictive magic from.) If what you're looking for is &quot;I can do some broadly-defined thing Solars can't ever do by any means, no matter what, even through sorcery or artifacts&quot;, then... you're SOL, mostly, because that isn't a healthy desire for the gameline.<br /> <br /> With two important caveats, though: There <i>are</i> limitations on what Solars can do, of course. But those limitations are based around what preserves the Solar narrative rather than in an attempt to make you feel better about playing something else. And all of this applies to everyone, not just Solars -- that is to say, this is the reason Alchemicals can have really good crafting charms even though Solars had craft in the core; this is why Sidereals can turn into a raven or Infernals can take on monstrous Shintai forms even though shapeshifting is so central to Lunars. Solars tend to be the most flexible splat in terms of what you can build with them, but the entire game is designed around &quot;tell this interesting story&quot;, not &quot;make sure the asshole across the table doesn't get his dirty foot on your story.&quot; If you're worried about -- say -- a Solar player introducing Wayfinder, the Sword of Wisdom in your game and focusing on its evocations in a way that might conflict with your Sidereal's role in the story, that's an issue to be resolved at your table, not an underlying issue with the game (because you get the same issue whenever two people want to do the same general thing.)<br /> <br /> The other important caveat is the term 'broadly-defined'. As you define things more narrowly and specifically, they become increasingly inextricable from one specific story, which makes it generally dumb to reuse them elsewhere -- eg. 'manipulate fate' is broad, but 'Sidereal Astrology' is specific; a sword that can cut through fate is cool, but a needle that can weave Sidereal Astrology directly and specifically should probably only work for Sidereals, because making that available to other people genuinely would undercut the Sidereal narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-07-2015, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:04:06-07:00","id":196322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196309#post196309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it is that a Solar couldn't really have the &quot;Daiklaive of Generic Siderealness and power of Fate&quot; that gives him access to all these generic Sidereal effects over Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, putting aside the fact that I'd be willing to lay money that the One-Handed Grand Goremaul of Other Exalted's Entire Charmset But Better And Only Useable By Solars will be the very first homebrew evocation weapon written up, I don't <i>think</i> Hamsterweheel and friends would be silly enough to write something like that for a book. But ya'know, BMR and PPE are enough to put that little niggling doubt in the back of my mind...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He could have Daiklaive of Endings that has its own specific aesthetics beyond that which allows him to use certain powers over Endings that aren't the same as or better than those in the Sidereal set (no matter how far he branches down his evocation tree). </div> </div> </div>This I think I would be fine with, so long as it's a two-way street. So long as other Exalts can use weapons that draw on Solar themes. Which I wish I could feel was a given, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and access to Astrology (which should hopefully be actually good) </div> </div> </div>Hahahahaha.<br /> <br /> Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:11:15-07:00","id":196331,"title":"","content":"I was a bit dubious about that myself, Coik, but then I realized that if that was the case if just make all my characters Solars and save money by not buying splat books. I'll just make a solar with shape changing armor, a cape of the stars and a sword of fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:12:46-07:00","id":196332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196322#post196322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, putting aside the fact that I'd be willing to lay money that the One-Handed Grand Goremaul of Other Exalted's Entire Charmset But Better And Only Useable By Solars will be the very first homebrew evocation weapon written up...</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Coik, we get it, you don't like Solars.</i><br /> <br /> Seriously, this is like the fourth anti-Solar post out of you in as many posts*; what's got you in this mood today?<br /> <br /> *Admittedly, one of 'em was a few days ago, but before this relapse you had a decent streak of <i>not</i>-Solar-ranting going for a good bit there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-13-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:34:10-07:00","id":196340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196322#post196322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, putting aside the fact that I'd be willing to lay money that the One-Handed Grand Goremaul of Other Exalted's Entire Charmset But Better And Only Useable By Solars will be the very first homebrew evocation weapon written up, I don't <i>think</i> Hamsterweheel and friends would be silly enough to write something like that for a book. But ya'know, BMR and PPE are enough to put that little niggling doubt in the back of my mind...</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be silly, the very first homebrew evocation weapon will be the the <i>Holy Flamin' Frost-Brand Gronk-Slayin' Vorpal Hammer o Woundin' an' Returnin' an' Shootin' Lightnin-Out-Yer Bum</i>.<br /> <br /> However, I am totally going to write up my own custom daiklave, named <i>Better Than You At Everything</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-13-2014, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:40:52-07:00","id":196357,"title":"","content":"Evocations are meant in large part to fill out regions that your native Charmset does not provide for, which is...a lot of regions! In this respect they're similar to Sorcery and Martial Arts in allowing you to make effects that are iconic to <i>your character</i> but fall outside your ordinary purview. This is particularly desirable for Solars because they don't have any especially ostentatious &quot;power themes&quot; that would clash with evocations.<br /> <br /> The difference between Evocations and Sorcery/MA is that they're all different paradigms. Evocations are about having a Kickass Magic Sword, clearly, so it seems likely that they will appeal to people who are more focused on the &quot;I have a sword and know how to use it&quot; thing than &quot;I know kung fu&quot;, and they build a legend around the sword itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196273#post196273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh...I honestly hope that this is the <i>least</i> reason to use Evocations. But then, I despise Black Mirror Revelation and Primordial Principal Emulation and think that they never should have been written. I'm a bit hopeful in that regard, though, if only because it would be rather silly to par Eclipse charmsteal down to a vetted list and then turn around and say &quot;Solars can steal any theme and call it an evocation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this complaint puzzling because the game already lets you do this with MA or Sorcery, the other two big &quot;splat-agnostic power suites&quot;. The idea that Evocations would somehow radically warp things in a way that MA and Sorcery <i>don't</i> seems unlikely; certainly unlikely given what we've heard at this point. You can make a ridiculous MA too -- legend has it that the first draft of Fivefold Shadow Hand was as large as a BWC-enhanced Yozi tree and included every power ever attributed to a ninja -- but this is not really a problem with MA so much as it is an inevitability of having a game where people are allowed to use unpublished powers.<br /> <br /> Solars can steal any theme and turn it into an Evocation...provided it's appropriate for an Evocation (likely a fairly stringent filter). Also: everyone else can do this, too. Being &quot;the best&quot; at Evocations seems to mean that Solars get access to those Adamant Circle Evocations, which if true means that they don't get to the Solar-only toys until they've gone through a lot of generally-accessible stuff. Solars can also practice Fire Dragon Style, or cast Bone Lion -- just like Lunars, Sidereals, Abyssals, and Infernals.<br /> <br /> (It surprises me that you cite BMR as an illustration of this complaint, since, while it <i>was</i> the only Charmshare ability in the game that actually allowed you to steal other splats' thematics effectively, it only worked on Abyssals, and they got a charm that did the <i>exact same thing</i> for Solar charms.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-13-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T10:34:12-07:00","id":196423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196357#post196357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It surprises me that you cite BMR as an illustration of this complaint, since, while it <i>was</i> the only Charmshare ability in the game that actually allowed you to steal other splats' thematics effectively, it only worked on Abyssals, and they got a charm that did the <i>exact same thing</i> for Solar charms.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Even more amusingly, Abyssals got their version, <i>Unconquered Hero's Faith</i>, long before BMR was printed (although it referenced a hypothetical Solar version, it didn't confirm that it was possible.)<br /> <br /> But people complained <i>way</i> more about BMR... admittedly, probably because it was for a splat that people actually played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-20-2015, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T10:52:07-07:00","id":196428,"title":"","content":"My personal theory on this is that outside of Solars (the kings of Evocations) you can only reach adamant level with a weapon of a material that is native to you. Dragon Blooded for example could only reach admanet with their own brand of jade, sapphire with any jade.<br /> <br /> So yes a Solar could get fire based powers if he atunes to a Red Jade weapon, but unless that was also a blue jade not air powers. And so on down the spiral. Plus I think it was hinted at, that you need an intimacy to your weapon of a certain strength in order to tap into an Evocation.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a lunar might be able to tap into saphire level Oricalcum influenced evocations but use Adamant level Moon silver. even if her weapon is a composite of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 07-13-2014, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T10:52:31-07:00","id":196429,"title":"","content":"The light of the Unconquered Sun shining out through the darkness of an Abyssal exaltation makes sense. The reverse, less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T11:15:35-07:00","id":196443,"title":"","content":"BMR is one of the instances of the Mirror keyword being an awful idea where it goes in the opposite of the normal direction: instead of Abyssals getting a watered-down Solar Charm, Solars get a Charm that makes absolutely no sense aside from sheer &quot;Solars are the bestest Exalts ever and should have all the powers&quot;. It's hard to argue whether BMR or PPE is worse from a conceptual standpoint, in both cases the justifications offered for why Solars would be able to do the things they cover are tenuous at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T11:22:07-07:00","id":196465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196332#post196332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Coik, we get it, you don't like Solars.</i><br /> <br /> Seriously, this is like the fourth anti-Solar post out of you in as many posts*; what's got you in this mood today?<br /> <br /> *Admittedly, one of 'em was a few days ago, but before this relapse you had a decent streak of <i>not</i>-Solar-ranting going for a good bit there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, because complaining about complaining is in any way better.<br /> <br /> I'm aware of the hypocrisy of this, but I'm cranky.<br /> <br /> And it's not anti-solar when it was a geniune issue and problem with the previous edition written in part by the people that are now devs. It's a simple fact and worry.<br /> <br /> And at least HIS post is on topic(Once again, I invoke the cranky clause.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T11:24:46-07:00","id":196486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo;n196357<br /> <br /> (It surprises me that you cite BMR as an illustration of this complaint, since, while it [I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">was[/I] the only Charmshare ability in the game that actually allowed you to steal other splats' thematics effectively, it only worked on Abyssals, and they got a charm that did the <i>exact same thing</i> for Solar charms.)</div> </div> </div> </div>PPE and Power From Darkness, both Solar unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":".  Get outta there, the! No one wants you around. 07-13-2014, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:03:36-07:00","id":196510,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Just a thought, but you know Ascendancy Mantle Of (Yozi) form Broken Winged Crane? What if we made it so learning to access a Yozi's charms using PPE had downsides like the ones that charm causes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:10:06-07:00","id":196513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196322#post196322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Well, putting aside the fact that I'd be willing to lay money that the One-Handed Grand Goremaul of Other Exalted's Entire Charmset But Better And Only Useable By Solars will be the very first homebrew evocation weapon written up</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I'm not too worried about that. No system can be so completely balanced that it is completely immune to shitty home-brew. Anyone with a mind to can write broken hoembrew even if the base system is balanced. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">But homebrew isn't threatening to game line balance; </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">the great thing about shitty home-brew is how irrelevant it is to the published game line. So in that manner, it won't affect future products (unlike, say, shittily done canon Charmsets, of which there were several in 2e). If that kind of home-brew pops up, I feel for the other people who have to play with the guy who designs it, but it doesn't make me worried that it's going to effect the canon game line. And certainly while there will probably be home-brew Evocations possible, it sounds like there will be enough options to pick from when designing an Artifact that home-brew won't be the first thing on peoples' minds, it'll be finding cool Evocation combinations from the presented examples in the Core and Arms.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196322#post196322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I think I would be fine with, so long as it's a two-way street. So long as other Exalts can use weapons that draw on Solar themes. Which I wish I could feel was a given, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think of it in a different way. Take the kickstarter example, Volcano Cutter. Volcano Cutter <i>seems </i>to be kinda like &quot;my sword strikes evoke the fury of lava,&quot; which is not necessarily the same as &quot;my sword strikes are effective fire Elemental Bolt or draw from DB themes.&quot; Ditto with the one that's like &quot;when it is drawn, a literal hurricane starts above me.&quot; I just hope it branches into non-elemental things, which is probably likely when you're not talking about elementalized jade weapons. And it even seems like a moon silverweapon's Evocations are't all going to be about moonsilver or Lunar themes. Some might be some (like, maybe Evocations relating to mutability and fluidness, but specifically NOT shapeshifting), but some are probably also going to be about the themes of the weapon, its crafter, and its wielder, even if it just so happens to be made of moonsilver.<br /> <br /> It'd be a bad idea to let Artifact Evocations just steal wholesale from other splats' themes, let alone replicate their Charms - that was such a criticized part of Eclipse charmshare the last 2 eds, where every Charm had to be balaced against Solars getting it, where Knacks existed because they needed to be kinda Charms but also definitively outside of the reach of Eclipses...it was a huge mess, and if the Eclipse anima is getting revamped to prevent that issue, I doubt the debs are just going to reintroduce it with Evocations.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:12:07-07:00","id":196514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196486#post196486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PPE and Power From Darkness, both Solar unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how PPE works, but Power from Darkness was similar to Eclipse charmshare in it was nearly useless for stealing anyone else's gimmicks. Even the errata'd version, which is actually usable, is really bad for actually copying other people's schticks. As with most other forms of charmshare, it has one use, and that is using low-hanging charms that weren't intended for Solar consumption to create game-breaking &quot;engines&quot;. Like, yes, a Solar <i>can</i> learn Avoidance Kata...if she's essence 7 occult 7, and she has analyzed it and all its prerequisites with AESS, and she is willing to commit 9m and take double limit forever, and she doesn't mind never using any of those powers at the same time as other charms (great fun if you're playing paranoia combat). But that's not even remotely worthwhile. If you're going to use it, you're almost certainly going to be aiming at mechanical interactions rather than niche or thematics.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can try really hard to be a poser to get much worse results than the person I'm imitating <i>and</i> much worse results than just being myself&quot; isn't the kind of gimmick anyone should be resentful or envious of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-13-2014, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:46:48-07:00","id":196526,"title":"","content":"PPE makes you pay 1 Limit at the start of a scene in which you use Yozi Charms, in exchange for being able to learn every Charm in a single Yozi's tree without need for a tutor. You have to take it multiple times to get more than one Yozi, but two purchases gives you access to an Infernal's entire favored charmset. If you've managed to break the Great Curse on yourself, you can use PPE to get a non-Yozi Primordial's Charms, i.e. Autochthon or Gaia's Charms.<br /> <br /> In both cases, BMR especially, there isn't actually a lot of reason to take a lot of Abyssal or Infernal Charms because Solar Charms are better. From a mechanical standpoint they are therefore not technically broken, or at least not much more so than being an E6 Solar in the first place. What's irritating about them is the statement they make, that Solars should be able to take entire charmsets for themselves so that they can be even better than everyone else than they already are. BMR can at least be excused for being developers mindlessly following the Mirror keyword, PPE is just plain gluttony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:57:40-07:00","id":196530,"title":"","content":"There's also the system interaction issues. A lot of the Yozi charms are permanents, non-activation buffs. Meaning, that combined with other passive, Solar buffs that normally the Infernal wouldn't be able to get, you can get some preeetty broken combos going.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, got it in one, Couch. It's much less the result, it's the thematic statement that's made. Same with Power From Darkness, something I was trying to formulate, and failing, to respond to above.<br /> <br /> It's also a precidence issue. These are Essence 6/7 charms, and we aallll know that they just get more crazy as you go up in essence, so...yeah, upgrades that just laugh at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T13:07:56-07:00","id":196533,"title":"","content":"I always took BMR and PFD more as expressions of Solar hubris -- that is, they're not so much about &quot;anything you can do, I can do better&quot; (because in fact you usually do the copied effect <i>worse</i>) as a sort of taboo-breaking mad-scientist refusal to accept any sort of limitation on yourself. This is a theme that underlies many of the essence 6+ charms in Scroll of Errata, whose underlying thesis seems to be &quot;Essence 6+ Charms are those Charms best not taken&quot;, but the BMR and PFD express it very broadly. In all cases these powers still leave you worse off than the people you're imitating, <i>and</i> worse off than you would be if you just did your own thing, so it doesn't really come off to me as &quot;Solars are cadging everyone else's gimmicks&quot; as &quot;Solars can go to a huge amount of trouble to violate even this most fundamental of restrictions, but it will probably lead them to unpleasant places&quot;. The message with most of these effects isn't &quot;Solars are awesome&quot; or &quot;Solars are better than you,&quot; it's &quot;Solars don't know when to leave well enough alone.&quot; PPE sounds pretty dumb, though, admittedly!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T13:36:49-07:00","id":196539,"title":"","content":"As a note for you, Gayo, both BMR and PPE are from the same book, Glories: Sol. Literately one after another, if you wanted to go read and you have that book. (If this is coming off condensending or anything, my apologies, I'm really just trying to tell you where you can find it)<br /> <br /> <br /> And your view is...I can see that being a reasonable one, but it's never FELT that way to me, yanno?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T14:26:47-07:00","id":196555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196539#post196539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note for you, Gayo, both BMR and PPE are from the same book, Glories: Sol. Literately one after another, if you wanted to go read and you have that book. (If this is coming off condensending or anything, my apologies, I'm really just trying to tell you where you can find it)<br /> <br /> <br /> And your view is...I can see that being a reasonable one, but it's never FELT that way to me, yanno?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually we have dev statements to that effect.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to chime in because I'm the one who pushed these Charms and one of them was a recycle from one cut out of Abyssals. Holden was gracious enough to include them.<br /> <br /> In the case of Abyssal access, it serves a variety of functions. First, it allows you to have the Anakin Meets the Sand People effect where the Solar delivers Hungry Tiger Technique for the first three actions of his flurry and finishes off with artful maiming onslaught and all his Circle-mates are looking at him like &quot;Damn!&quot;<br /> <br /> It also completes a symmetry, that when you turn Solar Essence inside out, you get an Abyssal. The ramifications of that are terrifying, wherever you go with it. Or perhaps this isn't quite the case, but instead an Abyssal is what happens when Solars delve too hard into necromancy on their long fall down. It's not remotely beyond the pale to imagine a followup Charm that you can buy that lets you change yourself into an Abyssal completely on your own.<br /> <br /> The Charm also incidentally lets you do a First Age &quot;Abyssals&quot; game or include still living pre-Deathlords with hints of what they will become.<br /> <br /> As for the primordial Charm, the prerequisites are the first explanation. Sorcery is a pattern that the Primordials made for themselves and which they were the greatest wielders of right up until Mara said &quot;Here, catch!&quot; to Brigid. Primordial Charms are very often sorcery-like, if not outright sorcerous, and certainly do a variety of things Solar Charms simply can't do for matters of theme (rather than power). For a solar sorcerer who wants to press harder and deeper into this power, the path to cosmic power (Primordial Charms) beckons past Essence 5. It's a sideways leap because Solars are at once the most human of Creation's Exalted and yet have achieved all of the most intense transhuman feats in the setting. It's a paradox, but it's a cool paradox.<br /> <br /> We also know by way of the existence of Green Sun Princes that Solar Exaltation is strong enough to power Infernal Charms and can do so. An Infernal has nearly infinite sideways direction to grow because each Charm set they unlock will be radically different. Plus, because multiple sets can plug each other's Charm holes, diversity is the Green Sun Prince weapon for fighting with the reliable perfection of a Solar. However, if you tack on Solar Charms to plug the holes as a development option for any Infernal, then this short-circuits the omni-yozi evolution push. Thus, the Infernal set functions best as intended without this kind of broad access.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Solars don't have that kind of flexibility within their own Charms. They can go up and punch right through any ceiling, but they can't innately push their Charms in an alien path. For them to go sideways, they need to do something other than be Solars. Making the Charm Essence 6 ensures that by the time you get it, you already have your core competencies fleshed out and what you're looking for is exotic tricks to flavor you, basically new &quot;spells&quot; to add to your repertoire as a sorcerer. But they are expensive and you have elder Solar Charms you could buy instead for cheaper, so once again, the Solar is encouraged to stay a Solar, but given the opportunity to be something\u2026else.<br /> <br /> Oh, and bang for your buck, those two Charms open up more options for Solars than any other Charms they have, so in a book with limited space, this was a plus.<br /> <br /> The final reason I have for those two Charms is more personal and it stems from the fact that Infernal Charms are studies in abuse and various responses to abuse. When I was a child, if I screwed up and I knew it and I was sent to my room because I was in trouble, I would hit myself and bang myself against the wall. It wasn't an attention plea. It was me deciding that punishing myself worse than my parents would punish me gave me the power. It was me doing this to myself. Not someone else doing something to me. It was a tiny crum of self-empowerment at a time when I didn't feel that I had any (through no fault of my parents, bless them). What I also understand now is that it was a form of self-abuse. Even as I was protagonizing myself in my story, I was also ensuring that story was a tragedy.<br /> <br /> These &quot;damnation&quot; Charms take that principle to a Solar level. &quot;I will not be dragged into the darkness by some old ghost or an Abyssal; I'll drag MYSELF into the darkness and fuck you all.&quot; Also: &quot;I will not be your akuma slave; I will steal your secrets (that incidentally carry weaknesses that make me more like you and spread your concepts, but no matter).&quot; Even at their most degenerate fraying of every physical law they can get their shiny hands on, Solars should have the capacity to forge ahead in the direction they please. If that means they want to avoid having a Deathlord throw them into the Well of Oblivion by taking a swan dive of their own volition, that is still very much within the Solar prerogative. Solars are the captains of their own destiny. That also means they can get it wrong. Or weird. Or maybe perversely right. Who can say? All I know is that Solars are just as capable of self-abuse as spouse abuse and these two Charms capture that idea better than anything else I could think of. </div> </div> </div>Personally I always liked PPE because it offers one of the few ways I can imagine for a Solar to break the Great Curse without first going Abyssal; take the Negi Springfield route of dabbling in forbidden magic, and then (because we're not necessarily telling a morality tale about bad powers being bad so don't touch them) dive in so deep that you come out the other side as something completely different, like a pseudo-Infernal or a really weird devil tiger-ish thing and oh by the way you shed your limit track at some point, so while you're not shining perfection anymore you're also <i>more yourself</i> than you ever have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","user":"HK-87","date":". 07-13-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T14:38:50-07:00","id":196578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196322#post196322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But ya'know, BMR and PPE are enough to put that little niggling doubt in the back of my mind...</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily, Michael Goodwin wrote those, and he no longer writes for Exalted.<br /> So now you must dance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T15:43:54-07:00","id":196591,"title":"","content":"HK, are you familiar with Death of the Author?<br /> <br /> And MG, that doesn't really help any, given as the quotes above note, Holden explicitly approved of the charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T16:43:48-07:00","id":196604,"title":"","content":"Regardless of what I'd think of their actual utility, I'd be extremely wary of approaching those Charms in terms of Michael Goodwin's apparent usual impulse to come up with mechanics that he can attach elaborate punchy statements to after the fact. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">given as the quotes above note, Holden explicitly approved of the charms</div> </div> </div> </div> That's an era in which Holden approved all kinds of things he looks askance at now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T17:20:30-07:00","id":196610,"title":"","content":"Perhaps. But it's the grounded, behavor that was acted on. He can say he's changed, and I legit hope he has, but until he's actively acted on it, that's what he's judged by. Action, not words.<br /> <br /> Just...one of my things, yanno? Quite probably overly judgmental, just the line my life has lead me to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T19:45:42-07:00","id":196642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196513#post196513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I think of it in a different way. Take the kickstarter example, Volcano Cutter. Volcano Cutter <i>seems </i>to be kinda like &quot;my sword strikes evoke the fury of lava,&quot; which is not necessarily the same as &quot;my sword strikes are effective fire Elemental Bolt or draw from DB themes.&quot; Ditto with the one that's like &quot;when it is drawn, a literal hurricane starts above me.&quot; I just hope it branches into non-elemental things, which is probably likely when you're not talking about elementalized jade weapons. And it even seems like a moon silverweapon's Evocations are't all going to be about moonsilver or Lunar themes. Some might be some (like, maybe Evocations relating to mutability and fluidness, but specifically NOT shapeshifting), but some are probably also going to be about the themes of the weapon, its crafter, and its wielder, even if it just so happens to be made of moonsilver.<br /> <br /> It'd be a bad idea to let Artifact Evocations just steal wholesale from other splats' themes, let alone replicate their Charms - that was such a criticized part of Eclipse charmshare the last 2 eds, where every Charm had to be balaced against Solars getting it, where Knacks existed because they needed to be kinda Charms but also definitively outside of the reach of Eclipses...it was a huge mess, and if the Eclipse anima is getting revamped to prevent that issue, I doubt the debs are just going to reintroduce it with Evocations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with you. I would love to see exactly how the evocation system plays and how weapon style effects it. Do Grim Cleavers have different types of Evocations available than Daiklaves? I have said that, and it sounds like, the way Evocations will work is they will give us template evocations (Like Powers in Savage worlds) we fill in the details and that creates the final evocation.<br /> <br /> Either that or I hope they do what they did with Shadowrun and it's custom created spells system and give the formulas for determining mote costs, fair durations, ect. (Or at least I'm hoping they have one.) That way GM's have less to worry about balancing because so long as the player used the formula the Evocation will be balanced. It can be as unique as they like, but it will still be balanced by having them follow some clearly spelled out rules for evocation creation.<br /> <br /> Though I do wonder if Plunge a blade into the ground and raise a small army of trees as my warriors is even possible as an evocation. I think that would be cool for a Saphire level evocation for Iron Heartwood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T20:00:16-07:00","id":196644,"title":"","content":"Lunar evocations could probably have something to do with transmutation rather than shapeshifting specifically, just as one option among many. I'm remembering Ruby Rose's scythe shedding rose petals instead of blood in the first RWBY trailer and thinking that would be a neat way to get rid of the evidence of an assassination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T04:53:10-07:00","id":196665,"title":"","content":"Or transorm the weapon it's self. Shapeshift it between being a Daiklave, a Lyre, and a power bow? As examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T05:19:00-07:00","id":196688,"title":"","content":"I think a sensible thing to do would be to have X-splat-only evocations <i>and</i> X-Splat-gets-cheaper evocations. Shapeshifting weapons sounds like something common enough to let solars have (particualrly if it only has 2 or 3 forms), but I'd certainly give lunars a discount on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T05:43:45-07:00","id":196699,"title":"","content":"Weren't Evocations something specific to the weapon and not to a splat? With the Solars being able to tap into the fullest potential of a weapon, and thus having access to the strongest Evocations? This whole Lunar evocation thing doesn't sound right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T05:50:57-07:00","id":196702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196699#post196699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't Evocations something specific to the weapon and not to a splat? With the Solars being able to tap into the fullest potential of a weapon, and thus having access to the strongest Evocations? This whole Lunar evocation thing doesn't sound right to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, this is true.<br /> <br /> Though I took &quot;lunar evocations&quot; to mean &quot;of weapons made by Lunars and/or with Moonsilver&quot;. (In the same way Lunar Manses are &quot;of Luna&quot;, not necessarily &quot;Lunar-only&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  Celestia disapproves. 07-14-2014, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:03:12-07:00","id":196722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196665#post196665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or transorm the weapon it's self. Shapeshift it between being a Daiklave, a Lyre, and a power bow? As examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was also a Lunar Charm in the past, and I think most appropriate for them honestly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196688#post196688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a sensible thing to do would be to have X-splat-only evocations <i>and</i> X-Splat-gets-cheaper evocations. Shapeshifting weapons sounds like something common enough to let solars have (particualrly if it only has 2 or 3 forms), but I'd certainly give lunars a discount on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree with hardline splat-specific Evocations for the following reason. Evocations are built into the weapon, not in the user (unlike Charms); the user just accesses the weapon's Evocations. It's feasible for a Solar to be using moonsilver, or a DB to be using soulsteel, and doesn't make much sense if some of those Evocations are unavailable just because the character is a DB and not an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, Volcano Cutter has at least one Evocations in its tree that has a Solar Charm as a prereq. Possibly implying that the Evocation builds off of or adds functionality to uses of that Charm. I think that's evidence of an <i>effective </i>splat-specific Evocation since nobody else can get that Solar Charm (barring like BMR-type stuff for Solars existing in, say, the 3e Abyssal charm set or whatever...which may happen, but I kinda doubt it). But that still sits better with me than the idea that a lot of powers on an Artifact will be splat-specific, versus a couple low-hanging-fruit Evocations that have a native Charm as a prereq.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:11:47-07:00","id":196726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196702#post196702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, this is true.<br /> <br /> Though I took &quot;lunar evocations&quot; to mean &quot;of weapons made by Lunars and/or with Moonsilver&quot;. (In the same way Lunar Manses are &quot;of Luna&quot;, not necessarily &quot;Lunar-only&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my meaning too, but I seem to remember Volcano Cutter having one or two evocations attached to the tree that only a dragonblood could use because they had DB charms as a prerequisite. Therefore &quot;Lunar evocations&quot; could probably mean either weapons made of moonsilver or evocations with Lunar charms as a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:25:35-07:00","id":196731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196423#post196423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more amusingly, Abyssals got their version, <i>Unconquered Hero's Faith</i>, long before BMR was printed (although it referenced a hypothetical Solar version, it didn't confirm that it was possible.)<br /> <br /> But people complained <i>way</i> more abut BMR... admittedly, probably because it was for a splat that people actually played.</div> </div> </div> </div>My single biggest problem with Black Mirror Revelation vs. Unconquered Hero's Faith was that it treated Limit and Resonance costs as interchangeable and ignored the difference between the two mechanics. <br /> <br /> Resonance is something you're supposed to manage on a meta level, the entire Abyssal playstyle assumes you're aware of how close you are to killing loved ones on the other side of the world, alerting the Aerial Legion to your presence or being posessed by the Neverborn and measuring your rebellion against your dark fate carefully otherwise it'll be crushed before you can make any real progress meanwhile Limit is intended to be a sword of damocles that you never quite know when it'll fall.<br /> <br /> Charms that cause Limit gain are potentially beneficial in a way that charms that cause Resonance aren't because they allow you to have a bout of murderous rage, calculating cruelty (or what have you) at a moment where it can seem appropriate or even justified rather than blowing up at the wrong people.<br /> <br /> This is just confounded by the fact that the Holy keyword means that several Solar charms are unusable to Abyssals anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:35:31-07:00","id":196736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196726#post196726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my meaning too, but I seem to remember Volcano Cutter having one or two evocations attached to the tree that only a dragonblood could use because they had DB charms as a prerequisite. Therefore &quot;Lunar evocations&quot; could probably mean either weapons made of moonsilver or evocations with Lunar charms as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, there were also a couple that required Call the Blade. I wonder if this is (in part) what is meant by &quot;solars are the best at evocations&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:38:41-07:00","id":196738,"title":"","content":"Well, with the new version of resonance from shards they <i>are </i>sort of interchangeable. <br /> <br /> Aside from that maybe using abyssal charms this way could cause solars to gain resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:47:46-07:00","id":196747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196726#post196726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my meaning too, but I seem to remember Volcano Cutter having one or two evocations attached to the tree that only a dragonblood could use because they had DB charms as a prerequisite. Therefore &quot;Lunar evocations&quot; could probably mean either weapons made of moonsilver or evocations with Lunar charms as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right in principle, though it was actually a Solar Charm in the example Evocation array, &quot;Call the Blade.&quot; Even so, the spoiler also said Evocation arrays are meant to be flexible depending on the user. We'll see for sure when the book is (or books are) out, but I've speculated this means the Solar Charm may be shorthand less for &quot;only Solars can access this&quot; and more for &quot;only those with this or an analogous Charm can access this.&quot;<br /> <br /> This could indeed mean that if something has, say, a Lunar Charm in it, the particular Lunar Charm may determine if it's something a Solar or other splats can use, or it may be something so particular to Lunars that nobody else really can (outside maybe a particular sort of Exigent or other custom Exalt). I'd think this would be particularly apt for Sidereals. Yes, yes, &quot;worst at Evocations,&quot; but there are many things that could mean, such as that they may be wholly/largely restricted to Starmetal, but some of their more unique Charms could take such artifacts in directions pretty much nobody else can go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-14-2014, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T08:11:55-07:00","id":196791,"title":"","content":"I don't expect to see Resonance in its 2e form at all. Resonance as-written forces a certain play style, in the same way as &quot;Sidereals losing astrology if they go rogue&quot; and those forced play style renders all kinds of stories impossible, which is bad. The 3e devs seem to see how the system forcing a certain play style, because the author though that was the Only Appropriate Play Style, is a terribly toxic concept.<br /> <br /> Ditto for Limit Break, for other reasons: 2e did it kind of nonsensically, so I expect 3e's version to make more narrative sense. Gaining Limit intentionally to control your eruptions is only a real benefit when the system defines eruptions as &quot;I have been upset a lot and now just resisted some UMI so I run away to the top of this mountain, shave my head, and meditate on asceticism...but only for today, because otherwise it would be too disruptive.&quot; As if that mechanic isn't disruptive enough!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:21:44-07:00","id":196852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196313#post196313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations are not Solar-only, no more than Sorcery or Martial Arts are.<br /> <br /> And let me flip it around and put it like this: It is bad to say &quot;you cannot create an artifact to do X&quot;, &quot;you cannot create a spell to do X&quot; or &quot;you cannot create a martial art to do X&quot; simply because an unrelated splatbook on the other end of the gameline also has a take on X.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to say that artifacts that can do W can never be made. I'm trying to express that I don't want to see, six months to a year down the line, that the best way to build a Lunar is to make a Solar and take evocations for artifacts X, Y and Z. And why wouldn't you? Artifact Y has evocations that are better than Lunar shapeshifting, even if that wasn't the intent, and X and Z are almost as good; getting Solar mote pools and Charms out of it as well more than makes up for it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm talking from a purely mechanical standpoint there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If what you're looking for is &quot;I can do some broadly-defined Solars can't ever do by any means, no matter what, even through sorcery or artifacts&quot;, then... you're SOL, mostly, because that isn't a healthy desire for the gameline. </div> </div> </div>I don't want to say &quot;Evocations can never do this not ever.&quot; Mostly, I just don't want evocations to be Anything-You-Can-Do-I-Can-Do-Better effects like Loom-Snarling Deception, or outright power steals like PPE or BMR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't be silly, the very first homebrew evocation weapon will be the the <i>Holy Flamin' Frost-Brand Gronk-Slayin' Vorpal Hammer o Woundin' an' Returnin' an' Shootin' Lightnin-Out-Yer Bum</i>. </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're going to go cross-game munchking, then we need to get Steve Jackson involved.<br /> <br /> Hmmpth...I wonder if Exalted Munchkin would sell...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But people complained <i>way</i> more abut BMR... admittedly, probably because it was for a splat that people actually played. </div> </div> </div>Visibility, too. If I remember right, Unconquered Hero's Faith is buried in the Abyssals fatsplat. PPE and BMR are right next to each other in a comparatively much thinner book.<br /> <br /> And also, it gets tedious to type. That's why I still use &quot;Solaroids&quot; instead of typing out &quot;Solars, Abyssals and Infernals&quot; every single time.<br /> <br /> I'm busy! I have things to do!<br /> <br /> So it's imperative that my time spent on virtual corkboards talking about slaying imaginary dragon be as efficient as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196357#post196357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this complaint puzzling because the game already lets you do this with MA or Sorcery, the other two big &quot;splat-agnostic power suites&quot;. The idea that Evocations would somehow radically warp things in a way that MA and Sorcery <i>don't</i> seems unlikely; certainly unlikely given what we've heard at this point. You can make a ridiculous MA too -- legend has it that the first draft of Fivefold Shadow Hand was as large as a BWC-enhanced Yozi tree and included every power ever attributed to a ninja -- but this is not really a problem with MA so much as it is an inevitability of having a game where people are allowed to use unpublished powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocations are terra incognita. Martial Arts and Sorcery are known factors, to an extent...if nothing else, there's a decent frame of reference for how they worked and influenced the system in the last two editions. To my mind, that gives evocations are higher chance of being the cog that goes in the opposite direction to the rest of the system...<i>some</i> sort of growing pains involving them seems inevitable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196332#post196332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Coik, we get it, you don't like Solars.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, I have been subtly hinting about that for a bit now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously, this is like the fourth anti-Solar post out of you in as many posts*; what's got you in this mood today? </div> </div> </div>Well, I didn't really consider the Merela post so much an anti-Solar post as against players who obsess about their characters' previous incarnations (seriously, that was a big reason I disliked the Kickstarter comic...we got almost no information on the guy in front of us other than he has an annoying verbal tic and like 40 pages of exposition on how cool the guy who had the Exaltation before him was. With that sort of premise I probably would have disliked it no matter what type of Exalt what's-his-face was).<br /> <br /> My posts in this thread I actually tried to moderate, so they were more &quot;Here's a concern I have&quot; and less &quot;fucking Solars ruining the game forever, <i>again</i>.&quot; I was actually thinking that I've been fairly mellow lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:37:22-07:00","id":196866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196852#post196852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not trying to say that artifacts that can do W can never be made. I'm trying to express that I don't want to see, six months to a year down the line, that the best way to build a Lunar is to make a Solar and take evocations for artifacts X, Y and Z. And why wouldn't you? Artifact Y has evocations that are better than Lunar shapeshifting, even if that wasn't the intent, and X and Z are almost as good; getting Solar mote pools and Charms out of it as well more than makes up for it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm talking from a purely mechanical standpoint there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely from a mechanical standpoint, the conclusion there would be, &quot;The Evocations for Artifact Y are bad and need errata,&quot; not &quot;The entire system of Evocations is conceptually busted.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:52:25-07:00","id":196895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196747#post196747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right in principle, though it was actually a Solar Charm in the example Evocation array, &quot;Call the Blade.&quot; Even so, the spoiler also said Evocation arrays are meant to be flexible depending on the user. We'll see for sure when the book is (or books are) out, but I've speculated this means the Solar Charm may be shorthand less for &quot;only Solars can access this&quot; and more for &quot;only those with this or an analogous Charm can access this.&quot;<br /> <br /> This could indeed mean that if something has, say, a Lunar Charm in it, the particular Lunar Charm may determine if it's something a Solar or other splats can use, or it may be something so particular to Lunars that nobody else really can (outside maybe a particular sort of Exigent or other custom Exalt). I'd think this would be particularly apt for Sidereals. Yes, yes, &quot;worst at Evocations,&quot; but there are many things that could mean, such as that they may be wholly/largely restricted to Starmetal, but some of their more unique Charms could take such artifacts in directions pretty much nobody else can go.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that the Call the Blade prereq was less saying you need this charm to get this evocation, and actually saying you don't need the other evocations to access this evocation, if you have Call the Blade. Like it is a short cut to better or more powerful evocations without having to buy all the evocations up to that point. Or the evocation that Call the Blade allows you to skip is similar to Call the Blade in function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:54:02-07:00","id":196898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196736#post196736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, there were also a couple that required Call the Blade. I wonder if this is (in part) what is meant by &quot;solars are the best at evocations&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a really interesting point. I wonder how other exalts would gain access to the sword's powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T10:00:17-07:00","id":196922,"title":"","content":"It seems that approaching Exalts holistically means that you can sometimes have a Lunar Charm which is mechanically more powerful than a Solar Charm and it doesn't make Lunars as a whole stronger because there are all kinds of considerations for complementary effects and synergies between Charms and a character developing Charms. I would imagine that, conversely, it's possible to have a Charm, or even a section of Charms, based around shapeshifting (maybe even a thematically and aesthetically similar to Lunars kind of shapeshifting) accessable via development with an artifact that might individually be mechanically stronger than what a Lunar can do while in no way capturing the actual play style and sense of a Lunar. If Exalted are ideally more than the sum of their parts, than I feel as though occasionally having a certain (external, tool based) access to parts can't really approximate the sense of playing a certain Exalt at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T10:59:06-07:00","id":196973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196191#post196191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are the best kind of dogs.<br /> <br /> Wait no. Second best. Forgot about puppies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about master swordsman lava puppies? And to make it superlative, they're Jack Russels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T11:02:54-07:00","id":196976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196357#post196357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I find this complaint puzzling because the game already lets you do this with MA or Sorcery,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I sincerely hope that this is kind of the last reason to use Evocations. I hope the first reason is that they are awesome. The second is so that I can use really cool evocation based stunts. Charm trees I couldn't create as a Solar? Yeah, that's a reason, but a solid third reason, and not the first and best. Still, a reason I can get behind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T11:20:24-07:00","id":196985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196699#post196699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't Evocations something specific to the weapon and not to a splat? With the Solars being able to tap into the fullest potential of a weapon, and thus having access to the strongest Evocations? This whole Lunar evocation thing doesn't sound right to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds perfect if its not a Lunar Evocation, but a Moonsilver Evocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T03:27:46-07:00","id":197737,"title":"","content":"I know in the case of my posts I may have said &quot;Lunar Evocation&quot; when meaning Moonsilver Evocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T00:39:04-07:00","id":198648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196852#post196852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to say that artifacts that can do W can never be made. I'm trying to express that I don't want to see, six months to a year down the line, that the best way to build a Lunar is to make a Solar and take evocations for artifacts X, Y and Z. And why wouldn't you? Artifact Y has evocations that are better than Lunar shapeshifting, even if that wasn't the intent, and X and Z are almost as good; getting Solar mote pools and Charms out of it as well more than makes up for it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm talking from a purely mechanical standpoint there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that that falls into the same category as &quot;won't people just make an Exigent that is just like Lunars, but better?&quot; Artifacts are meant to be unique. They might overlap with certain tricks various splats have, but their overarching direction is likely to be their own. You can make the Sword of the Sun, but it probably won't give you Solar Stealth. If an artifact is directly overlapping with the <i>core</i> of an Exalt type (rather than just overlapping with some of what they can do), that's probably not an artifact that most games would allow by default.<br /> <br /> Remember -- artifacts still have attunement costs. Therefore, if your plan is to attune to three powerful artifacts which, collectively, cover large portions of what's important to you from the Lunar charmset, you're probably going to end up with most of your mote pool locked up in them. If you swap between them, then you're not really a <i>Lunar</i>, in the same way that Alchemicals might have some individual charms that can compete with Solars at Solar stuff in certain areas, but can't equip them all at once -- that's already a clear way in which you're functioning distinctly from a regular Lunar. Not to mention you're also spending a bunch of background dots (or craft-efforts) that could have been spent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Finally, artifacts, by definition, can be taken away from you. It's not easy, sure, but there's a fundamental difference between &quot;I am the mighty shapeshifter, moon-blessed master of the wilds&quot; and &quot;I am a mighty Solar Exalt with the legendary blade that lets me assume ten-thousand shapes.&quot; It seems great until you run into someone with epic larceny or disarming charms or something and the next thing you know you're standing there empty-handed looking stupid and unable to shapeshift.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With all that said, remember that Exalted are defined by what they cannot do as much as by what they can. Part of the reason to play a Lunar Exalt is because you like the Lunar story; and part of that story means <i>not being a Solar</i>. That means that worrying that a hypothetical Solar Exalt with a cloak of shapeshifting might, in certain ways and under certain circumstances, be better than you is silly -- if you care so much about Solar charms, play a Solar; if someone wants to play a shapeshifter who uses Solar charms, I don't feel that the game needs to kick them in the nads by telling them that artifacts and sorcery don't do that or by trying to keep those charms from 'overshadowing' Lunars.<br /> <br /> If someone is trying to play that character in a game where you're the one Lunar in a Solar group, hit them with a book. If the mere thought that that character <i>might</i> exist somewhere and might sometimes be better than you while having abilities that overlap with yours is intolerable to you, well, so what. I don't feel that they'll ever be a better way to <i>play a Lunar</i>, which is what really matters.<br /> <br /> (Remembering that as I said, relying on artifacts to shapeshift already has a significant built-in thematic limitation in that you, well, are reliant on those artifacts; and that has mechanical / balance implications. The story of the Solar with a daiklave that lets him take on ten-thousand shapes is cool, but it is not a Lunar story -- no Lunar has to worry about someone disarming or stealing their ability to shapeshift. If you want to play someone who has shapeshifting as the intrinsic, inseparable core of their being, you still have to play a Lunar, even before you get to the fact that Lunars probably have a different take on shapeshifting, probably have other additional themes, etc.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I'll step back and point out again that the issue here continues to be Lunars specifically (in that the books have failed to really make them distinct enough on their own) -- you wouldn't have the same problem with Sidereals, say, because even a Solar with the sword of prophecy in one hand, the Fate-Cutting Blade in the other, and mastery of SMA from a Sidereal tutor is still going to have a very very different storyline from a Sidereal Exalt due to the different background their Exaltation implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-16-2014, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T01:39:49-07:00","id":198705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198648#post198648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that that falls into the same category as &quot;won't people just make an Exigent that is just like Lunars, but better?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, of course not.<br /> <br /> <i>Verzio carefully hides his notes for the Exalted Exalted, Exigents of Lytek, who wield Pulsarelectrum weapons and a strict superset of the abilities of Solars and Lunars.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:20:42-07:00","id":198743,"title":"","content":"Eclipses can use their anima power to learn Charms that will let them walk on clouds, write with their fingertips, and breath oxygen into the mouth of a drowning lover with a kiss, and many other powerful and interesting effects, and these Charms will not cost more than Solar Charms. But they won't be doing TN lowering, or gaining extra health levels, or buffing their mote pools, or gaining other combat advantages that makes them a superior choice to any other alternative caste, because those things are unbalanced.<br /> <br /> Evocations do not feel or act exactly like Charms and certainly do not replace Charms. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T04:26:40-07:00","id":198795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198743#post198743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eclipses can use their anima power to learn Charms that will let them walk on clouds, write with their fingertips, and breath oxygen into the mouth of a drowning lover with a kiss, and many other powerful and interesting effects, and these Charms will not cost more than Solar Charms. But they won't be doing TN lowering, or gaining extra health levels, or buffing their mote pools, or gaining other combat advantages that makes them a superior choice to any other alternative caste, because those things are unbalanced.<br /> <br /> Evocations do not feel or act exactly like Charms and certainly do not replace Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, that <i>would</i> seem the more sensible alternative to worries about stuffing a Lunar inside of a sword for a Solar to wield.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198705#post198705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Verzio carefully hides his notes for the Exalted Exalted, Exigents of Lytek, who wield Pulsarelectrum weapons and a strict superset of the abilities of Solars and Lunars.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, I've currently got this image of Lytek where, although he doesn't really have much power over Exaltation, and doesn't really even understand it as much as most people in Heaven tend to think he does, his association with it during its heyday made him extremely powerful, just in a kind of generic &quot;divine might&quot; sense, rather than a particular &quot;controlling domain&quot; one (his office as Shogun of Abstract Matters also helped with that). I picture it as being the godly equivalent of having those almost meaningless sinecure positions, like Master of Horse or something, where the actual administrative duties don't confer much power, but the large salaries and elevated social position do.<br /> <br /> I think it lends an interesting dimension to certain interactions with Lytek; he can't really do much for or to your Exalted power, but if you could get him both mighty again and indebted to you by facilitating a more comprehensive Exalted dominion over the Earth again, it would have certain advantages.<br /> <br /> (I've still a mind to have him as custodian and cultivator of Exalted Essence between incarnations, mind, albeit continuing that idea of sinecure position in conveying it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:04:35-07:00","id":198826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198743#post198743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations do not feel or act exactly like Charms and certainly do not replace Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except in the case of Pulsarelectrum artifacts, where the Evocations are identical to the whole Sidereal charmset, except you can also add custom Charms built off of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:07:02-07:00","id":198827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196357#post196357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can steal any theme and turn it into an Evocation...provided it's appropriate for an Evocation (likely a fairly stringent filter). Also: everyone else can do this, too. Being &quot;the best&quot; at Evocations seems to mean that Solars get access to those Adamant Circle Evocations, which if true means that they don't get to the Solar-only toys until they've gone through a lot of generally-accessible stuff. Solars can also practice Fire Dragon Style, or cast Bone Lion -- just like Lunars, Sidereals, Abyssals, and Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... hope you're wrong about that. The impression I got wasn't that Solars get access to a higher tier of Evocations, but rather that they get access to the entire breadth of the system. So a Solar can theoretically use a starmetal weapon just as well as a Sidereal, say, whereas the Sidereal can't do a whole lot with orichalcum.<br /> <br /> This bugged the bit of me that cares about niche protection at first, but I got over it when I realized that it would mean that Jiunan Nightwarden could use his axe properly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Although I'm less enthusiastic about the prospect of having something similar done with Necromancy...)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:20:11-07:00","id":198838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198827#post198827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm... hope you're wrong about that. The impression I got wasn't that Solars get access to a higher tier of Evocations, but rather that they get access to the entire breadth of the system. So a Solar can theoretically use a starmetal weapon just as well as a Sidereal, say, whereas the Sidereal can't do a whole lot with orichalcum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I had the complete opposite impression.<br /> A solar is all about being the greatest at something, the best tracker, the best fighter, the best sailor, etc, as well as bringing out the best in his followers, pets, subjects etc. So why wouldn't a solar be able to do the same with his tools? His Weapons? His Armor? His Ship.<br /> <br /> On top of that, using the system you suggest would pretty much force all the Exalted, except for the Solars, to use particular types of materials, since they'd get penalized for using another material.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, Volcano Cutter's Evocation layout was ranked in tiers, just like Sorcery and (though this has been removed, to an extend) Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> So wouldn't it make more sense that a Solar can access all the way up to Adamant Evocations, while a Sidereal (who gets reality-fu to compensate for that) only gets access to the Emerald Evocations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 07-16-2014, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:21:27-07:00","id":198840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198827#post198827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... hope you're wrong about that. The impression I got wasn't that Solars get access to a higher tier of Evocations, but rather that they get access to the entire breadth of the system. So a Solar can theoretically use a starmetal weapon just as well as a Sidereal, say, whereas the Sidereal can't do a whole lot with orichalcum.<br /> <br /> This bugged the bit of me that cares about niche protection at first, but I got over it when I realized that it would mean that Jiunan Nightwarden could use his axe properly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Although I'm less enthusiastic about the prospect of having something similar done with Necromancy...)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be pretty surprised if a Sidereal can use Starmetal as well as a Solar -- I imagine there <i>will </i>be splats who are just as good with their favoured MM as Solars are with everything, but the comments we've heard suggest that there are more than two levels of goodness, and Sidereals are at the bottom, which makes me think that they might be, like, &quot;Only Emerald&quot; or &quot;Sapphire for Starmetal, only Emerald for everything else&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T06:41:42-07:00","id":198885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198838#post198838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly, Volcano Cutter's Evocation layout was ranked in tiers, just like Sorcery and (though this has been removed, to an extend) Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> So wouldn't it make more sense that a Solar can access all the way up to Adamant Evocations, while a Sidereal (who gets reality-fu to compensate for that) only gets access to the Emerald Evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they do it differently than how sorcery is done, at least for variety of effect. &quot;Solars get up to Adamant Evocations because they get up to Adamant Sorcery&quot; is kinda boring. I'd hope for more nuance in the new Evocation system, especially as DBs are supposed to be better at Evocations than at least Sidereals and possibly other Celestials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T06:47:19-07:00","id":198888,"title":"","content":"I figured it was more &quot;Solars get adamant evocations because they're goddamn Solars&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T07:06:43-07:00","id":198912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198888#post198888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured it was more &quot;Solars get adamant evocations because they're goddamn Solars&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:40:28-07:00","id":198986,"title":"","content":"I personally hate it when one group doesn't get access to something in their specialty because another group is supposed to be more powerful. In this case, I fully accept Solars get access to all Adamant Evocations. I would really prefer that everybody get up to Adamant evocations in their specific fields: Dragon-Blooded in Jade, Sidereals in Starmetal. Then, what you get from other people's magical materials is based on how good you are with evocations: Dragon-Blooded are supposed to be really good get Tier 3 in Jade and Tier 2 in everything else. Sidereals, the weakest, get Tier 3 in Starmetal, and Tier 1 in everything else.<br /> <br /> Needs some work, I know, but I think its better than 'Solars get everything, and no-one else ever gets Adamant evocations.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:46:25-07:00","id":198987,"title":"","content":"What if Orichalcum evocations just go up to 11 compared with everything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:54:26-07:00","id":198995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198986#post198986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hate it when one group doesn't get access to something in their specialty because another group is supposed to be more powerful. In this case, I fully accept Solars get access to all Adamant Evocations. I would really prefer that everybody get up to Adamant evocations in their specific fields: Dragon-Blooded in Jade, Sidereals in Starmetal. Then, what you get from other people's magical materials is based on how good you are with evocations: Dragon-Blooded are supposed to be really good get Tier 3 in Jade and Tier 2 in everything else. Sidereals, the weakest, get Tier 3 in Starmetal, and Tier 1 in everything else.<br /> <br /> Needs some work, I know, but I think its better than 'Solars get everything, and no-one else ever gets Adamant evocations.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you unlucky enough to have a &quot;Every Words Are Sacred&quot; GM then it's pretty easy to just say every splats are the best at Evocation. Just don't post your opinion on the forum or &quot;Solar Supremacy&quot; fan gonna tear you apart and scatter your ash across dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-16-2014, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:01:45-07:00","id":199005,"title":"","content":"It strikes me that dragonblooded might be quite good at evocations (or at least, considered better at it than sidereals) not because of raw power but because of breadth of application. Five types of jade potentially means five different subsets of evocation they have equal affinity with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:02:13-07:00","id":199006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198987#post198987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Orichalcum evocations just go up to 11 compared with everything else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could be. But then what about Orichalcum Caste Alchemicals? Do they get 'better' evocations too for being Orichalcum? Also, I think Holden specifically said that he wanted the Exalt types to really want their own magical materials, but he wants Solars to be better with other peoples stuff.<br /> <br /> I don't know exactly how they plan to balance it all out, but they have a goal, and it doesn't seem like it would be too hard to come up with a compromise based on what their ove rall goals are... which we don't really know yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:06:52-07:00","id":199011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198986#post198986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hate it when one group doesn't get access to something in their specialty because another group is supposed to be more powerful. In this case, I fully accept Solars get access to all Adamant Evocations. I would really prefer that everybody get up to Adamant evocations in their specific fields: Dragon-Blooded in Jade, Sidereals in Starmetal. Then, what you get from other people's magical materials is based on how good you are with evocations: Dragon-Blooded are supposed to be really good get Tier 3 in Jade and Tier 2 in everything else. Sidereals, the weakest, get Tier 3 in Starmetal, and Tier 1 in everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why would I want my Sidereal to have anything but a Starmetal Weapon? It gives me the coolest stuff.<br /> Honestly, I hope the connection between MM's and Specific types of Exalted gets seperated as much as possible. In 1e, it made sense, five types of exalted, five magic Materials, but Now we're at 3rd, and we now have at least 10 different types of Exalted (counting Exigents as one group) and the number of MM's has not increased. It just seems like making material type A better for Exalted type A pigeonholes Exalted type A into picking Material A, since it's objectively the best choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 07-16-2014, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:09:28-07:00","id":199013,"title":"","content":"We got <i>one</i> extra magical material - adamant. And I guess &quot;demon&quot; sort of counted as far as helltech was concerned if you squint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:17:20-07:00","id":199023,"title":"","content":"Each Exalt type still links to a particular magical material. Just some of the exalt types weren't supposed to be there. The way I read it.<br /> <br /> Solars -&gt; Orichalcum, as intended<br /> Abyssals -&gt; Corrupted to use Soulsteel<br /> Infernals -&gt; No related magical material (at least at this time). Maybe demon-tainted Orichalcum, an alloy of brass and Orichalcum?<br /> Lunars -&gt; Moonsilver, as intended<br /> Sidereals -&gt; Starmetal, as intended<br /> Dragon-Blooded -&gt; Jade, as intended<br /> Alchemicals -&gt; All, as intended<br /> Getimen -&gt; Adamant? Or possibly Starmetal, as they are very much like Sidereals. In fact, so close as to be the good or evil twin.<br /> Liminals -&gt; Soulsteel? As Solars to Orichalcum, Liminals to Soulsteel. Lots of stuff about Abyssals not completely connecting to Soulsteel.<br /> Exigent -&gt; No clue. As one offs, they generally don't belong in this discussion, I think.<br /> Fair Folk -&gt; Gossamer, as before.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:20:26-07:00","id":199026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199011#post199011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why would I want my Sidereal to have anything but a Starmetal Weapon? It gives me the coolest stuff.<br /> Honestly, I hope the connection between MM's and Specific types of Exalted gets seperated as much as possible. In 1e, it made sense, five types of exalted, five magic Materials, but Now we're at 3rd, and we now have at least 10 different types of Exalted (counting Exigents as one group) and the number of MM's has not increased. It just seems like making material type A better for Exalted type A pigeonholes Exalted type A into picking Material A, since it's objectively the best choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As per Holden, this is the goal. Sidereals get Starmetal weapons, because it gives you the best stuff. As for 10 Exalt types, and no new MMs, see my above posts. 6 MMs, six base exalt types as near as I can tell (Liminals, Getimen, Dragon-Blooded, Sidereals, Lunars, Solars). Alchemicals are also composed of the six types, so they don't get their own MM. It's been hinted multiple times that Abyssals aren't naturally linked to Soulsteel, and that there is a sixth Exalt type, hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:21:47-07:00","id":199027,"title":"","content":"Hmm I never thought about the Fey having crazy evocations of their own. THAT would certainly be an awesome weapon to have, if you could somehow get a gossamer weapon and keep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:24:59-07:00","id":199031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199027#post199027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm I never thought about the Fey having crazy evocations of their own. THAT would certainly be an awesome weapon to have, if you could somehow get a gossamer weapon and keep it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, a million ways. Cut a deal, win a bet, kick a Fair Folk's ass, insult him, take his weapon, and dare him to come take it back, get an enemy to lend you one so that he can betray you at the appropriate moment by stealing it back... the fun never ends with those guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:28:37-07:00","id":199033,"title":"","content":"Soulsteel isn't exactly natural to begin with. The stuff you find in creation only started being made after the neverborn fell, and before that it was made when Autochthon did something nasty to a bunch of souls he didn't want reincarnating. Also bear in mind that Auto is currently in the process of dying, which primordials are supposed to be <i>metaphysically incapable of doing on their own. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:38:35-07:00","id":199040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199033#post199033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soulsteel isn't exactly natural to begin with. The stuff you find in creation only started being made after the neverborn fell, and before that it was made when Autochthon did something nasty to a bunch of souls he didn't want reincarnating. Also bear in mind that Auto is currently in the process of dying, which primordials are supposed to be <i>metaphysically incapable of doing on their own. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite my interpretation of it, and I don't think Autocthon made the Underworld and the Labyrinth. I've seen stuff from 'It's a dark mirror of Cration, tied to it and apart' to 'It appeared when the first primordial died.' Still, Soulsteel is a thing, and a fully recognized magical material. Orichalcum isn't exactly natural either, as it has to be created using vast magic-volcano-forges and sun-lasers. Starmetal isn't exactly natural, as it requires a god to die and his star to fall from the sky. Moonsilver also has to be created by special Luna-blessed rituals. <br /> <br /> As for a Primordial dying, which isn't supposed to happen? It probably wasn't in the Primordial planogram, but, things happen. The Primordials weren't all knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:46:31-07:00","id":199047,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the death of the primordials is regularly touted as number one on the list of impossible stuff the solars managed to do anyway. It was such a momentous event that it broke reality and created another realm of existence entirely and now Autochthon is sitting in elsewhere casually dying with no help whatsoever. <br /> <br /> It's like, if the war had never happened sooner or later He'd have gone &quot;hey guys, look what I made! The Underworld!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;also I'm this thing called a neverborn now&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;this really fucking hurts. ow.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:54:14-07:00","id":199062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199047#post199047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but the death of the primordials is regularly touted as number one on the list of impossible stuff the solars managed to do anyway. It was such a momentous event that it broke reality and created another realm of existence entirely and now Autochthon is sitting in elsewhere casually dying with no help whatsoever.<br /> <br /> It's like, if the war had never happened sooner or later He'd have gone &quot;hey guys, look what I made! The Underworld!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;also I'm this thing called a neverborn now&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;this really fucking hurts. ow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always had this idea that he had Soulsteel before the Underworld. Just another one of those things that he made with an idea of making a lot of stuff with it later, but it didn't really come into its own until the Underworld showed up. Also, I'm not entirely sure that time ran correctly during the entire Primordial War. Wouldn't surprise me if Autochthon found this stuff, thought it was really neat, figured out a bunch of stuff to do with it, and then the Underworld came into being, and he found the source. <br /> <br /> Actually, I have this idea that there were five magical metals, and five core Exalt types, and five casts of Alchemicals, and then Soulsteel showed up, and he figured he needed a sixth Exalt type to go with it. Like any good craftsman, he saw the material and wondered what he could do with it.<br /> <br /> Actually, I have like six ideas about how this could go, and that's because I haven't thought about it yet. I don't ahve a clue what the canon will be for 3rd, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:02:59-07:00","id":199082,"title":"","content":"In canon he made soulsteel before the war by smelting an entire primordial race with ore from his own body (which I personally think he had because he's kinda sorta partially-neverborn to begin with). No underworld involved at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:11:14-07:00","id":199092,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I vaguely remembered something like this, but I couldn't remember how he got it before the Underworld. I like the idea that he is transitioning between Primordial and Neverborn, opening the possibility to Primordials dying by his illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:34:43-07:00","id":199132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199062#post199062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't ahve a clue what the canon will be for 3rd, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that it will not be discussed at all, but that actually coming up with rules for a lost host of Exalted from the war of the gods will be much easier to do on your own, especially with the Exigent book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:01:29-07:00","id":199184,"title":"","content":"Soulsteel was something that bugged me in the past because it required something that couldn't exist before the war because the universe its self could not conceive of a titan dying and staying dead so it had to make a place for that. The ore to make soulsteel came from the universe understanding a stagnation of death, a terminal end to things that should last forever, that nothing is that exists is without a way to pass from existance.<br /> <br /> That made me wonder if the first Soulsteel, was in truth a more primitive soul steel made from a less effective ore and souls. It was less effective at it's job, more time consuming and difficult to make because the forces that it needed to reach it's final state did not yet exist. After the primordial war, the powers of death became stronger and death had a true sting and the Labyrinth Dark Ore became manifest.<br /> <br /> The new artifact systems actually make sense with pre-existing lore because prior to this why would solars or lunar bother with the stuff when you could mine oricalcum, atune easier to it, and get more benefit. from using a none matching material. A Dragon Blood might want a Jade and Soul Steel Daiklave to hunt solars with because it makes sense to him. Yes the Dragon Blood might not get as much out of the Soulsteel as a Abyssal but he can still use it to bring out some amazing power in his weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:16:52-07:00","id":199192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198888#post198888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured it was more &quot;Solars get adamant evocations because they're goddamn Solars&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. I would hope someone else got to that level, at least in a more limited way. Say, DBs for jade weapons only. &quot;Because Solars&quot; is kind of played out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=198987#post198987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Orichalcum evocations just go up to 11 compared with everything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Orichalcum was never presented as an <i>inherently superior</i> MM compared to the other MM, just because it's the one favored by Solars. I wouldn't mind seeing Fivefold (Sixfold, I guess) Harmonic Adapters making a comeback and would hope those had no effect on Evocation access, just attunement cost.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199006#post199006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be. But then what about Orichalcum Caste Alchemicals? Do they get 'better' evocations too for being Orichalcum?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading that Alchemicals may not get access to Evocations at all. Of course, that might have changed and may still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199011#post199011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I hope the connection between MM's and Specific types of Exalted gets seperated as much as possible. In 1e, it made sense, five types of exalted, five magic Materials, but Now we're at 3rd, and we now have at least 10 different types of Exalted (counting Exigents as one group) and the number of MM's has not increased.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they ditch the &quot;fivefold symmetry plus one&quot; thing (hell, they've ditched it in other ways already) and just have dozens of kinds of magical materials. The sig Eclipse has an orichalcum/red Chiaroscuro glass daiklave after all, I assume the glass isn't there just for show but because it added a magical component the maker thought was necessary to achieve his goal when making the weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199184#post199184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soulsteel was something that bugged me in the past because it required something that couldn't exist before the war because the universe its self could not conceive of a titan dying and staying dead so it had to make a place for that. The ore to make soulsteel came from the universe understanding a stagnation of death, a terminal end to things that should last forever, that nothing is that exists is without a way to pass from existance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense if the first soulsteel came out of Autochthon. He does have themes of &quot;the sickly/broken crafter&quot; which are heavily present in myth, paired with the fact that he could keep his &quot;disease&quot; in remission while in Creation but not Elsewhere. He could easily have had the Labyrinth-ore-esque component within himself the whole time, before the first Primordial was killed, and made soulsteel with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-16-2014, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:33:10-07:00","id":199210,"title":"","content":"Personally, I wouldn't mind if they loosened the associations between specific Exalts and Magical Materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:33:47-07:00","id":199272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199210#post199210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I wouldn't mind if they loosened the associations between specific Exalts and Magical Materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, a thousand times this. I honestly think that the caste / magical material associations were a bad idea and should be massively downplayed or even removed entirely.<br /> <br /> It encourages people to make more boring, generic characters (you play the DEATH EXALT and use weapons with the DEATH METAL; you play the SUN EXALT and use weapons with the SUN METAL etc). When you look at heroes with legendary weapons, their weapons are generally entirely their own thing -- that is to say, a five-dot or N/A artifact should feel almost like a second Exaltation (like, if you want to use game-terms, a secondary class or something) -- not like a duplicate of your main Exaltation. Using artifacts to just let you do what you can already do but better is incredibly boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-16-2014, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:40:49-07:00","id":199287,"title":"","content":"It just wouldn't look right for the solars to not be decked head to foot in golden bling though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:47:09-07:00","id":199297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199287#post199287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just wouldn't look right for the solars to not be decked head to foot in golden bling though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's often how it feels when something has historically been only one way. I'd certainly prefer that being an approach that's still supported -- and encouraged depending on what you're after -- but not mandated as such. The writers seem to be going in this direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephenls</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're working to ensure there's reason to want to stick with your own Magical Material, and there's definitely going to be reasons in place for Solars to not particularly favor Starmetal over any other MM while Sidereals drop everything and chase fallen stars because that shit is so useful to them, and we definitely want to ensure that Dragon-Blooded are incentivized towards jade, but Solars get to use everything with equal facility for a number of reasons ranging from &quot;John wants Solars to be especially proficient with Evocations, not just Evocations form orichalcum weapons&quot; to &quot;Because Solars are the primary player-character-type and it's more fun if everyone playing Solars can further differentiate their characters aesthetically via a wide range of weapon appearances.&quot;<br /> <br /> We are aware this is a change, and believe we are doing it for the right reasons, and are working to ensure it doesn't come off as gratuitous Solar favoritism. It'll make sense. And I am not cleared to provide details.<br /> <br /> (Also this edition will tend to have a lot more hybrid material artifacts -- Prince Diamond wields a sword made of orichalcum and Chiaroscuro glass, for example.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:01:29-07:00","id":199309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199287#post199287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just wouldn't look right for the solars to not be decked head to foot in golden bling though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody is saying they can't still do that. Just that it might be less of a default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:04:40-07:00","id":199310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199297#post199297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd certainly prefer that being an approach that's still supported -- and encouraged depending on what you're after -- but not mandated as such. The writers seem to be going in this direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, cool! We have confirmation. Where'd you dig that up?<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see artifacts in general be a bit more independent of the MMs, myself, but there's actually a way for us to have our cake and eat it too I think - just give them aspects. Like with manses, y'know? They'd express the thematics of the associated splat, without being tied to quite so specific an aesthetic. So, say, a big goremaul made of bone might be of an Abyssal aspect (that'd be the obvious choice anyway), but it could also easily be Lunar, depending on the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:13:28-07:00","id":199365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199310#post199310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, cool! We have confirmation. Where'd you dig that up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I guess it's been a while since I've gone on a quoting spree. The links in my signature make it easier to find quotes from the EX3 team. To save time (or if you've got sigs disabled), this quote is near the end of the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Artifacts\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts sub-section</a> on the EX3 &quot;What We Know&quot; Wiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:38:14-07:00","id":199399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations depend on how much power you draw from within; by contrast, if you wear more of your power on the outside (Sidereals, Lunars, Abyssals, Infernals) you aren't as good at them . . . It's about how far your Essence can carry you, and where it goes. Lunars put all of their power into their Charms, and their Charms represent all of their creative, motive energy transitioning into a visible expression of power (like DBT). In essence, Lunars aren't as good at Evocations because their Charms already evoke most of their creative, transformative potential . . . It is also why, when a Lunar goes DBT, his Evocations stop working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Just pondering this and its implications. Maybe Sidereals are so bad at Evocations because of how much they have to rely on Martial Arts (closed Charmset and all). Maybe activating a Form-type Charm takes a lot of &quot;motive energy&quot; and shows &quot;wearing power on the outside&quot; and might reduce Evocation power for anyone wearing a Form-tyle Charm from an MA, much like how DBT would shut down Evocation use for Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo maybe for Sidereals, starmetal is super important because it allows them to keep accessing (more/higher level) Evocations even while using &quot;external&quot; MA Charms and Forms, where if they were using a non-starmetal weapon, they could not do so.<br /> <br /> That would be a pretty good reason to be so gung-ho for starmetal!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:08:31-07:00","id":199434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199399#post199399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Just pondering this and its implications. Maybe Sidereals are so bad at Evocations because of how much they have to rely on Martial Arts (closed Charmset and all). Maybe activating a Form-type Charm takes a lot of &quot;motive energy&quot; and shows &quot;wearing power on the outside&quot; and might reduce Evocation power for anyone wearing a Form-tyle Charm from an MA, much like how DBT would shut down Evocation use for Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo maybe for Sidereals, starmetal is super important because it allows them to keep accessing (more/higher level) Evocations even while using &quot;external&quot; MA Charms and Forms, where if they were using a non-starmetal weapon, they could not do so.<br /> <br /> That would be a pretty good reason to be so gung-ho for starmetal!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it. We honestly don't know what the Bennies and Perks are of the magical materials yet either, which for those of you who know is why I'm still hanging back so much on my personal project the Lesser Magical Materials. Because I think with so many new types of exalted these elements will come forward more but I'm not exactly sure how I want to play them. The other magical materials add (except for jade in 2.5) a +4 bonus, or equivalent.<br /> <br /> So we don't exactly know what Oricalcum does, or and we theorise that Jade will be by color, Star Metal sounds logical will be associated with martial arts, and Soul Steel with death, and moonsilver is Primal (my best guess). You can see why I haven't done more than introduction stuff, and look for artists.<br /> <br /> But here is a big question, Attunement, what happens for a dragon blood who is using a direlance that is jade and Oricalcum? Or a Sidereal using a starmetal and Soul Steel Daiklave? Do they have to pay an extra attunement cost? Are some materials more functional to compositing like the Oricalcum and Red Glass of Prince Diamond's sword? <br /> <br /> My guess is you don't have to pay extra to attune if the primary material is your native one, evocations for that second one are capped normally, Though I am very curious to see how the evocation system works and it surprises me that Abyssals and Infernals (both derivatives of solars) are actually lesser wielders of Evocations. This means out of the original 5 exalted types only the Solars and Dragon Blooded don't wear their power on their sleeves as much, so they can draw upon Evocations with near solar efficiency (also helping to close that power gap).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:24:43-07:00","id":199457,"title":"","content":"Another reason to go with aspects over MMs. Short-circuits those sorts of questions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:21:18-07:00","id":199616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199434#post199434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here is a big question, Attunement, what happens for a dragon blood who is using a direlance that is jade and Oricalcum? Or a Sidereal using a starmetal and Soul Steel Daiklave? Do they have to pay an extra attunement cost? Are some materials more functional to compositing like the Oricalcum and Red Glass of Prince Diamond's sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy answer: kill the double cost rule. What did it ever add to the game, besides being the justification for an Artifact (harmonic adapters) to just get around it? I say nothing. Solars should want orichalcum, Lunars moonsilver, etc. for interesting, in-setting reasons. Not &quot;it costs less to attune.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:44:04-07:00","id":199699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199616#post199616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy answer: kill the double cost rule. What did it ever add to the game, besides being the justification for an Artifact (harmonic adapters) to just get around it? I say nothing. Solars should want orichalcum, Lunars moonsilver, etc. for interesting, in-setting reasons. Not &quot;it costs less to attune.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This'd be more my guess (and preference), too. The devs have spoken a lot about taking holistic views on splat balance, and I have no doubt that includes their associated Artifacts. Whatever benefits and Evocations moonsilver Artifacts can give, I expect they will generally be very attractive for those with a Lunar's capabilities and typical methods. The same should go for every splat with an associated Magical Material. Thus, absent other factors, individual characters of a splat may thus favor Artifacts of other Magical Materials for their purposes, even while most will gravitate to their associated ones, and none are necessarily making dumb decisions.<br /> <br /> I could see cases where a Solar could theoretically get greater Evocations with an artifact than a member of its associated splat, but the Evocations and other benefits the non-Solar <i>does</i> get just synergize so well with native abilities. On balance, the non-Solar might come out nearly, just as, or more impressive than a hypothetical Solar would (albeit maybe in different ways). I mean, the Sidereal toolkit has some rather peculiar and unique powers in it. I could see some Starmetal Evocations that are helpful if unwieldy for most, but downright devastating in the hands of a Vizier with the right Charms (and/or presumably functional Astrology).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:38:03-07:00","id":199803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199210#post199210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I wouldn't mind if they loosened the associations between specific Exalts and Magical Materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Including being able to have decent artifacts that are not chunks of gaudy magical material and still get good evocations. Because seriously, there is a time and a place for looking like a Saint Seiya character (which is usually what going around in Orichalcum armor and weapons gets you), but, say, a Solar game of pirates in the West is not it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T02:35:23-07:00","id":199860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199803#post199803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Including being able to have decent artifacts that are not chunks of gaudy magical material and still get good evocations. Because seriously, there is a time and a place for looking like a Saint Seiya character (which is usually what going around in Orichalcum armor and weapons gets you), but, say, a Solar game of pirates in the West is not it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helltech don't benefit from MM bonus but always have some niffy effects to go along with the Artifact, but they got published so late along the line plus being all kind of broken so now you get black Exalted wearing black metal, golden Exalted using golden metal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T06:10:39-07:00","id":199923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199803#post199803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Including being able to have decent artifacts that are not chunks of gaudy magical material and still get good evocations. Because seriously, there is a time and a place for looking like a Saint Seiya character (which is usually what going around in Orichalcum armor and weapons gets you), but, say, a Solar game of pirates in the West is not it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is one of the areas I think my project fits in. A Daiklave made of Lightning Crystal (Quartz struck by lighting that flash froze), Obsidian (Said to absorb negative energy and over time convert it to positive energy), Thousand Fold Steel (Steel that has been treated and bears a portion of the smiths will and conviction making it naturally receptive to magic), Ice Heart Crystal (Core sample from a glacier, ice that has seen the Primordial rise and fall), and my favorite the bones of beasts and demons defeated (Think the monster hunter game.)d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 07-17-2014, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:04:17-07:00","id":199979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199860#post199860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Helltech don't benefit from MM bonus but always have some niffy effects to go along with the Artifact, but they got published so late along the line plus being all kind of broken so now you get black Exalted wearing black metal, golden Exalted using golden metal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Infernals got preferential attunement to all MM, as long as it was soaked in vitriol first. I hope that bit stays (maybe if it doesn't help with attunement costs, it'll help them with accessing more powerful Evocations of that material). Though the old definition of vitriol is my preference (congealed Yozi spite that just kind of bubbles up from the ground of the Demon City, aka it's basically Malfeas's angry angry sweat and tears - how cool is that!) Versus &quot;ultimate transformative element from 50,000 years ago vetoed by Gaia&quot; blah blah blah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:10:55-07:00","id":199985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=199979#post199979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Infernals got preferential attunement to all MM, as long as it was soaked in vitriol first. I hope that bit stays (maybe if it doesn't help with attunement costs, it'll help them with accessing more powerful Evocations of that material). Though the old definition of vitriol is my preference (congealed Yozi spite that just kind of bubbles up from the ground of the Demon City, aka it's basically Malfeas's angry angry sweat and tears - how cool is that!) Versus &quot;ultimate transformative element from 50,000 years ago vetoed by Gaia&quot; blah blah blah</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmhm. The name makes a lot more sense that way too.<br /> <br /> (Although I do kinda like the metody.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:33:21-07:00","id":200000,"title":"","content":"Why not both? Created by the spite, but takes the particular form that it does (instead of poison or a virus or some other thing) because of old memories of that vetoed element?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T17:18:45-07:00","id":200570,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I am left wondering what the appeal of orichalcum <i>will</i> be, if everyone but Solars has a preferable option, because it seems like as a Solar player you would be less likely to want a weapon whose powers feel overly similar to what you can already do, and orichalcum is the hardest MM to pin evocative thematics onto. Making orichalcum artifacts mechanically superior to other types, or making their evocations cost less XP, would do the trick, but would come off like a &quot;flavour or effectiveness&quot; trade-off, which is always a bit ashes-in-mouth. It's tricky! I am curious to see what they do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-17-2014, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T17:52:17-07:00","id":200589,"title":"","content":"I imagine it is because Oricalcum has it's own cool effects and it's own interesting and unique powers that will make you want to choose it because it is amazing on it's own and it will feel very much like something you will drool over. Oh jade will be awesome too in it's own respects and you will jump for joy at it, and moonsilver will be nice and you will want to put both in your weapon. You will salivate over all the options available to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T00:04:24-07:00","id":202714,"title":"","content":"Why Solars work with all materials: Because of the humanizing nature of their Charms, the Solars can spread out externally and in abstract ways a lot better than Sidereals, Lunars, etc., the way they do with Sorcery. Artifacts are complex workings of magic and sorcery. This is just an expansion of how things already work for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T02:21:30-07:00","id":202768,"title":"","content":"...so it's literately BECAUSE SOLAR. Jesus. That's totally what I wanted to hear.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should be less flippant. But I had seriously hoped for a real reason. Not just that. I'm extremely disappointed in that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 07-20-2014, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T02:35:36-07:00","id":202775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's totally what I wanted to hear.</div> </div> </div> </div> So much so that it seems to override anything that actually gets said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:35:23-07:00","id":202969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=202768#post202768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so it's literately BECAUSE SOLAR. Jesus. That's totally what I wanted to hear.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should be less flippant. But I had seriously hoped for a real reason. Not just that. I'm extremely disappointed in that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the fact that Solar charms are now &quot;Humanizing&quot; which means less Over the top op, and more down to earth means that Solars are now the expression of human excellence as well as the sun's power. But they are still very human. Less so than a Lunar who accepts a portion of a beastial nature into them, and a Sidreal who seperates themselves from humanity.<br /> <br /> This makes me wonder if Dragon Blooded will also be very good with Evocations (Second to Solars?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:45:55-07:00","id":202985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I had seriously hoped for a real reason.</div> </div> </div> </div> Meaning what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:58:39-07:00","id":202997,"title":"","content":"I'm totally okay with the reason being &quot;because Solars are the default PC type&quot;, actually, without any handwaving. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And come on, it'll take one minute to houserule that any Exalt can attune to any material without breaking anything in the mechanics or setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T09:32:27-07:00","id":203017,"title":"","content":"I remember that Evocations are tied to the tool AND user. So over time as you master your weapon/armor/etc you unlock unique ones that only you and the device can have. It's just a new layers of customization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:21:08-07:00","id":203056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=202985#post202985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Meaning what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meaning something other then a damn tautology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:37:30-07:00","id":203060,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help that by &quot;humanizing&quot; we mean &quot;Solars don't have to deal with working around any constraints of their motif to solve problems, they can just do it&quot;. It is not some sort of downside that on the plus side means they get more affinity with external systems to help make up for what they can't do with their Charms, it is the benefit of having the best, most consistently useful Charms and then on top of that having the best affinity with everything else too. This makes it a less than satisfying explanation, if you're disinclined towards Solars, to find that the brand-new exciting Evocations system is just another thing for them to be better than everyone else at because it's &quot;an expansion of how things already work for them&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not exactly irritated by the response, because it's been made clear since the beginning that Solars were going to be the best at Evocations, but it's not exactly satisfying either because it just reiterates &quot;Solars are the best at Evocations because they're the best at every subsystem&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:46:53-07:00","id":203063,"title":"","content":"Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted, so their abilities reflect the fact that they're the mightiest of the Exalted. I'm not seeing the problem here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:15:04-07:00","id":203071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203063#post203063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted, so their abilities reflect the fact that they're the mightiest of the Exalted. I'm not seeing the problem here.</div> </div> </div> </div>*SCREAMS EXTERNALLY*<br /> <br /> Wait, I shouldn't scream. Thank you for showing off exactly what I meant about a tautology, just even more nakedly then Mork did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:29:07-07:00","id":203076,"title":"","content":"People who are &quot;disinclined towards Solars&quot; will have issues with Exalted, as the core premise of the game is how the return of the champions of old will shake the world. This is the story of how they shape the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:37:21-07:00","id":203078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203071#post203071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thank you for showing off exactly what I meant about a tautology, just even more nakedly then Mork did.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I ask what the problem is with the fact that it's tautology?<br /> The Solars represent the pinnacle of what humanity can do, the greatest swordsmen, the greatest athlete, the greatest sailor, etc. To me, it makes sense that, by extension, they are able to bring out a similar greatness in their weaponry and tools. This does not mean that every solar is going to be the greatest at everything. Like every character, you'll have to pick what you're good at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:37:34-07:00","id":203079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203076#post203076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who are &quot;disinclined towards Solars&quot; will have issues with Exalted, as the core premise of the game is how the return of the champions of old will shake the world. This is the story of how they shape the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they should just drop all pretense, then and just call the game Solars, perhaps? Because for the moment, it's still called Exalted, as in the story of ALL of the Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:41:49-07:00","id":203082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203071#post203071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *SCREAMS EXTERNALLY*<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But... &quot;being better than you&quot; is <i>literally </i>their shtick. Why is this scream-inducing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:42:58-07:00","id":203083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203079#post203079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they should just drop all pretense, then and just call the game Solars, perhaps? Because for the moment, it's still called Exalted, as in the story of ALL of the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a reason the Solar Exalted are fully playable out of the corebook, and all the other Exalted types quickly presented in the &quot;Antagonist&quot; chapter.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted are the default protagonists of the game. The story of Exalted is how their return will shake the world. They are the mightiest of the Chosen.<br /> <br /> All other stories are good stories as well! You can play a Lunar game, a Sidereal game, a Dragon-Blooded game...<br /> <br /> Unless you homebrew your own setting, however, you will be playing a Lunar within the specific context of &quot;the Solars are returning and shaking the world.&quot; What will you do about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:49:16-07:00","id":203088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203082#post203082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But... &quot;being better than you&quot; is <i>literally </i>their shtick. Why is this scream-inducing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Revan does not like the Solars and wants a different splat the be better than them, or at least be able to compete with them (something that 2e was not good at representing, and, from what I've gathered, is something that is definatly going to happen in 3e.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:51:37-07:00","id":203089,"title":"","content":"....put more words in my damn mouth, why don't you. How about, and this is just a thought, you speak for you, and only you, and no one but you because you're not in my head?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:52:30-07:00","id":203091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203071#post203071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *SCREAMS EXTERNALLY*<br /> <br /> Wait, I shouldn't scream. Thank you for showing off exactly what I meant about a tautology, just even more nakedly then Mork did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that's a tautology. Solars are the best at evocations because they're the best at evocations because they're the best at evocations. They're axiomatically the best at everything, and flowing from that they are the best at evocations. They're just the best at it because in this universe the UCS is the god of perfection, the most skilled at whatever he chooses to do, and his chosen reflect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:53:33-07:00","id":203094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203088#post203088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Revan does not like the Solars and wants a different splat the be better than them, or <b>at least be able to compete with them </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's something I can fully support, but... when you take away &quot;excellency&quot; as the distinguishing feature of the Solar Exalted, what remains?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:56:08-07:00","id":203097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203091#post203091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how that's a tautology. Solars are the best at evocations because they're the best at evocations because they're the best at evocations. They're axiomatically the best at everything, and flowing from that they are the best at evocations. They're just the best at it because in this universe the UCS is the god of perfection, the most skilled at whatever he chooses to do, and his chosen reflect that.</div> </div> </div> </div>...did you just...write that. And seriously not think about the implications? The WHOLE THING is one massive tautology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203094#post203094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's something I can fully support, but... when you take away &quot;excellency&quot; as the distinguishing feature of the Solar Exalted, what remains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, indeed. What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:58:12-07:00","id":203098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203094#post203094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, that's something I can fully support, but... when you take away &quot;excellency&quot; as the distinguishing feature of the Solar Exalted, what remains?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're gold and shiney.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:58:23-07:00","id":203100,"title":"","content":"Seems to me like there obviously isn't any deep logic that flows directly from the essence of the Solar splat as to why they should get the highest Sorcery or Evocations. It's just their place in the game.<br /> <br /> Solars who used Fate weaving magic as their primary tool Sidereals wouldn't be or feel like Solars. Sidereals who could use Solar Circle Sorcery like Solars would still feel like Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say it is annoying that Solars can do more with Evocations by default than other splats as, after all, it is the easiest thing in the world to houserule if you are so inclined and its pretty consistent with their role in the narrative. It is just annoying, perhaps, to see it cast in terms of the Solars getting such an ability as a deep birthright from their very nature (let alone a questionable &quot;humanising&quot; nature to their power), rather than their designated protagonist role in the game. To me, this just seems like some unconvincing flim flam because John Morke feels its important for Solars to feel like they &quot;deserve&quot; everything they have, that they aren't arbitrarily the mightiest of the chosen.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> &quot;The return of the champions of old will shake the world&quot; as the core premise of the game..? This is part of the game, however I find calling this a core premise implies, to me, that if you wanted to write up a shard where things were more or less exactly as they were except without any Usurpation or Solar power edge, then that would fail to be Exalted or it wouldn't share the same core premise or it would be rejecting the core premise of canon Exalted. That feels really obviously false to me - 99% of what makes Creation an interesting and unique setting to play in and consider and most of what makes it appealing to most of its fans, has absolutely no dependency on where the Solars sit in their power and narrative role. &quot;Core premise&quot; feels wrong here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:01:54-07:00","id":203104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203079#post203079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they should just drop all pretense, then and just call the game Solars, perhaps? Because for the moment, it's still called Exalted, as in the story of ALL of the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:solars-and-other-splats\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a little essay from John on the topic of the Solars and how they relate to the other splats. <br /> <br /> In fact I would suggest reading all of the writer quotes on that site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:03:17-07:00","id":203109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203082#post203082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... &quot;being better than you&quot; is <i>literally </i>their shtick. Why is this scream-inducing?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JPA9bKz2meI\" target=\"_blank\">Very few people actually want to play with Cartman at the table</a>.<br /> <br /> This isn't quite accurate, as Solars do have a tiny number of things they can't do that other Exalts can, like shapeshifting or fate-weaving, but they don't actually need any of those things because those things are tools to solve problems with and Solars already have better tools for solving all of those problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:05:09-07:00","id":203110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203097#post203097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...did you just...write that. And seriously not think about the implications? The WHOLE THING is one massive tautology.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry there should have been a &quot;not&quot; in there, iPads suck. Either way, in the universe of exalted &quot;the sun is the best at everything&quot; is as axiomatic as &quot;for every variable x, x=x is valid&quot;. When determining logic from the setting you need to understand that time flows forward, no two corporeal things can be in the same place at the same time, and the UCS is the apex of perfection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:13:23-07:00","id":203127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203104#post203104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:solars-and-other-splats\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a little essay from John on the topic of the Solars and how they relate to the other splats.<br /> <br /> In fact I would suggest reading all of the writer quotes on that site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Words =/= action. You can write one thing as many times as you want, but when your every action says something else, why should I bother to believe anything you might say? Because that's where it's at, really. I can look at their past actions, and their past words, and compare them. Holden once argued for HOURS that some Solar Holy charms should be able to flat out, no roll, turn off some Abyssal mirrors. And in fact, put at least one charm to that effect into the game.<br /> <br /> I'll wait and see how the game itself shakes out. But nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:16:04-07:00","id":203137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203109#post203109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JPA9bKz2meI\" target=\"_blank\">Very few people actually want to play with Cartman at the table</a>.<br /> <br /> This isn't quite accurate, as Solars do have a tiny number of things they can't do that other Exalts can, like shapeshifting or fate-weaving, but they don't actually need any of those things because those things are tools to solve problems with and Solars already have better tools for solving all of those problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing different splats is about having a different game experience, with different themes and stories. It's not about playing someone who is &quot;better&quot; at some subset than the splats you aren't playing. You play a Lunar because you are interested in playing a mythic shapeshifter, not because playing a mythic shapeshifter lets you succeed better at stuff than if you had played a Solar.<br /> <br /> It's about the journey, not the destination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:18:34-07:00","id":203141,"title":"","content":"Better? No. It would be nice if you'd bother to read his point though. Because that's not what he said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:19:45-07:00","id":203142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203071#post203071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *SCREAMS EXTERNALLY*<br /> <br /> Wait, I shouldn't scream. Thank you for showing off exactly what I meant about a tautology, just even more nakedly then Mork did.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not understand how language works. <br /> <br /> Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted. That is one of their definitive traits. That has always been been one of their definitive traits. In any area where Solars are competing against any other Exalted, Solars will have the advantage because having an advantage over others is part of what it means to be a Solar. That is how Exalted defines Solars. <br /> <br /> All the powers, of all the Exalted, are tautological because they are derived from the definitive traits of the Exalted chosen by the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:20:00-07:00","id":203143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=196731#post196731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My single biggest problem with Black Mirror Revelation vs. Unconquered Hero's Faith was that it treated Limit and Resonance costs as interchangeable and ignored the difference between the two mechanics.<br /> <br /> Resonance is something you're supposed to manage on a meta level, the entire Abyssal playstyle assumes you're aware of how close you are to killing loved ones on the other side of the world, alerting the Aerial Legion to your presence or being posessed by the Neverborn and measuring your rebellion against your dark fate carefully otherwise it'll be crushed before you can make any real progress meanwhile Limit is intended to be a sword of damocles that you never quite know when it'll fall.<br /> <br /> Charms that cause Limit gain are potentially beneficial in a way that charms that cause Resonance aren't because they allow you to have a bout of murderous rage, calculating cruelty (or what have you) at a moment where it can seem appropriate or even justified rather than blowing up at the wrong people.<br /> <br /> This is just confounded by the fact that the Holy keyword means that several Solar charms are unusable to Abyssals anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also feel that Black Mirror Revelation chickened out compared to the Unconquered Hero's Faith mirror that was hypothesised in MoEP: Abyssals which would send the Solar's soul to Oblivion upon their death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:30:41-07:00","id":203145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203142#post203142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do not understand how language works.<br /> <br /> Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted. That is one of their definitive traits. That has always been been one of their definitive traits. In any area where Solars are competing against any other Exalted, Solars will have the advantage because having an advantage over others is part of what it means to be a Solar. That is how Exalted defines Solars.<br /> <br /> All the powers, of all the Exalted, are tautological because they are derived from the definitive traits of the Exalted chosen by the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...don't know how language works by saying exactly the thing it is? That's a new one.<br /> <br /> And...not really. Please, show me how anyone else is even close to that tautological level, where their might is derived from the fact they are the mightiest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 07-20-2014, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:36:07-07:00","id":203148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203145#post203145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I...don't know how language works by saying exactly the thing it is? That's a new one.<br /> <br /> And...not really. Please, show me how anyone else is even close to that tautological level, where their might is derived from the fact they are the mightiest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their might comes from the sun, the suns might comes from the creators of the universe getting together and making the most powerful being they could to defend the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:42:51-07:00","id":203151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203094#post203094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's something I can fully support, but... when you take away &quot;excellency&quot; as the distinguishing feature of the Solar Exalted, what remains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity.<br /> <br /> The richest theme among all the Exalted, and the most original of them -- almost no game plays up humanity as a concept, and instead demote it to a baseline where one adds external gimmicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 07-20-2014, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:47:15-07:00","id":203157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=202969#post202969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes the fact that Solar charms are now &quot;Humanizing&quot; which means less Over the top op, and more down to earth means that Solars are now the expression of human excellence as well as the sun's power. But they are still very human. Less so than a Lunar who accepts a portion of a beastial nature into them, and a Sidreal who seperates themselves from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking Evocation access we're basically talking basic functionally built into the Exaltation itself. There, Lunars taking in beast power is a relevant part, but Sidereal isolation is a cultural thing within the Bureau of Destiny, not an inherent Exaltation thing (Arcane Fate also not being built on in the same way, but being a consequence of actions). So I think it's less that Sidereals are separate from humanity, and more the nature of their Charms and reliance on martial arts that affects their Evocations, not their culture of standing apart and dealing with spirits much more than the common man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203142#post203142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In any area where Solars are competing against any other Exalted, Solars will have the advantage because having an advantage over others is part of what it means to be a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this has been stated as not being 100% true. As in, there may be some non-Solar Charms that at least appear more powerful than Solar Charms, it it's felt like that superiority is important to the theme of the splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203083#post203083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you homebrew your own setting, however, you will be playing a Lunar within the specific context of &quot;the Solars are returning and shaking the world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the Solars are returning and shaking the world doesn't mean that Lunar stories should be less epic. If anything the Solar return breaks their stalemate with the Sidereals and allows them to exploit the panic over the Solar return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-20-2014, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:56:56-07:00","id":203161,"title":"","content":"The Solars being the best at evocations because they are the mightiest and being the mightiest because the game says they're the mightiest, I don't know about a tautology, but it isn't what I would call a very interesting or sympathetic explanation.<br /> <br /> For comparison, look at how Exalted : The Sidereals sells how they are &quot;peerless&quot; at the martial arts. It bookends out of the limitations they face in developing new Charms, a narrative about overcoming weaknesses within themselves and a natural synergy with how their other Ability Charms work and what martial arts are like in Exalted. After we read about their martial arts, we both have a sense that it would be very hard for them not to be like this, and for it to be satisfying that they are like this. It's an interesting explanation and an interesting reason.<br /> <br /> Is this quite like that? Not yet, and from the comments so far doesn't seem like it will be. It might get better after it is presented in their book, like, I don't think John Morke is going to sell this as well in some random internet discussion, so no need overreacting on that. Of course, maybe it doesn't *have* to be interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:06:52-07:00","id":203169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203109#post203109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't quite accurate, as Solars do have a tiny number of things they can't do that other Exalts can, like shapeshifting or fate-weaving, but they don't actually need any of those things because those things are tools to solve problems with and Solars already have better tools for solving all of those problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would refrain from judgmental language saying that Solars have &quot;better&quot; tools for solving problems compared to Lunars and Sidereals and DBs etc. Solars certainly have <i>different</i> tools for solving the same problems. But <i>better</i>? That's <i>really</i> subjective. Holden's even talked about this idea before, and given examples of where Lunars definitely have a &quot;better&quot; toolkit (in shapeshifting - better in this case meaning &quot;more directly applicable to the problem, and an easier way of solving the problem&quot;) than Solars do, to solve <i>certain problems</i>. Absolute statements like &quot;Solars have better tools, always, period&quot; aren't helpful and are actually incorrect.<br /> <br /> I wish I could think of a good example for Sids, but all forms of astrology that we've seen suck ass, so yadda yadda hoping for the best with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203110#post203110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, in the universe of exalted &quot;the sun is the best at everything&quot; is as axiomatic as &quot;for every variable x, x=x is valid&quot;. When determining logic from the setting you need to understand that time flows forward, no two corporeal things can be in the same place at the same time, and the UCS is the apex of perfection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a relatively new concept that came about late in 2e when we started getting Incarnae stats. I certainly don't recall earlier early-2e or 1e portrayals of UCS being &quot;he's the best at everything, period&quot; or &quot;he is the apex of perfection.&quot; He was always depicted as King of the Gods, proud yet flaws to turn away from his Chosen and to find addiction in the Games, but I don't think some of these &quot;perfection&quot; ideas/ideals existed, or at least were not so explicit, before Glories (feel free to correct me if I'm wrong there, could be misremembering).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-20-2014, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:23:02-07:00","id":203195,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that Solars are supposed to get the most from their evocations because they are the ones that drive themselves and those around them to excellence. Is it at all surprising that they get the most out of their tools? Also, without having seen what everyone is getting, here is the way I am reading it: Solar's get top level evocations out of every magical material, because they can push everything to the maximum ability the thing is capable of, whether human followers, tools, or their voice. Others get the top level evocations out of their own magical material because they are attuned to it. Dragon-Blooded are awesome at it because they are also very closely tied to the concepts of making and using tools. Lunars, less so. They adapt themselves to the tools they have, or don't have, as needed. They just aren't the dedicated tool-using splat. Sidereals? They master themselves, and work with destiny. They should get max out of Starmetal, which is deeply associated with that. Should they get giant golden glowing swords? Sure, but they don't express that way, so they can't get the most out of it. Soulsteel? Jade? Basically the same deal. <br /> <br /> We also don't know exactly what is going to happen. May we will see that moonsilver evocations don't resonate well with what the Solar wants, so even if he can get to the uppermost evocation, they don't really help him in anyway. A sword that attaches itself to you while you swing it is great for not being disarmed, but its even better when you don't have hands to hold it.<br /> <br /> Also, what if Solar's get top tier access to every magical material type, but lots of artifacts made of say, moonsilver, build off of Lunar charms? Solar can get to top tier, but can't get to any charms with that Lunar pre-req. <br /> <br /> There's a million ways to handle this, some of which could be very bad (Sidereals suck, so they only get lowest tier access to Starmetal, and access to nothing else: that would be pretty crappy), or generally everyone gets access to the top of their own, 1st or 2nd in others, but still can't get anything with a prereq? Does that make Eclipse too good, because they can take a Jade artifact, learn the prereqs, and get the most out of it? Does that screw the Dawn caste over? Not really, he still has stuff to do, and he's not really hindered in any way. He just doesn't fill that particular niche that the Eclipse can. <br /> <br /> Is the Sidereal screwed because he's not going to be as good using Jade evocations, or soulsteel? Those are outliers in the concept of their Exaltation. That is not the case for Solars. Solars are more broad, and represent the potential of humanity, good or bad, as big damn heroes, or soul-eating villains. If that's what you hate about Exalted, don't think 3rd is going to help. If your problem is just that 'That Solar wields a Soulsteel daiklaive better than my Sidereal!' then Ex3 is probably going to annoy you as well. If that Solar uses that Soulsteel daiklaive as well as my Deathknight, but my Deathknight has a couple of tricks because the evocations build off of my charm set, I think that's fantastic. If the Solar uses that Soulsteel daiklaive exactly the same why my Deathknight does, I think that's kinda boring.<br /> <br /> I think I see what the developers are trying to do. At least, I hope they do, because the idea seems fantastic. It needs to be implemented carefully though, and with more subtlety than I can manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:25:41-07:00","id":203196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203145#post203145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And...not really. Please, show me how anyone else is even close to that tautological level, where their might is derived from the fact they are the mightiest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars shapeshift because they are shapeshifters and they are shapesfhiters because they shapeshift. Unless you are willing to accept &quot;Because Luna&quot; as a reason, but then you have to also accept &quot;Because Unconquered Sun&quot; in the case of Solars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:34:54-07:00","id":203208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203195#post203195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that make Eclipse too good, because they can take a Jade artifact, learn the prereqs, and get the most out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just on this: my impressions is that &quot;Eclipses can learn other Exalted Charms&quot; part of the anima was being discarded and replaced with a Keyword denoting &quot;Eclipses can learn this&quot; on certain Charms of other non-Exalt supernatural entities. So an Eclipse could not learn Evocations down a tree that has a Lunar or DB Charm as a prereq for that part of the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:44:58-07:00","id":203213,"title":"","content":"The way I always read it was that Conky isn't the best at everything because he's King of the Gods, it's because Perfection is his major domain. He is perfect because that is the core defining axiom of his existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T13:56:59-07:00","id":203217,"title":"","content":"Which is largely a conceit of the later parts of 2ed, as Zelbinnean noted. I just went and checked Games of Divinity, nothing of that sort in there. Hell, a quick CRL+F yielded no resuts of Perfection attached to the US at all, in the 2ed corebook. Nor the word Perfect attached to him, only solars. So we're back to a tauology that was later retroactively justifed via adding perfection onto the Sun.<br /> <br /> Sooo. There's where you're wrong, danelsan. Lunars themes flow from Luna, yes, but Solars did not until they were post-added. (And in addition, Luna's flow from real life folklore and the like, with limitations, unlike the LOLPERFECT parts of the solar. )<br /> <br /> ...I have zero idea why most of that is one big link and I have no idea how to change it. So please, ignore thattttt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 07-20-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T14:35:43-07:00","id":203255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203151#post203151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humanity.<br /> <br /> The richest theme among all the Exalted, and the most original of them -- almost no game plays up humanity as a concept, and instead demote it to a baseline where one adds external gimmicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed a valid point, but how do you propose making it mechanically interesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T14:51:30-07:00","id":203263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203217#post203217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is largely a conceit of the later parts of 2ed, as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean\">Zelbinnean</a> noted. I just went and checked Games of Divinity, nothing of that sort in there. Hell, a quick CRL+F yielded no resuts of Perfection attached to the US at all, in the 2ed corebook. Nor the word Perfect attached to him, only solars. So we're back to a tauology that was later retroactively justifed via adding perfection onto the Sun.<br /> <br /> Sooo. There's where you're wrong, danelsan. Lunars themes flow from Luna, yes, but Solars did not until they were post-added. (And in addition, Luna's flow from real life folklore and the like, with limitations, unlike the LOLPERFECT parts of the solar. )<br /> <br /> ...I have zero idea why most of that is one big link and I have no idea how to change it. So please, ignore thattttt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Url tag is at the end of your post before your ellipses just move that where you want it and it should clear right up for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T15:03:16-07:00","id":203265,"title":"","content":"Wundabar, thanks much. Zero idea how that happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T15:05:11-07:00","id":203268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203217#post203217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo. There's where you're wrong, danelsan. Lunars themes flow from Luna, yes, but Solars did not until they were post-added.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't quite right. All of the Exalted's themes flow from their patrons and always have. Whether or not a given patron's themes have been defined (or defined to one's satisfaction) is irrelevant to this fact. Also, the game designers rightly view the splats themselves as the really important parts: the traits the patrons have are partly whatever's fitting and cool, but mostly whatever traits are necessary for the splats to turn out as they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (And in addition, Luna's flow from real life folklore and the like, with limitations, unlike the LOLPERFECT parts of the solar. ) </div> </div> </div>Look up some sun deities.They're often associated with power, perfection, and kingship (which is itself associated with being the greatest). No, not all of them do this. This also doesn't matter. Luna doesn't live up to all depictions of all moon deities there have ever been, either. She lives up to the parts of moon associations the game designers chose, much as the Unconquered Sun lives up to the parts of sun associations the game designers chose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I have zero idea why most of that is one big link and I have no idea how to change it. So please, ignore thattttt. </div> </div> </div>nalak42 beat me to it, but a [/URL] tag got away from you in there. Cut and paste it at the end of whatever word you meant to be the end of the link (I presume the word &quot;noted&quot;). As for why? Eh, the forum software does wonky things sometimes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:03:32-07:00","id":203378,"title":"","content":"I definitely remember a quote that I'm pretty sure was Grabowski, back somewhere in the middle of 1e, about how you could bust into heaven and gank all the Primordials but the Unconquered Sun might be impossible to defeat due to being &quot;a priori unbeatable and unkillable&quot;, or something like that. I can't find it now (it's not on the old wiki that I can see), but I know some quotes are lost, so hopefully someone else will corroborate. It's also pretty easy to read between the lines and see that the things associated with the UCS, like orichalcum and Solars, have themes of perfection and universal excellence, and extrapolate those to him. It's not as though the line talks about him at length while leaving such descriptions conspicuously absent -- the Incarnae are almost completely ignored as subject matter until Glories, on purpose.<br /> <br /> All that said: I thought Morke's answer was pretty good? I mean, it was basically a clearer reiteration of what he said when asked about it originally. Distilling it to &quot;because Solars&quot; seems a little silly, because...yes, &quot;why do Solars get this thing other people don't get&quot; it going to be a question answered in terms of the properties of Solars. What else could it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:57:22-07:00","id":203459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203076#post203076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who are &quot;disinclined towards Solars&quot; will have issues with Exalted, as the core premise of the game is how the return of the champions of old will shake the world. This is the story of how they shape the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I find sort of amusing is that this &quot;core premise&quot; is being diluted by the addition of Exigents (who are also returning to shape the future and whatnot), Getimiansnas and Liminals. And whatever the other new Exalts are. Solaroids aren't the only new hotness shaking up the status quo anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a reason the Solar Exalted are fully playable out of the corebook, and all the other Exalted types quickly presented in the &quot;Antagonist&quot; chapter. </div> </div> </div>Thanks to the magic of PDFs, this problem now has a solution. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:03:21-07:00","id":203460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203459#post203459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find sort of amusing is that this &quot;core premise&quot; is being diluted by the addition of Exigents (who are also returning to shape the future and whatnot), Getimiansnas and Liminals. And whatever the other new Exalts are. Solaroids aren't the only new hotness shaking up the status quo anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've gathered, none of these are returning God-Kings, so the core premise is not actually diluted. Also, since 3e is more like the Ultimate Universe for Exalted, with parts of the backstory rewritten, who says the Liminals are 'returning'? They could've been around for millenia as far as we know.<br /> <br /> And lastly... isn't the whole point of EVERY type of Exalted to shake up the status quo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:23:28-07:00","id":203516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203460#post203460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've gathered, none of these are returning God-Kings, so the core premise is not actually diluted. Also, since 3e is more like the Ultimate Universe for Exalted, with parts of the backstory rewritten, who says the Liminals are 'returning'? They could've been around for millenia as far as we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Not millennia, maybe, but Liminals have definitely been around for centuries by the time the game starts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First Age ends with the fall of the Solars, which sends the world into a period of decline that culminates in the near total death of Creation. Therefore, the Liminals first appear during the Shogunate, and probably toward the end of that era. I will say that this is just a projection; it is concievable that I will change my mind between now and then and have them pop up even earlier. The period I drop them into will help set the tone for the splat, and that leaves me with a few entry points.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you say, it seems unreasonable to assume that Getimians are first popping up at the same time the Solars return, too. The return of Exigents <i>has</i> been said to be a result of the Solars' return in some way (and I've been interested in the particulars). As you say, though, they're not returning God-Kings, so it's all good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And lastly... isn't the whole point of EVERY type of Exalted to shake up the status quo? </div> </div> </div>Well, after a fashion. The goals and aims of the Liminals really aren't clear yet, but as a splat they don't seem pointed in that direction:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Liminals are interesting, because unlike the other new Exalt types, they don\u2019t really have a huge impact on the setting or its history. They are purely a fun idea, an indulgence on our part\u2013where we saw room for something really cool that the setting could produce, and we took advantage of the opportunity to put them into play. The Liminals will be fun, playable, and will mesh in interesting ways with the classic Exalted, but they will also serve as an example to the players and storytellers of how to unwind and find these great new character opportunities throughout Exalted. They are an example of what the lore of the game can make possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:23:38-07:00","id":203517,"title":"","content":"I always find it funny/weird how mad people get about Solars being the best at every subsystem when they don't actually <i>have</i> a native subsystem of their own. Lunars had shapeshifting, Sidereals had Astrology and Dragon-Blooded had elemental teamwork synergy.<br /> <br /> The only thing Solars have is to be really really good at the things that everyone has access to.<br /> <br /> I actually found that it really helps drive home their nature as the &quot;Exemplary human skill&quot; Exalted. They don't have an esoteric subsytem because normal humans don't have any esoteric magic to use natively, and any magic they do have is the result of mastering a particular skill, which is exactly what Martial Arts/Sorcery/Evocations are meant to be expressions of, Mastery of Facepunching, Occult Forces and your favored weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:28:33-07:00","id":203522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203208#post203208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just on this: my impressions is that &quot;Eclipses can learn other Exalted Charms&quot; part of the anima was being discarded and replaced with a Keyword denoting &quot;Eclipses can learn this&quot; on certain Charms of other non-Exalt supernatural entities. So an Eclipse could not learn Evocations down a tree that has a Lunar or DB Charm as a prereq for that part of the tree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But if that prereq Charm has the Eclipse-OK keyword? I suspect we will see that more of them do than don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:32:54-07:00","id":203525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203460#post203460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I've gathered, none of these are returning God-Kings, so the core premise is not actually diluted. Also, since 3e is more like the Ultimate Universe for Exalted, with parts of the backstory rewritten, who says the Liminals are 'returning'? They could've been around for millenia as far as we know.<br /> <br /> And lastly... isn't the whole point of EVERY type of Exalted to shake up the status quo?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, DBs are kind of the status quo. Same with Sidereals. I suspect the same with the Liminals. Of course, all PCs are supposed to shake up the status quo. I've seen references to 'a missing Exalt type' since way way back in MoEP: Alchemicals, and I think even further back, but I'm not sure. Some of that may have been writers deliberately leaving a hole for another writer to fill later, but I figure that counts, since the current writers are filling those holes, knowing they are there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:36:49-07:00","id":203528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203522#post203522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that prereq Charm has the Eclipse-OK keyword? I suspect we will see that more of them do than don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess if it's an Evocation depending on a spirit's or raksha's Charm or something. They've been really clear about how Eclipses won't get the Charms of other Exalted at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:42:44-07:00","id":203575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203517#post203517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always find it funny/weird how mad people get about Solars being the best at every subsystem when they don't actually <i>have</i> a native subsystem of their own. Lunars had shapeshifting, Sidereals had Astrology and Dragon-Blooded had elemental teamwork synergy.<br /> <br /> The only thing Solars have is to be really really good at the things that everyone has access to.<br /> <br /> I actually found that it really helps drive home their nature as the &quot;Exemplary human skill&quot; Exalted. They don't have an esoteric subsytem because normal humans don't have any esoteric magic to use natively, and any magic they do have is the result of mastering a particular skill, which is exactly what Martial Arts/Sorcery/Evocations are meant to be expressions of, Mastery of Facepunching, Occult Forces and your favored weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the sub-systems that other then the DB synergy, are total trash and hinder more then help you other then some very specific combinations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:03:59-07:00","id":203584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203575#post203575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the sub-systems that other then the DB synergy, are total trash and hinder more then help you other then some very specific combinations?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the fault of bad writers, not because the sub-systems are, in and of themselves bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:40:19-07:00","id":203595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203584#post203584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the fault of bad writers, not because the sub-systems are, in and of themselves bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does that alivate the point of being a bit vexed when someone can do something better then you in every way, and when you point it out, the return is &quot;Oh, but they can't do this useless subsystem&quot;? Because it doesn't seem to in the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:19:39-07:00","id":203623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203595#post203595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how does that alivate the point of being <u>a bit vexed</u> when someone can do something <u>better then you in every way</u>, and when you point it out, the return is &quot;Oh, but they can't do this <u>useless subsystem</u>&quot;? Because it doesn't seem to in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Addressing the underlined parts in order:<br /> <br /> 1: Unless I've been grossly misinformed, your feelings aren't a concern when it comes to Exalted's development. What is a concern is developing a solid set of rules to support a game that has several themes for each Exalt type, as well as making sure that the narrative of the overall game makes sense. At present, Solars being good at the commonly available subsystems is a way to express their themes as the &quot;exemplary skill&quot; Exalted.<br /> <br /> 2: Solars aren't &quot;Better than you in every way&quot;, they are very very good in areas that they make an effort to be very very good in, but they are not unbeatable.<br /> <br /> 3: Stop thinking about the game in terms of 2E. This wont apply anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:36:49-07:00","id":203632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203595#post203595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how does that alivate the point of being a bit vexed when someone can do something better then you in every way, and when you point it out, the return is &quot;Oh, but they can't do this useless subsystem&quot;? Because it doesn't seem to in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, let's start working under the assumption that the Devs don't want to create useless subsystems, and that they plan on making shapeshifting, astrology, elemental teamwork charms, robotic charm swapouts, and...whatever the Getimians and the Liminals do...as cool as they possibly can. I mean, they're designing a game, they want that game to be fun to play, they're gonna put all the effort they can into making those exalt-type-specific tricks cool.<br /> <br /> If your character concept is &quot;I want to be the very best at X,&quot; then you want to play a Solar, unless X is something weird that solar themes of &quot;paragon of mortal skill&quot; don't let you do, like shapeshifting or altering probability through the use of judicious red ink. Solar magic is all about &quot;I am a peerless paragon who takes this thing mortals can do and then does it orders of magnitude better, to the point where I outclass gods.&quot; Nobody is gonna be a better swordsman than Invincible Sword Princess...but that doesn't mean you can't beat her in a fight, if the game's well-designed. It just means you can't beat her in a swordfight, unless you play dirty.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a Lunar or a Sidereal or whatever, your concept is probably not &quot;I am the best swordsman there is.&quot; It's probably &quot;I am a swordsman who can fly like Peter Pan,&quot; or &quot;I am a swordsman who can cut you so fast your grandpa falls over dead,&quot; or &quot;I am a swordsman who grows six arms and has swords in ALL of them and did I mention the arms are long and super-stretchy because I have an octopus totem and that I change color rapidly to hypnotize my opponents with color and weirdly beautiful movements while we fight?&quot;<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, though, these other character concepts are about making fun use of interesting tricks not available to Solars. What Solars do is just practice swordfighting a while bunch, and develop a deeper bond with the very soul of their sword because they're spending all their time and energy on mastering it rather than mastering Dancing Octopus Style. A Solar is busy meditating and sharpening his blade while the Sidereal is busy planning fate to arrange who he's going to swordfight over the next week and the Lunar is busy developing a trick to secrete blinding poison from his suckers to spray on his enemies. These guys might beat Invincible Sword Princess in a fight! They're not strictly worse at combat! It's just that she's better at bonding with her sword, and they're better at other things.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Please note I picked swords because they're an easier example than other things, but this holds true of most areas of the game. Solars do a human thing (like get really good with their favorite tools) with divine skill. Other Exalts can do human things really good, but their true power lies in inhuman powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:50:03-07:00","id":203637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203632#post203632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your character concept is &quot;I want to be the very best at X,&quot; then you want to play a Solar, unless X is something weird that solar themes of &quot;paragon of mortal skill&quot; don't let you do, like shapeshifting or altering probability through the use of judicious red ink. Solar magic is all about &quot;I am a peerless paragon who takes this thing mortals can do and then does it orders of magnitude better, to the point where I outclass gods.&quot; Nobody is gonna be a better swordsman than Invincible Sword Princess...but that doesn't mean you can't beat her in a fight, if the game's well-designed. It just means you can't beat her in a swordfight, unless you play dirty.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, what I don't like about the Solar swordswoman is that there is this place of \u201cOh, you don't beat her unless you play dirty\u201d.<br /> <br /> Like there's this whole idea that the Lunar swordfighter (or fighter) can't beat her just because in the heat of the fight, there always going to be some variation, you can't control everything, and sometimes the second best wins. Instead they have to cheat or be weird.<br /> <br /> I think like if you play a Lunar swordswoman, you maybe don't want to play \u201cbest in the universe, check it out\u201d, but why not let them play someone who can become close enough to sometimes beat the best, through skill alone?<br /> <br /> I suspect most people who play a Lunar would be fine with &quot;I only win sometimes, and I have my own flavour&quot;, but not &quot;I never win unless I'm a cheating cheater, but I have my own flavour&quot;. Being told &quot;Solars generally win&quot; fine. Being told &quot;You always lose unless you cheat&quot; seems to suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:02:05-07:00","id":203643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203637#post203637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, what I don't like about the Solar swordswoman is that there is this place of \u201cOh, you don't beat her unless you play dirty\u201d.<br /> <br /> Like there's this whole idea that the Lunar swordfighter (or fighter) can't beat her just because in the heat of the fight, there always going to be some variation, you can't control everything, and sometimes the second best wins. Instead they have to cheat or be weird.<br /> <br /> I think like if you play a Lunar swordswoman, you maybe don't want to play \u201cbest in the universe, check it out\u201d, but why not let them play someone who can become close enough to sometimes beat the best, through skill alone?<br /> <br /> I suspect most people who play a Lunar would be fine with &quot;I only win sometimes, and I have my own flavour&quot;, but not &quot;I never win unless I'm a cheating cheater, but I have my own flavour&quot;. Being told &quot;Solars generally win&quot; fine. Being told &quot;You always lose unless you cheat&quot; seems to suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I've played Lunars, and I get that, I really do.<br /> <br /> But when I say &quot;play dirty,&quot; I don't mean always mean &quot;cheat.&quot;<br /> <br /> In real life, the most skilled swordsman does not always win. Sometimes they're in a fight with another swordsman who isn't as SKILLED...but has more endurance and tires them out. Or is just straight up FASTER and outmaneuvers them. Or has much better reach. Or is freaky strong and snaps their sword with heavy hammering blows. This is how a Lunar swordsman beats a Solar swordsman. Sometimes the more skilled swordsman is up against an opponent who has mastered some esoteric sword style they've never heard of, like an epee fencer faced with some Shao Lin monk coming after her with paired scimitars and what the bleeding hell he just kicked me in the face I thought this was a goddam swordfight! Sometimes a skilled swordsman goes up against someone who, whether or not they Know Kung Fu, is just plain LUCKIER than they are. That's how a Sidereal wins. You're not gonna be more skilled than she is, but at the end of the day her skill and her supernal connection with the soul of her sword might not save her when you're coming at her with the grace of a gazelle and the strength of a bear and almost as much skill as she's got, or if Fate demands that she slip on a banana peel right as you thrust.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the less skilled competitor wins, especially if the less skilled competitor has other talents that can make up or overcome the difference in skill. Lunar PC can TOTALLY beat Invincible Sword Princess in a fair fight in an arena setting without spraying poison in her eyes, sure! They're trying to smooth out the power disparities in 3E, remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-21-2014, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:11:10-07:00","id":203647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203459#post203459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I find sort of amusing is that this &quot;core premise&quot; is being diluted by the addition of Exigents (who are also returning to shape the future and whatnot), Getimiansnas and Liminals. And whatever the other new Exalts are. Solaroids aren't the only new hotness shaking up the status quo anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents date back to the Primordial War, Liminals possibly back to the Shogunate, and Getimians also seem like they've been a problem for the Sidereals for quite some time if dealing with them is basically one of the functions of Sidereal Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:16:22-07:00","id":203650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203056#post203056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meaning something other then a damn tautology.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like saying that a description of why real life human beings are the dominant species in terms of our genetics, our manual dexterity and our neurology is a tautology.<br /> <br /> John's explanation isn't &quot;because Solar&quot;, it's a reference to how the premise of Solars and the premise of Evocations line up together thematically. What other possible type of explanation for this setting of theme and mythology is there?<br /> <br /> I mean Jesus, describing the capabilities of Lunars in terms of moon mythology is okay, but describing Solars in terms of human culture hero mythology is a tautology?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-21-2014, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:21:06-07:00","id":203661,"title":"","content":"<br /> &quot;2: Solars aren't &quot;Better than you in every way&quot;, they are very very good in areas that they make an effort to be very very good in, but they are not unbeatable.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, thematically this includes pretty much anything. I get that Solars are meant to be a big deal and the most powerful <b><i>overall</i></b>, no problem there, but sometimes it feels like no one else can outdo them in any one thing because they are Solars and have to the best in every single thing - which essentially constrains the other themes. There are exceptions, but not that many - shapeshifting (which a solar can definitely tap into with bio-augmentations and artefacts, which they are the best at), and astrology. Maybe martial arts too, but once they have learned an SMA style I am not sure if their higher mote pools don't cancel out any sidereal bonuses.I'd love it if 3E solars weren't automatically the favourites in pretty much any single thing they care to do, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not so sold on the whole &quot;solars are defined by their humanity&quot; theme. Many charms, especially non-starting ones, go way beyond human perfection and limitations - conjuring a magical golden sword out of thin air, for example, Being defined by humanity giving you access to the broadest and best powers makes no more sense than getting them through the theme of other exalted - Lunars experience the world through myriads of forms that give them unparalleled insight into its working, Dragonblooded are infused by the elements that created and define Creation, etc. These two splats in particular can also have archetypes and charms play on the humanity them (they don't have to be that, but it's definitely a possibility in their theme). They just seem to be humans exposed to something else than what solars got.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203632#post203632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar magic is all about &quot;I am a peerless paragon who takes this thing mortals can do and then does it orders of magnitude better, to the point where I outclass gods.&quot; Nobody is gonna be a better swordsman than Invincible Sword Princess...but that doesn't mean you can't beat her in a fight, if the game's well-designed. It just means you can't beat her in a swordfight, unless you play dirty.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a Lunar or a Sidereal or whatever, your concept is probably not &quot;I am the best swordsman there is.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>/headdesk. By Cthulhu, how I hate this argument. You are an exalted, a great hero, but you can never be as great at &quot;Insert heroism here&quot; as the other type of great<b>er</b> hero, because that is how heroes work - by not overcoming the odds and not becoming something greater than they were. You could try to cheat to win, but actually, the great<b>er</b> hero can be even better at cheating, because it is a thing and thus not something you as not-great<b>er </b>hero can be better at (if they care to do it at all). &quot;Everything humans do, better than everyone else&quot; can really be a bitch to build around when there are 5-6 other splats who are also great heroes with incredible powers and potential (a.k.a. Exalted)<br /> <br /> To me, the concept - if it is to be the cornerstone of Solar design philosophy, though I prefer &quot;Returned god-kings of old&quot; as the more definite and thematic one - it involved solars being the most accomplished at the pure implementation of a skill. However, this need not and should not equal automatically being the better at everything involving this skill. For example, you are the best guitar player because you are best at actually playing the guitar, but when it comes to an overall performance, others can compensate with on-stage presence or a better designed song. The best swordsman may be the one with the most pure technique, but in a fight, this could be offset by the enemy being stronger and more agile. They can be the better swordsman - as in, fighter who uses a sword - even if they aren't the best at their sword technique. This is okay, what I don't want to see (but fear is possible) is something that boils down to &quot;You are a solar, this is something a solar can do, you win.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to evocations - the idea of having special abilities based on your weapon and stuff only you can do with it is cool enough, and has been in some games I've played with. Though I'm not sure it is so good if evocations allow something that impinges on the theme of another splat, like a solar throwing off waves of flame and molten earth that rival or outdo the mastery of a Dragon-blooded who uses their innate powers to do the same.<br /> <br /> edit: Wise Old Guru, I saw your clarification - that I can definitely agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-21-2014, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T03:18:51-07:00","id":203703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203661#post203661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being defined by humanity giving you access to the broadest and best powers makes no more sense than getting them through the theme of other exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how the majority of mythological and literary heroes are basically human in form and function, and consistently overcome all the monsters and things?<br /> <br /> You know how humankind is by far the most impressive living thing in existence, as exemplified by stuff like this wonder box we're communicating by?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T03:32:43-07:00","id":203705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203703#post203703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know how the majority of mythological and literary heroes are basically human in form and function, and consistently overcome all the monsters and things?<br /> <br /> You know how humankind is by far the most impressive living thing in existence, as exemplified by stuff like this wonder box we're communicating by?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from, but honestly whole humans are pretty terrifying, ants impress me more. Simplicity is beautiful to me, and complexity rising from simplicity. We humans are an action packed novel, but ants are like a perfectly composed poem...anyway, I think sleepiness is causing me to drift off topic here, so I'll just reiterate that Solars should be good at inventing tools and stealing fire from the gods and defeating monsters and talking attractive divinities into bed or out of eating them, and mastering their magical toys lets them play into culture hero tropes really well. Other exalt types have slightly more specific genre tropes to play into already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T03:50:42-07:00","id":203717,"title":"","content":"I think in this edition I think you're going to have to want to be something pretty specific not to want to be a Solar. I can easily see an awesome character being a solar agent of heaven with a starmetal daiklave gifted to him by his sidereal friend, but if you want to be a super astrologer you should probably be a sidereal. Likewise you can be from an ancient noble family or be a terrifying monster from the edge of the world, with a flaming spear or flowing shape changing weapon. But you're entire family won't likely be exalted and you won't be able to easily turn into a hundred different forms. Lunars have a pretty awesome &quot;exclusively lunar&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T04:07:38-07:00","id":203725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203717#post203717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can easily see an awesome character being a solar agent of heaven with a starmetal daiklave gifted to him by his sidereal friend, but if you want to be a super astrologer you should probably be a sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even super astrologer for me; the idea of having a niche thing that they're superior at interests me less than the idea that they've got a literary archetype (in this case, prophet, advisor and teacher) and set of expressions (esoteric causality weirdness) that pervades their whole range of Abilities. Being the &quot;best&quot; at astrology or destiny controlling or whatever doesn't capture my imagination as much as punching somebody and giving them a choice between taking severe damage and having something extremely fortunate for you happen.<br /> <br /> Even Martial Arts... disregarding Sidereal Arts, I have a feeling John has something in mind for them by his comments about Scroll of the Monk II, something that might not be about being the best, but something they're more intimately connected to.<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't really see them as being about mastery of powerful tools (insert snarky comment about manipulating Dynasts).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T04:24:19-07:00","id":203729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203703#post203703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how the majority of mythological and literary heroes are basically human in form and function, and consistently overcome all the monsters and things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is sort of expected in a human mythology, on a world where humans are the sole intelligent life. Creation is a world created by inhuman primorial beings, run by spirits and gods, with intelligent elemental spirits, and populated by all matter of mystical creatures. If their link to &quot;humanity&quot; is the biggest or one of the biggest defining traits of Solars, there must be a reason why that matters so much - what about Humanity justifies these abilities in that world. Perhaps solars are defined by heroic virtues, and sure, humans can be heroes - but in a world where there are other intelligent creatures, there is no reason why heroism should be limited to humanity. Just because we are the sole heroes in our culture doesn't make it a universally valid archetype for every possible situation. Plus, heroism is defined by its opposition to the mundane and mass traits as a whole. Heroes are different to most humans - in a sense, they are outsiders.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this connection to humanity should mean solars are the most human exalts, and I'm not sure this makes much sense - the association of the Solar Exalted with humanity seems to be more about the lack of association with anything else (at least anything concrete). After all, all exalted start as humans, and become been empowered by an exaltation related to one of the incarna (or the sub-soul of a Primordial, in case of Dragon-blooded), none of whom is particularly human in itself. Sol Invictus favors humans, sure, but that in itself does make them any more important. Every exalt has begun their existance as a human and as the High First Age taught us, at the peak of their power the chosen of the Sun were no more human than their mates and viziers... if not less.<br /> <br /> I would argue that if anything, it is the link to (classical) heroism that makes solars so special, but to me beyond their gimmicks all exalts are heroes. This is why I prefer to stress the other Solar defining traits - that they are the chosen of the Sun (with all the influences that entails), the God-Kings of old, the leaders and bearers of the original mandate of Creation. They give them a much better place and legitimacy within the setting.<br /> <br /> A somewhat narrower theme will in turn determine what someone is good at. Perhaps solars could have evocations that stress their mastery and power - a gleaming armor that make everyone who wishes to strike the bearer avert their gaze or go blind, a bow whose arrows disappear and instead the rays of the sun fall as orihalcum spikes, or a banner which, unfurled, will restore make routing troops turn back or summon guardian spirits to battle (though the latter could work for sidereals as well,with a minor twist). Tremors of earth or waves of fire seem like something more in tune with what I would expect from a Dragon-blooded. It is not so much about which does the most damage but what sort of things fit someone's type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-21-2014, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T05:04:39-07:00","id":203739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">conjuring a magical golden sword out of thin air, for example</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm... mental note, come up with Solar who construes Glorious Solar Saber in terms of going through sword katas with such prowess that they cut despite the lack of a sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T05:11:17-07:00","id":203743,"title":"","content":"I think they need some flashy light/fire based abilities just to remind everyone that they're called solars for a <i>reason</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T05:15:46-07:00","id":203746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203743#post203743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they need some flashy light/fire based abilities just to remind everyone that they're called solars for a <i>reason</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what their Anima is for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T05:33:58-07:00","id":203754,"title":"","content":"The anima is an extension of that theme, but it only provides you with 1-2 more effects that tend to be either personal or cover a small area in your immediate vicinity. For more you should have charms, and I guess some evocations can also help drive home the theme or modify it ever so slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:42:54-07:00","id":203840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203743#post203743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they need some flashy light/fire based abilities just to remind everyone that they're called solars for a <i>reason</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they've had em in prior editions and those Charms are rather iconic...Glorious Solar Saber, Glorious Solar Plate, Immaculate Golden Bow, Spirit Weapons...Phantom-Conjuring Performance, Phantom Steed, Terrifying Apparition of Glory, Words-as-Workshop Method, <i>Wyld-Shaping Technique.</i><br /> <br /> There's no reason to think they won't be in 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203522#post203522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that prereq Charm has the Eclipse-OK keyword? I suspect we will see that more of them do than don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's an Exalted Charm, I bet you won't. And imo that's perfectly fine. It doesn't hurt Solar power at all not to be able to access a couple of Evocations on non-orichalcum Artifacts. Hell, it doesn't even affect their &quot;best at Evocations&quot; thing. &quot;Best&quot; doesn't necessarily mean &quot;has access to every single thing therein.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:53:21-07:00","id":203845,"title":"","content":"If I had to pick a caste to be the best at Evocations It'd be Dawn, but the idea of eclipses having a couple of extra tricks up their sleeves doesn't sound too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-21-2014, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:16:26-07:00","id":203894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203729#post203729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A somewhat narrower theme will in turn determine what someone is good at. Perhaps solars could have evocations that stress their mastery and power - a gleaming armor that make everyone who wishes to strike the bearer avert their gaze or go blind, a bow whose arrows disappear and instead the rays of the sun fall as orihalcum spikes, or a banner which, unfurled, will restore make routing troops turn back or summon guardian spirits to battle (though the latter could work for sidereals as well,with a minor twist). Tremors of earth or waves of fire seem like something more in tune with what I would expect from a Dragon-blooded. It is not so much about which does the most damage but what sort of things fit someone's type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was kind of the point of evocations? I don't have to play a DB to play somebody who calls down bolts of lightning from the sky and forms a hurricane as I fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:27:17-07:00","id":203900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203729#post203729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A somewhat narrower theme will in turn determine what someone is good at. Perhaps solars could have evocations that stress their mastery and power - a gleaming armor that make everyone who wishes to strike the bearer avert their gaze or go blind, a bow whose arrows disappear and instead the rays of the sun fall as orihalcum spikes, or a banner which, unfurled, will restore make routing troops turn back or summon guardian spirits to battle (though the latter could work for sidereals as well,with a minor twist). Tremors of earth or waves of fire seem like something more in tune with what I would expect from a Dragon-blooded. It is not so much about which does the most damage but what sort of things fit someone's type.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those would be very cool ideas for Evocations on orichalcum gear. I just wonder how much some of those effects you mentioned might be better served as native Charms. Then again we haven't seen an actual Evocation spelled out in detail yet so it's hard to say what kinds of effects are &quot;normal&quot; for them. I'd just be a little disappointed if the Artifact legion banner threaded through with orichalcum wire had the same mechanical effect as, say, the War Charm Rout-Stemming Gesture or whatever.<br /> <br /> To the second point: the only Evocation tree we've seen is for a red jade daiklave. We've heard about other ones, sure (Stormcaller, which spawns a real hurricane above you when drawn - that effect implies it may be blue jade but we don't have that detail yet), but the only cascade publicized is Volcano Cutter. So it makes sense that the Evocations on Volcano Cutter have names evoking fire and magma (it's supposed be a sword that cut a volcano, right?) and probably also playing in to volcanic effects. We haven't seen any Evocations specifically designed for an orichalcum weapon, but it stands to reason that orichalcum won't involve throwing magma at people or creating an earthquake. Probably.<br /> <br /> On this note I feel like jade Artifacts would be the easiest to guess Evocation effects for. They'll likely build off of colored jade elemental themes, at least loosely. The other MM have very different themes and feels, so I'd expect fewer overt elemental effects, but possibly obtaining those effects through a different method than directly doing it with elemental jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:45:04-07:00","id":203923,"title":"","content":"Any firey orichalcum stuff is going to be of the golden nuclear inferno sort. Magma is too ground based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:35:39-07:00","id":203949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203923#post203923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any firey orichalcum stuff is going to be of the golden nuclear inferno sort. Magma is too ground based.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>\u2622CAUTION!!\u2622</b><br /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:42:57-07:00","id":203953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203923#post203923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any firey orichalcum stuff is going to be of the golden nuclear inferno sort. Magma is too ground based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Maybe. Volcanoes/magma aren't entirely out of theme for orichalcum. Remember that refining pure orichalcum from ore required caldera-level ambient heat in the past couple eds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:57:55-07:00","id":203974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203528#post203528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess if it's an Evocation depending on a spirit's or raksha's Charm or something. They've been really clear about how Eclipses won't get the Charms of other Exalted at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hadn't heard that. I just heard that they were going to get any Charm that was specifically tagged Eclipse-OK. Interesting. Do you have the quote for that, that they will not be tagging Lunar, Sidereal, DB, or other charms Eclipse-OK?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:02:01-07:00","id":203978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">New Eclipse anima power: <b>No more Charmshare between Exalts via the anima power.</b> Eclipses -do- retain the ability to learn certain magics of other sorts of supernatural beings, such as spirits-- there's a Keyword denoting powers they can pick up (generally flavorful ones such as the ability to walk on clouds or interrogate the sea to give up its secrets, which would help them in their role as walkers-among-all-courts). These shared Charms don't have a special price hike, since the fact that they're Eclipse-available means we already judged they weren't going to break anything in an Eclipse's hand, and with that in place, there's no reason to tax your fun.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Emphasis mine. It's off the &quot;what we know&quot; wiki, so sure the final product may look different, but this was the design intent from over a year ago and I don't know why it would change after all the problems cross-Exalt charmshare caused in 2e.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:16:49-07:00","id":203985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203978#post203978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Emphasis mine. It's off the &quot;what we know&quot; wiki, so sure the final product may look different, but this was the design intent from over a year ago and I don't know why it would change after all the problems cross-Exalt charmshare caused in 2e.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. I think I like that. I'm surprised, but I do like it. I mean, the other splat books are a LONG way away, so things could change, but I think this is a very good thing. I like the idea that they can now write the charm's for all the other splats without worrying about Eclipse balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:52:06-07:00","id":204035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203650#post203650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean Jesus, describing the capabilities of Lunars in terms of moon mythology is okay, but describing Solars in terms of human culture hero mythology is a tautology?</div> </div> </div> </div>The simple fact that you can't see the difference between a collection of moon mythology, with flaws and downsides, verses a combined algmeram that equates to perfection forever(And if you dare bring up Limit I will slap you because every damn exalt has that) means this conversation is done, because there's not a fucking thing I can do to even slightly shift your mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T12:08:12-07:00","id":204041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204035#post204035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simple fact that you can't see the difference between a collection of moon mythology, with flaws and downsides, verses a combined algmeram that equates to perfection forever(And if you dare bring up Limit I will slap you because every damn exalt has that) means this conversation is done, because there's not a fucking thing I can do to even slightly shift your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect doesn't necessarily mean unbeatable. And it isn't perfect forever anyway, just perfect in whatever your specialized little field is. A solar shouldn't want to face 12 to 1 odds against DBs or walk right into an expertly set sidereal trap. Nevermind in second ed they could do both easily, but even if they keep perfection as a theme they shouldn't in the next edition. I don't care if you make zero mistakes going 30-1 against a trained, equipped, Wyld hunt should be a feat, even for a perfect swordsman. Again though, previous editions not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T12:22:10-07:00","id":204049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203643#post203643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look, I've played Lunars, and I get that, I really do.<br /> <br /> But when I say &quot;play dirty,&quot; I don't mean always mean &quot;cheat.&quot;<br /> <br /> In real life, the most skilled swordsman does not always win. Sometimes they're in a fight with another swordsman who isn't as SKILLED...but has more endurance and tires them out. Or is just straight up FASTER and outmaneuvers them. Or has much better reach. Or is freaky strong and snaps their sword with heavy hammering blows. This is how a Lunar swordsman beats a Solar swordsman. Sometimes the more skilled swordsman is up against an opponent who has mastered some esoteric sword style they've never heard of, like an epee fencer faced with some Shao Lin monk coming after her with paired scimitars and what the bleeding hell he just kicked me in the face I thought this was a goddam swordfight! Sometimes a skilled swordsman goes up against someone who, whether or not they Know Kung Fu, is just plain LUCKIER than they are. That's how a Sidereal wins. You're not gonna be more skilled than she is, but at the end of the day her skill and her supernal connection with the soul of her sword might not save her when you're coming at her with the grace of a gazelle and the strength of a bear and almost as much skill as she's got, or if Fate demands that she slip on a banana peel right as you thrust.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the less skilled competitor wins, especially if the less skilled competitor has other talents that can make up or overcome the difference in skill. Lunar PC can TOTALLY beat Invincible Sword Princess in a fair fight in an arena setting without spraying poison in her eyes, sure! They're trying to smooth out the power disparities in 3E, remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's seems more reasonable than what I thought you were saying.<br /> <br /> But another point of view - it's still hard for me to see how the guy who goes and does weight and speed training to win against the more skilled fencer is playing dirty. He just has the will and the skill in him go through that hard work, to train harder and better and do more with his body, and the fencer doesn't. So why would the fencer get to arrogantly call out that he's playing dirty when he does? Seriously, what's more entitled than thinking your &quot;skill&quot; gets to win out over the guy who trains and develops his athleticism, and that its not fair when someone else puts in the effort to train that? And that's essentially what Lunars are doing - they're not being helped out by some cheat.<br /> <br /> Similar with a Sidereal. He's a lot like a sorceror - he's not really &quot;playing dirty&quot; when he has the will and the skill and the dedication to understand and sacrifice of himself and master occult forces that are beyond your ken. Yeah, maybe you step on a banana peel, but he's not necessarily doing anything so gross - he's exerting skill to subtly move and change the world around him so that, how the forces of the world are pushing things to move so, even when he doesn't do anything that skilled in terms of swordsmanship, he's in the right place, and he's winning.<br /> <br /> Like, I don't disagree with you, just still feels weird to call any of this playing dirty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:24:11-07:00","id":204157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203894#post203894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was kind of the point of evocations? I don't have to play a DB to play somebody who calls down bolts of lightning from the sky and forms a hurricane as I fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a point, maybe. As far as I understand it, evocations are about the sort of special unique stuff you can do with a specific weapon. If they are determined by the material, then yes, a red jade daiklave might give you some firey powers, and that is ok. However, a solar with a red jave daiklave out-burninating or even rivaling an actual fire aspect dragonblood with the respective charms is a big no-no for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-21-2014, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:41:40-07:00","id":204186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204035#post204035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simple fact that you can't see the difference between a collection of moon mythology, with flaws and downsides, verses a combined algmeram that equates to perfection forever</div> </div> </div> </div>Three points:<br /> 1) I thought the problem was that explanations for Solar superiority were tautological, not that Solars were superior at all.<br /> 2) Who else has said &quot;perfection forever&quot;?<br /> 3) The hell is an &quot;algmeram&quot;?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:57:40-07:00","id":204198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204186#post204186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The hell is an &quot;algmeram&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>From context, it's a typo of &quot;amalgam.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:02:01-07:00","id":204201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=203643#post203643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, the less skilled competitor wins, especially if the less skilled competitor has other talents that can make up or overcome the difference in skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, because this is one of those things that bears repeating: Sometimes the less skilled competitor wins even if he or she has no other talents that can overcome the difference in skill. Superiority is not certainty. The odds of victory are rarely exactly 0% or 100%. The better fighter can lose without trickery; the weaker fighter can win without pulling out an ace in the hole.<br /> <br /> This is why we roll dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:03:01-07:00","id":204202,"title":"","content":"OK, so...if the objection not &quot;I don't get why Solars are the best at this particular thing.&quot; but just &quot;I hate that Solars are the best at nearly everything&quot;, I am going to have to direct you to almost any other game, and <i>especially</i> to any other game published by White Wolf. &quot;Solars on top&quot; is one of the core things that differentiates Exalted from other games; it was a radical and decisive reversal of everything else the company had ever published and ties into the core themes of the line as a whole. The other splats should be fun and powerful and have their own thing, but they should be <i>generally weaker than Solars</i>, because that is hugely important to the setting. The people who really press this complaint generally seem not to be upset about the quality of life as non-Solars so much as they just resent that the game explicitly makes one Exalted type better at all, and under the circumstances I'm not terribly sympathetic to that complaint, because it's asking the game to be something it's intentionally not.<br /> <br /> That said, suggesting that the other splat-specific subsystems don't count because they're poorly implemented is kind of a low blow. That's like saying that Solars being the best sorcerers doesn't count because sorcery is a crappy XP sink -- it's not a design goal, those subsystems just happened to be handled badly, and if heaven forbid they're handled badly <i>this</i> time it will <i>still</i> be a fluke. <i>Of course</i> they aren't going to design 10 pages of specialized splat-specific mechanics and then make them pointlessly awful just to drive home how much better Solars are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:03:34-07:00","id":204203,"title":"","content":"Well that's still wrong, since the literary and mythological basis for the folk hero is pretty consistent and fully portrayed by the Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:11:04-07:00","id":204208,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ok. I think we're really done here, because you're flat out ignoring arguments and inserting what you want to read at this point. And it's not a low blow when that's the garbage that's been put out. They've been MADE to be less then the solar tools. In and out of fluff, time and time again, it's been &quot;Here's this neat thing. However, it's weaker and not importnt because we can't introduce a problem that a solar can't fix&quot; AND THAT. IS SHITTY. GAME DESIGN.<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't defined by solars being on top. There as so many other things that make this game unique that if that's what you boil it down to, I'm just...I'm fucking agast. That's just. No. That is the core of my problem, why I so rarely bother to say anything, because that's...if that's ALL that makes this game unque, why should I CARE? At that point it's just one big gameline of sucking glorious golden dick. You just swept aside EVERTHING ELSE that is Exalted, everything that sets the game apart from others, all it's rich history, the interplay of things, for the simple sum-up of the gameline being Solar&gt; You. What the shit is WRONG with you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eric, thanks much, that was what I was trying to say. The damn spell-checker here is..not great. At all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 07-21-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:17:42-07:00","id":204220,"title":"","content":"Sorry, dude, but &quot;the Solars are back, and everything is different now because of how much of a game-changer they are&quot; has pretty much been the central premise of Exalted since day one.<br /> <br /> You're within your rights to not like it, I can respect that, but if you're going to claim that one of Exalted's primary focuses isn't the Solars, then you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:22:04-07:00","id":204221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204201#post204201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, because this is one of those things that bears repeating: Sometimes the less skilled competitor wins even if he or she has no other talents that can overcome the difference in skill. Superiority is not certainty. The odds of victory are rarely exactly 0% or 100%. The better fighter can lose without trickery; the weaker fighter can win without pulling out an ace in the hole.<br /> <br /> This is why we roll dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is commonly demonstrated in the very popular ELO rating system where a player rated 200 points higher is actually only expected to win 76% of the time. In a single bout it's actually pretty likely that the less skilled competitor will win. This is why competitions usually utilize a fairly high number of bouts to make that statistically unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:40:22-07:00","id":204257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204220#post204220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, dude, but &quot;the Solars are back, and everything is different now because of how much of a game-changer they are&quot; has pretty much been the central premise of Exalted since day one.<br /> <br /> You're within your rights to not like it, I can respect that, but if you're going to claim that one of Exalted's primary focuses isn't the Solars, then you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those have pretty consistently <i>not</i> been his points, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:11:22-07:00","id":204373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204208#post204208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted isn't defined by solars being on top. There as so many other things that make this game unique that if that's what you boil it down to, I'm just...I'm fucking agast. That's just. No. That is the core of my problem, why I so rarely bother to say anything, because that's...if that's ALL that makes this game unque, why should I CARE? At that point it's just one big gameline of sucking glorious golden dick. You just swept aside EVERTHING ELSE that is Exalted, everything that sets the game apart from others, all it's rich history, the interplay of things, for the simple sum-up of the gameline being Solar&amp;gt; You. What the shit is WRONG with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chill out, dude. I get mad at the forums too sometimes, but just...log off and punch a thing, and commiserate with your friends about how awful I am, or something. This isn't a knife fight.<br /> <br /> The Solars being on top is not specifically about the Solars, though obviously that's core to the game's setting structure. Rather, the Solars are the purest expression of the game's themes: overcoming adversity and achieving the impossible, humans defeating powerful monsters, mythic heroes, and so forth. These themes apply to all Exalted, but they appear in their purest and most unadulterated form in Solars, so making Solars the most powerful is making a thematic statement about human power overcoming esoteric power, the weak vanquishing the strong, achieving the impossible through your spirit, etc. Lunars are less powerful than Solars because their power is channelled through monstrous aspects, and that reduces the degree to which they can express the core themes. This is a calculated reversal of many other games and oWoD in particular, where the more esoteric and sinister-seeming your power source is, the stronger you are.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Solars are the most powerful does not mean that everybody else falls over themselves prostrating themselves to the Solars, or that the game exists entirely to show how awesome the Solars are, or anything like that. If you're playing a different type of Exalted, the return of the Solars provides a <i>context</i> for you to establish your own awesomeness, and not only does that not require that your splat be as powerful as Solars, in many cases it works better if they aren't. The return of the Solars is meant to be a challenge and a question to the established splats, but it is <i>not</i> meant to be a challenge they will surely lose, or a question they will answer with &quot;let me hold your coat&quot;. But the dynamic established there just <i>does not work</i> if the other Celestials are on completely even footing. Making Lunars and Sidereals totally on par with Solars, in particular, would be tremendously damaging to both of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-21-2014, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T18:05:01-07:00","id":204489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204208#post204208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, ok. I think we're really done here, because you're flat out ignoring arguments and inserting what you want to read at this point. And it's not a low blow when that's the garbage that's been put out. They've been MADE to be less then the solar tools. In and out of fluff, time and time again, it's been &quot;Here's this neat thing. However, it's weaker and not importnt because we can't introduce a problem that a solar can't fix&quot; AND THAT. IS SHITTY. GAME DESIGN.<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't defined by solars being on top. There as so many other things that make this game unique that if that's what you boil it down to, I'm just...I'm fucking agast. That's just. No. That is the core of my problem, why I so rarely bother to say anything, because that's...if that's ALL that makes this game unque, why should I CARE? At that point it's just one big gameline of sucking glorious golden dick. You just swept aside EVERTHING ELSE that is Exalted, everything that sets the game apart from others, all it's rich history, the interplay of things, for the simple sum-up of the gameline being Solar&gt; You. What the shit is WRONG with you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eric, thanks much, that was what I was trying to say. The damn spell-checker here is..not great. At all.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a spell checker? Recently every time when I try to right click something to correct the spelling I get this strange menu with cut, copy, paste add table pops up and not the spelling corrections.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T18:09:42-07:00","id":204493,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that Solars get nothing outside their charms. Lunar shape shifting is a crazy useful ability that all lunars everywhere always get. You can eat a rat, sneak into a palace via the sewer, chomp down on an unsuspecting palace cat/dog/iguana whatever, and now you have free reign of the palace. Go snuggle up with the emperor in bed, then become a bear, bite his face off and then become a common local bird and flit off. None of that costed any XP, had any ability prereqs and unlike most &quot;but a solar/infernal whatever can just do this!&quot; any chosen lunar could do that. Sadly astrology sucks and I can't think of a DB version, but you get the idea. You need to get to the bottom of a lake to recover an artifact, the solar says &quot;ah-ha! I'm six charms deep into resistance and can hold my reach for five hours!&quot; Your lunar rolls his eyes and says &quot;that's great, good for you golden boy.&quot; Before turning into a fish or whale or whatever.<br /> <br /> Solars are better with all their charms because, barring first age douche artifacts, you're never special just for being a solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T18:29:27-07:00","id":204506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204493#post204493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that Solars get nothing outside their charms. Lunar shape shifting is a crazy useful ability that all lunars everywhere always get. You can eat a rat, sneak into a palace via the sewer, chomp down on an unsuspecting palace cat/dog/iguana whatever, and now you have free reign of the palace. Go snuggle up with the emperor in bed, then become a bear, bite his face off and then become a common local bird and flit off. None of that costed any XP, had any ability prereqs and unlike most &quot;but a solar/infernal whatever can just do this!&quot; any chosen lunar could do that. Sadly astrology sucks and I can't think of a DB version, but you get the idea. You need to get to the bottom of a lake to recover an artifact, the solar says &quot;ah-ha! I'm six charms deep into resistance and can hold my reach for five hours!&quot; Your lunar rolls his eyes and says &quot;that's great, good for you golden boy.&quot; Before turning into a fish or whale or whatever.<br /> <br /> Solars are better with all their charms because, barring first age douche artifacts, you're never special just for being a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I might add the DB thing you were thinking of.<br /> Each caste of the Dragonblood are attuned to an element. Fire can walk through a fire without problems, and hell in one book one demonstrated immunity to lava because of her anima banner. Water aspects can breath and be fully functional underwater even if said action shouldn't work. Wood are immune to poison so long as it's plant based. I forget the air and earth aspect abilities. All Dragonblood beyond that are able to bind together and become a greater force then they could be individually. Solar's aren't garuanteed to work too well together Dragonbloods can all basically do that.<br /> <br /> Frankly I like the alchemical's ability to slot out charms as part of their limbs. What can I say I love the idea of a character keeping a flame piece in their hand just in case it's needed and to use their archery charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T18:47:21-07:00","id":204519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204493#post204493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that Solars get nothing outside their charms. Lunar shape shifting is a crazy useful ability that all lunars everywhere always get. You can eat a rat, sneak into a palace via the sewer, chomp down on an unsuspecting palace cat/dog/iguana whatever, and now you have free reign of the palace. Go snuggle up with the emperor in bed, then become a bear, bite his face off and then become a common local bird and flit off. None of that costed any XP, had any ability prereqs and unlike most &quot;but a solar/infernal whatever can just do this!&quot; any chosen lunar could do that. Sadly astrology sucks and I can't think of a DB version, but you get the idea. You need to get to the bottom of a lake to recover an artifact, the solar says &quot;ah-ha! I'm six charms deep into resistance and can hold my reach for five hours!&quot; Your lunar rolls his eyes and says &quot;that's great, good for you golden boy.&quot; Before turning into a fish or whale or whatever.<br /> <br /> Solars are better with all their charms because, barring first age douche artifacts, you're never special just for being a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon bloods are very good at team work. Leader charms and the like let them effect their whole unit plus many of their charms are geared tward helping other characters or giving dice bonuses to others. The other thing they were very good at was reflexive charms. They had a rule on their reflexives that let them ignore the need for combos. That probably is gone but I bet they will still be the reflexive kings with more reflexive powers and maybe more use of the elemental keyword than before causing them to have more cool, flashy powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T01:22:12-07:00","id":204785,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204373#post204373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solars being on top is not specifically about the Solars, though obviously that's core to the game's setting structure. Rather, the Solars are the purest expression of the game's themes: overcoming adversity and achieving the impossible, humans defeating powerful monsters, mythic heroes, and so forth. These themes apply to all Exalted, but they appear in their purest and most unadulterated form in Solars, so making Solars the most powerful is making a thematic statement about human power overcoming esoteric power, the weak vanquishing the strong, achieving the impossible through your spirit, etc. Lunars are less powerful than Solars because their power is channelled through monstrous aspects, and that reduces the degree to which they can express the core themes. This is a calculated reversal of many other games and oWoD in particular, where the more esoteric and sinister-seeming your power source is, the stronger you are.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">On this, this is all far from unreasonable, but I would like to say, when a Solar beats a Sidereal or Lunar, I never have really seen that as more some kind of laudable triumph for the human spirit over magical forces any more than when a Solar who uses a sword beats a Solar who uses Sorcery (and sorcerors being intended to arguably the strongest amongst Solars anyway) or in the new game, a Solar who uses blatantly magical evocations. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Such Solars are defeating a human who has triumphed over and mastered magical forces and their self through painstaking talent, effort and work (using human aptitudes of sorts the Solars don't necessarily have), not humans who are tools of supernatural forces, or who're becoming inhuman somehow, or who've luckily landed on supernatural power through random unfairness.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">When Solars triumph over demons and Fair Folk, yes fine, myth hero overcoming the supernatural, if you like. Not Sidereals or Lunars, or really any other sort of Exalted, except maybe those whose story is about becoming inhuman, like Abyssals and Infernals, but even then, that's a fact of their political position, not nature.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">I think its bad news for the game if Sidereals and Lunars start to become to be seen as tools of supernatural forces to be defeated or monsters to be triumphed over, rather than as people who've mastered particular magical skills and abilities that just aren't in the Solars' genre. I can't see any reason for it other than to try to justify Solars in a way which is unnecessary and misleading anyway</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T03:49:49-07:00","id":204854,"title":"","content":"Also, we should note that the writers have stated that 3E solars, while still powerful are NOT as far beyond the other exalted as they were in earlier books. So there's that. On the other hand, if a Solar isn't more powerful than any other splat for a given XP level you run into a problem called &quot;the entire premise of the game falls flat&quot; Supposedly, the realm and Sidereals are both terrified of the danger of letting solars gt their feet under them so they make damned certain to kill them before they get that power for the reason that the solars can outstrip the other exalted if given time to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T04:09:15-07:00","id":204860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204854#post204854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, we should note that the writers have stated that 3E solars, while still powerful are NOT as far beyond the other exalted as they were in earlier books. So there's that. On the other hand, if a Solar isn't more powerful than any other splat for a given XP level you run into a problem called &amp;quot;the entire premise of the game falls flat&amp;quot; Supposedly, the realm and Sidereals are both terrified of the danger of letting solars gt their feet under them so they make damned certain to kill them before they get that power for the reason that the solars can outstrip the other exalted if given time to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also I think they stated that solar empires have risen in the past, and even after getting up and running eventually lost a war to the Realm/sidereals/Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T06:04:26-07:00","id":204890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204785#post204785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> When Solars triumph over demons and Fair Folk, yes fine, myth hero overcoming the supernatural, if you like. Not Sidereals or Lunars, or really any other sort of Exalted, except maybe those whose story is about becoming inhuman, like Abyssals and Infernals, but even then, that's a fact of their political position, not nature.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">I think its bad news for the game if Sidereals and Lunars start to become to be seen as tools of supernatural forces to be defeated or monsters to be triumphed over, rather than as people who've mastered particular magical skills and abilities that just aren't in the Solars' genre. I can't see any reason for it other than to try to justify Solars in a way which is unnecessary and misleading anyway</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is more that the Sidereals and Lunar's powers by their nature distance them from being human. The more powerful a Lunar gets the more obvious it is they are something Protean, Primal, Savage. The sid becomes more and more distant, detached, and a Plutocrat. They become so wrapped up in their convention and area that they start to seem like the gods. Always worried about their reports and domains rather than the people who might come to harm. They are not becoming monsters just their power and it's nature distances them from the very things that make a person human.<br /> <br /> Solars on the other hand (and to some extent Dragon Blooded) draw from humanistic elements. Their nature makes them draw closer to the emotions, thoughts, and mind of being human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T06:33:55-07:00","id":204901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204854#post204854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, we should note that the writers have stated that 3E solars, while still powerful are NOT as far beyond the other exalted as they were in earlier books. So there's that. On the other hand, if a Solar isn't more powerful than any other splat for a given XP level you run into a problem called &quot;the entire premise of the game falls flat&quot; Supposedly, the realm and Sidereals are both terrified of the danger of letting solars gt their feet under them so they make damned certain to kill them before they get that power for the reason that the solars can outstrip the other exalted if given time to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars will probably still be more powerful, generally, in terms of magic of broad competence and scope (Charms vs shapeshifting/astrology, each of which should be more powerful or at least more useful in its niche). <br /> <br /> But my impression is they're lowering the ceiling of power from the creep that 2e implemented even in the core, where you have single, low-tree Charms that negate entire challenges outright (IPP, perfect &quot;I know if you're lying&quot; Charms, spammable social and combat perfects, etc) or that play themselves without you doing any work (TID etc). Those will probably be massively overhauled to provide advantages without outright negating all challenges tied to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T06:41:34-07:00","id":204904,"title":"","content":"I wonder if in the future when I suggest that non-Solar can access the highest circle of Evocation, would I get the same kind of pleasant acid bath when I suggest that other non-Solar can access the highest circle of Sorcery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T07:10:30-07:00","id":204915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204904#post204904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if in the future when I suggest that non-Solar can access the highest circle of Evocation, would I get the same kind of pleasant acid bath when I suggest that other non-Solar can access the highest circle of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before you get dunked in the acid bath, I'd like to ask, why would a non-solar have access to the highest circle of Evocation?<br /> -Starts preparing the bath.- You rather have Sulfuric or Hydrochloric Acid?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T07:33:31-07:00","id":204937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204915#post204915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before you get dunked in the acid bath, I'd like to ask, why would a non-solar have access to the highest circle of Evocation?<br /> -Starts preparing the bath.- You rather have Sulfuric or Hydrochloric Acid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was refer to the &quot;If you are unhappy, just houserule it so that DB/Lunar/Sidereal can access the highest circle of Evocation like Solar&quot; advice. Since I have never seen any non-Solar PC with access to SCS, the chance of a GM allowing non-Solar to learn Sapphire Circle Evocation is pretty much non-existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T07:36:52-07:00","id":204938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204937#post204937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I was refer to the &quot;If you are unhappy, just houserule it so that DB/Lunar/Sidereal can access the highest circle of Evocation like Solar&quot; advice. Since I have never seen any non-Solar PC with access to SCS, the chance of a GM allowing non-Solar to learn Sapphire Circle Evocation is pretty much non-existance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh like that, yeah, I don't see a reason to bathe you in acid then. Let people play the games they want to play, if everyone in in their group is fine with playing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T07:48:50-07:00","id":204939,"title":"","content":"People can give all the splats evocations for all I care, so long as they don't come here and complain that it wrecks the game balance. You opened the box, you voided the warranty, you deal with the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T07:50:43-07:00","id":204940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204937#post204937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I was refer to the &quot;If you are unhappy, just houserule it so that DB/Lunar/Sidereal can access the highest circle of Evocation like Solar&quot; advice. Since I have never seen any non-Solar PC with access to SCS, the chance of a GM allowing non-Solar to learn Sapphire Circle Evocation is pretty much non-existance.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in 2e, there's means of non-Solars learning Solar Circle Sorcery - for instance, becoming an akuma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/