_ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204951#post204951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen a <i>Solar </i>PC with SCS.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone want it, anyway? All the cool spells are Terrestrial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them are awesome, cleansing a shadowland or the third eyeless face charm, all so good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:06:15-07:00","id":204957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204951#post204951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen a <i>Solar </i>PC with SCS.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone want it, anyway? All the cool spells are Terrestrial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you don't want to have tea with Ligier ;D<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:08:17-07:00","id":204959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204915#post204915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before you get dunked in the acid bath, I'd like to ask, why would a non-solar have access to the highest circle of Evocation?</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is a reason for them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:27:42-07:00","id":204974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204904#post204904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if in the future when I suggest that non-Solar can access the highest circle of Evocation, would I get the same kind of pleasant acid bath when I suggest that other non-Solar can access the highest circle of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguing that non-Solars <i>shouldn't</i> get access to Adamant circle Evocations is premature at this point. It's not to say they necessarily will, but we really just don't know enough yet to say definitively. We know Solars are the greatest with Evocations. It doesn't automatically follow that a member of another splat is axiomatically unable to equal their use of Evocations with particular circumstances or artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:33:16-07:00","id":204977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204785#post204785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this, this is all far from unreasonable, but I would like to say, when a Solar beats a Sidereal or Lunar, I never have really seen that as more some kind of laudable triumph for the human spirit over magical forces any more than when a Solar who uses a sword beats a Solar who uses Sorcery (and sorcerors being intended to arguably the strongest amongst Solars anyway) or in the new game, a Solar who uses blatantly magical evocations.<br /> <br /> Such Solars are defeating a human who has triumphed over and mastered magical forces and their self through painstaking talent, effort and work (using human aptitudes of sorts the Solars don't necessarily have), not humans who are tools of supernatural forces, or who'rebecoming inhuman somehow, or who've luckily landed on supernatural power through random unfairness.<br /> <br /> When Solars triumph over demons and Fair Folk, yes fine, myth hero overcoming the supernatural, if you like. Not Sidereals or Lunars, or really any other sort of Exalted, except maybe those whose story is about becoming inhuman, like Abyssals and Infernals, but even then, that's a fact of their political position, not nature.<br /> <br /> I think its bad news for the game if Sidereals and Lunars start to become to be seen as tools of supernatural forces to be defeated or monsters to be triumphed over, rather than as people who've mastered particular magical skills and abilities that just aren't in the Solars' genre. I can't see any reason for it other than to try to justify Solars in a way which is unnecessary and misleading anyway]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it's more of a subtextual thematic. The game doesn't actually say &quot;the Solars are the strongest because they are the <i>most Exalted</i> and everyone else's power is compromised by alien aspects&quot;, because the setting doesn't work that way and probably shouldn't -- it isn't <i>supposed</i> to inform the experience of playing a Lunar or Sidereal to that degree, and stating it outright would, as you say, warp people''s understanding of the Exalted. It's a thematic and aesthetic undertone. You aren't <i>supposed</i> to think of Sidereals and Lunars and what not as alien monsters who exist to be defeated by humanity -- they're still Exalted, after all. But this is the reasoning that I think underlies the <i>design decision</i> to make Solars the most powerful, and regardless of how visible it's meant to be to players, this thread of discussion drags that stuff out into the open. This is the same underlying design process that made Sidereals the Secret Masters of Everything, the Lunars the Punk Rock Monster-People from the World's End, etc, which are both equally compelling concept-spaces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204854#post204854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, we should note that the writers have stated that 3E solars, while still powerful are NOT as far beyond the other exalted as they were in earlier books. So there's that. On the other hand, if a Solar isn't more powerful than any other splat for a given XP level you run into a problem called &quot;the entire premise of the game falls flat&quot; Supposedly, the realm and Sidereals are both terrified of the danger of letting solars gt their feet under them so they make damned certain to kill them before they get that power for the reason that the solars can outstrip the other exalted if given time to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I surmise from the writer quotes is that the goal is to put Solars, Sidereals and Lunars on roughly even footing out of the gate, with a few nominal concessions to Solars, like &quot;here, have an extra Charm and Favored ability&quot;. I wouldn't even be surprised to see Sidereals a little stronger at chargen, though there's been nothing said to that effect. Then Solars pull ahead a little bit at a time, and end up significantly more powerful at the end (by which time the others have had the opportunity to fully build on their own gimmicks in a mixed game, but most games are likely to end by Ess 3 anyway). I mean, there's no knowing what we'll actually get, but that seems to be the plan. Of course, from an in-setting (rather than in-party) perspective, the Solars are going to be dramatically weaker at the start, since they're virtually all freshly Exalted.<br /> <br /> The general structure of the Time of Tumult for established non-Solars with long memories is that the Solars are nuclear weapons, and the tension is in &quot;man, what do I do with all these Solars?&quot; because you know that they are vulnerable to manipulation and attack, but will eventually ripen into unimaginable power, and you have to decide how you want to deal with that. Do you ally with their enemies to put them down? Do you try to kill any who fuck with you, while otherwise leaving well enough alone? Do you wind them up, point them at something you want gone, and then stay out of it? Do you try to make friends and sell them on your own agenda, aware that you have to be careful because one day they may be too powerful for you to control?<br /> <br /> Making the Solars' overwhelming superiority something that they have to grow into plays to these themes while preserving the integrity of mixed-party games, and you can always make Solars &quot;feel&quot; stronger out of the gate with inconsequential changes like making their charms cost 1 xp less, giving them an extra favored pick, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-22-2014, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:38:01-07:00","id":204984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204951#post204951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen a <i>Solar </i>PC with SCS.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably because 2e games start at E2 and die before you can get E5. I've only seen SCS when the PCs all started with a lot of XP/higher Essence. I've never seen it gotten in-game, just in character-building when everyone started at E5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204937#post204937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I was refer to the &quot;If you are unhappy, just houserule it so that DB/Lunar/Sidereal can access the highest circle of Evocation like Solar&quot; advice. Since I have never seen any non-Solar PC with access to SCS, the chance of a GM allowing non-Solar to learn Sapphire Circle Evocation is pretty much non-existance.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know enough about Evocations yet to think DBs will only ever get Emerald Evocations because they only get TCS. In fact, author statements lead me to believe DBs will be the second-best at Evocations, above everyone but Solars. So basically don't assume the power or access tiers for Evocations will be the same as those for Sorcery. Personally I bet they won't, because that would just be boring and expected and would come across as overly formulaic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:39:01-07:00","id":204987,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've got a minimum of ten or so distinct types that everyone is going to have varying affinities for and solars are somehow going to be able to use them all whilst also being especially good with orichalcum presumably so it's almost certainly not going to be something as simple as a three tier system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:54:31-07:00","id":205001,"title":"","content":"from what i understand Exigents is the answer, there is absolutely no reason why some exigent cant learn Solar sorcery or be as proficient with evocations as a solar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:56:36-07:00","id":205003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204951#post204951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen a <i>Solar </i>PC with SCS.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone want it, anyway? All the cool spells are Terrestrial.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can answer this question actually. My character concept was one where my second age incarnation was actually hunted by his first age incarnation. He left traps and snares and hints around that would lead me to events that would shape me to be like him, leaving memory crystals and vast armories to give me his memories, and prepare me for a war of revenge with the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> I used the sacrifice stages to purge myself of him, such as releasing my familiar at Terrestrial (freeing it from many of the mind-warping charms it was under to influence me), breaking my weapons (which were a key to unlocking vast armories hidden in the Wyld, waiting for me to reach them, with their soldier-servant mind-altered inhabitants. For my Solar Circle, I gave up all memories of the First Age that were a part of my incarnation. I had to use an NA artifact, a Wyld zone, and a sidereal who had become half Fair folk to do it, and it left me with a serious long-term problem of progressive amnesia, where I could remember thelast few years, but that's it, and as time went by, I lost those memories as well. Was pretty bad at the point where I met one of my sons and didn't remember his mother, despite her being the love of my life.<br /> <br /> Still, that's what I use Solar Circle Sorcery for. It completes the transformation of a character. It's a mechanism for storytelling, not really a power grab.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:03:58-07:00","id":205015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204987#post204987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we've got a minimum of ten or so distinct types that everyone is going to have varying affinities for and solars are somehow going to be able to use them all whilst also being especially good with orichalcum presumably so it's almost certainly not going to be something as simple as a three tier system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about that, the tree we saw had three tiers of evocations on it. I'm also pretty sure that DBs being the second best at evocations doesn't mean access to higher circles. It would be really strange to have some evocation that can destroy a building and normally a celestial tier charm at least be accessible to terrestrials.<br /> <br /> It could imply that each type of jade has it's own sort of evocations and since DBs resonate with all of them then they kind of get five when every other non-solar gets one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:12:02-07:00","id":205032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204987#post204987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we've got a minimum of ten or so distinct types that everyone is going to have varying affinities for and solars are somehow going to be able to use them all whilst also being especially good with orichalcum presumably so it's almost certainly not going to be something as simple as a three tier system.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204987#post204987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we've got a minimum of ten or so distinct types that everyone is going to have varying affinities for and solars are somehow going to be able to use them all whilst also being especially good with orichalcum presumably so it's almost certainly not going to be something as simple as a three tier system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, its going to be more complex than this, in any case. Or at least I hope so. Everything I say here is SPECULATIVE at best. I see it as: everyone who has an associated material gets access to that material. Solars get top access to the six magical materials (Orichalcum, Moonsilver, Starmetal, Soulsteel, Jade, and Adamant). Most people get access to the second tier of materials other than their own, or only first tier if it 'opposes.' I don't know what that means, or if they will do something, but I wouldn't mind seeing Moonsilver oppose Jade, and Soulsteel oppose Starmetal, and Adamant oppose Orichalcum.<br /> <br /> I also want to see workarounds, and not some lame-ass five-fold universal adaptor. You want access to the top tier of a weapon type you normally don't get?<br /> Go talk to the Infernals. Get them to make you a replica out of hell-tainted brass that burns with green fire instead of gold.<br /> Go talk to the Yozis and sign up for one of those Akuma contracts.<br /> Go talk to the Fair Folk about forging you a replica, or shaping you into something that can use it. Better get that checkbook out! It's gonna cost.<br /> If you are a Lunar, go hunt down and eat a Solar, a la the Golden Widow society. Or Terrestrial, or Sidereal, or whatever. I really hope you don't pick soulsteel, because unless you have some Stamina charms, that's going to give you some bad rumbly-tumbly-tummy.<br /> If you are a Martial Artist, go master your essence to the point where you can mimic another splat's essence through a form-type kata.<br /> Go make a deal with the Alchemicals where they carve open your chest and put a big gold ring around your heart like Tony Stark. Oh, and don't forget the Clarity while you are there.<br /> <br /> Talk to your ST about it. And remember, you aren't playing Exalted right if you aren't breaking the rules! That's why I love it when the authors say 'Here's something you cannot do. Absolutely not, under any circumstances, can you have this cookie. That just means I have to write a damn good story about why I get this and you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","user":"Ejtaka","date":".  Just clarifying that 'I get it and you don't' to mean my character gets this evocation and NPCs don't. Not an attack on the users of this forum that they don't understand how to write a narrative. 07-22-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:17:02-07:00","id":205035,"title":"","content":"I could easily see the dragonblooded pulling some sort of All Your Colours Combined thing where they can access one or two tiers normally and get one higher by five of them working together. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:18:21-07:00","id":205036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205003#post205003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, that's what I use Solar Circle Sorcery for. It completes the transformation of a character. It's a mechanism for storytelling, not really a power grab.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1. IMHO, being a Solar Circle Sorcerer is one of those things that is terribly character-defining. I would imagine there are an odd assortment of Exalted who know Sorcery and a few spells, but legitimately don't consider themselves Sorcerers. You might--MIGHT--run into a few of those people at the Celestial Tier, but I doubt it.<br /> <br /> Most PC's either don't reach the tiers of power needed to access it or don't perceive it as integral enough for their character to really pursue it.<br /> <br /> No PCs in any of my games have. <br /> <br /> That said, one NPC did reach it. I almost mentioned her in the Whimsy topic: her sacrifices had amounted to her emotional capacity for anger, sorrow, and fear (a custom-bred slave from Cynis, she had plenty of call for all of these). The result was a sociopathic waif who had been the one to kill the Mask of Winters--spearing him through to Juggernaut with a casting of the Benediction of Archgenesis--and then nuked the recovering city-state of Thorns off the map months in a Lethean mushroom cloud produced by a geomantic experiment, with no more concern than, &quot;Oooo, so THAT's what happens when you do that!&quot;<br /> <br /> Another NPC didn't. But me and the player of her &quot;twin&quot; agreed that using Freedom Lets Go to delete all emotional rapport and memories of your life--and then deliberately leaving evidence to convince yourself that you were someone else entirely--so that your copies could go on living (...it's complicated) was well worth the Adamant Circle. But since she was sticking around with the PC's for a while, giving her access to an echelon of spellcasting well above what anyone else had was kind of undesirable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:19:58-07:00","id":205038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205035#post205035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily see the dragonblooded pulling some sort of All Your Colours Combined thing where they can access one or two tiers normally and get one higher by five of them working together.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly! Speaking as an ST, tell me why you should get to do this. Don't just tell me you want it, and that its unfair that it isn't handed to you on a (moon)silver platter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:26:18-07:00","id":205039,"title":"","content":"I thought that cooperative-type stuff was going away for DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:33:09-07:00","id":205048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205039#post205039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that cooperative-type stuff was going away for DBs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope the themes don't, even if the charms as written do. I would love to see some stuff like that come back, but integrated with the new combat system. The problem before was that it was much, much more effective to coordinate your attacks and attack individually than it was to team up into one super powerful Lore bolt. With the change in the combat system, my understanding is no flurries and no true Perfect Defenses, so maybe teaming up to conjoin powers will be really effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:50:16-07:00","id":205077,"title":"","content":"Oh, I get you and agree. I mean, after all, the DBs fight best as a coordinated group, rather than as powerful individuals.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the new system will have perfects in a recognizable but not spammable form, but whether DBs get anything like it or whether that will remain a purview of Celestials...who knows yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T10:34:27-07:00","id":205126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205048#post205048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hope the themes don't, even if the charms as written do. I would love to see some stuff like that come back, but integrated with the new combat system. The problem before was that it was much, much more effective to coordinate your attacks and attack individually than it was to team up into one super powerful Lore bolt. With the change in the combat system, my understanding is no flurries and no true Perfect Defenses, so maybe teaming up to conjoin powers will be really effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be even simpler than that. In the old system, if your opponent had a scenting DV penalty negator, teaming up didn't really do anything. Maybe now teaming up does a lot more and DBs just end up teaming up more often because there's more of them? I'd like to see some of that same kind of cooperation within a solar circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:04:42-07:00","id":205142,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't want to see Solars get new effects that improve them when working together/cooperating. First, because Solars just don't need any more help :P . Second, cooperation has long been a fundamental DB theme, especially in the mindsets of &quot;we are greater than the sum of our parts&quot; and &quot;united we stand.&quot; Third, I view Solars as solo dynamic powerhouses whose interests sometimes align in the same direction, who lead groups rather than participate jointly, compared to DBs (who are all &quot;brothers and sisters in the blood,&quot; even if extremely removed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:08:06-07:00","id":205144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204373#post204373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Solars are the most powerful does not mean that everybody else falls over themselves prostrating themselves to the Solars, or that the game exists entirely to show how awesome the Solars are, or anything like that...The return of the Solars is meant to be a challenge and a question to the established splats, but it is <i>not</i> meant to be a challenge they will surely lose, or a question they will answer with &quot;let me hold your coat&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've come to the conclusion that a large part of the vitriol I direct at Solars is because I believe that, for the last two editions at least, this statement simply isn't true. And there's that part of me that keeps asking &quot;Well, if they cocked it up the <i>last</i> two editions...&quot;<br /> <br /> Because, really, I'd prefer to <i>not</i> be known as &quot;one of the guys who spends all his time bitching about Solars.&quot; I'd rather not be in a position where I feel I have to hold the line against Solars engulfing the entire damn game.<br /> <br /> Because, ya'know, it's very important to the success of 3e that I personally be impressed and satisfied with it. <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"> Not really, I know.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:42:07-07:00","id":205176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205015#post205015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure about that, the tree we saw had three tiers of evocations on it. I'm also pretty sure that DBs being the second best at evocations doesn't mean access to higher circles. It would be really strange to have some evocation that can destroy a building and normally a celestial tier charm at least be accessible to terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear this, and I think about how the devs have said that thinking strictly in terms of tiers as in 2e is going to trip people up. I suspect this is one of those places. It's been said that Dragonblooded have &quot;a special dispensation&quot; with Evocations, which sounds to my ears like there's more to it than just &quot;there are 5 types of jade.&quot; As for Dragonblooded getting effects that punch above their traditional weight class? If they do with Evocations, this wouldn't be the only place for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Circle Sorcery contains E6+ effects. Likewise, Terrestrial and Celestial circles contain spells that are out of the scope of their Essence brackets. Sorcery intentionally gives you access to powers that are beyond your Essence score.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the consideration that this isn't a strictly binary &quot;Yes, all Terrestrials can/No, no Terrestrials can&quot; situation. That &quot;special dispensation&quot; wording makes me think about what they're doing with Martial Arts, much as they aren't necessarily going the same way. Terrestrials by default aren't as good at Martial Arts Charms, but can become just as good as Celestial Exalted with special effort:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The styles are calculated to ride at a power level that's suitable for a wide array of practitioners. Dragon-Blooded and Solars mostly just use the same Martial Arts Charms, though some Charms work a bit differently for DBs-- they get less out of them than others do. Dragon-Blooded who have undergone specific, rigorous training regimens (such as Immaculate monks) get to ignore those distinctions.<br /> <br /> This does mean that you can play a Dragon-Blooded and use Snake style, or a Solar and use Jade Mountain, and that will be a good decision for you either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T12:06:18-07:00","id":205205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204890#post204890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is more that the Sidereals and Lunar's powers by their nature distance them from being human. The more powerful a Lunar gets the more obvious it is they are something Protean, Primal, Savage. The sid becomes more and more distant, detached, and a Plutocrat. They become so wrapped up in their convention and area that they start to seem like the gods. Always worried about their reports and domains rather than the people who might come to harm. They are not becoming monsters just their power and it's nature distances them from the very things that make a person human.<br /> <br /> Solars on the other hand (and to some extent Dragon Blooded) draw from humanistic elements. Their nature makes them draw closer to the emotions, thoughts, and mind of being human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be. But I know loads of people have never found the argument that Solars become inevitably alienated by the scope of their power and distance unconvincing, so I don't find it that appealing transplanted to another Exalt type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204939#post204939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People can give all the splats evocations for all I care, so long as they don't come here and complain that it wrecks the game balance. You opened the box, you voided the warranty, you deal with the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or we could help people with play balance in their custom settings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204977#post204977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general structure of the Time of Tumult for established non-Solars with long memories is that the Solars are nuclear weapons, and the tension is in &quot;man, what do I do with all these Solars?&quot; because you know that they are vulnerable to manipulation and attack, but will eventually ripen into unimaginable power, and you have to decide how you want to deal with that. Do you ally with their enemies to put them down? Do you try to kill any who fuck with you, while otherwise leaving well enough alone? Do you wind them up, point them at something you want gone, and then stay out of it? Do you try to make friends and sell them on your own agenda, aware that you have to be careful because one day they may be too powerful for you to control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the balance could come out like that in the High Essence / Elder game. I'm not sure how much 3e is going to go in for power racheting elders. Not sure what the consensus is on the writer statements or if that's too much like Kremlinology at the moment anyway.<br /> <br /> (That theme of dealing unimaginably powerful individuals who can shape reality to their will versus the safety of consensus reality and laws of reality I think was done better in Mage*. The whole game was built around it there, while Exalted kind of isn't.<br /> <br /> IMO Mage is where Exalted : The Sidereals got that theme, as a more explicit nod back to Mage, shifting the focus to Sidereals worrying about Solar power as this nuclear scale that could break reality (very Mage-y), rather than them being very numerous, more powerful than other Celestials and mad enough that they could physically devastate the world by war and damn the world to Fair Folk invasion, as the sense of it was in the First Edition Core.<br /> <br /> Reading through the First Edition, I do think you get this sense that they are people whose absence would break a civilization without them being these magical engines of vast power that is a danger to reality... I think).<br /> <br /> I'd be fine with Solars being more powerful than the other Celestials but not really taking any major power leap upwards at any point, except for Solar Circle Sorcery which is pretty established.<br /> <br /> But I mean like, either way, a lot of this charting of high power is something its easy to probably get too obsessed with anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T12:22:06-07:00","id":205217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205142#post205142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't want to see Solars get new effects that improve them when working together/cooperating. First, because Solars just don't need any more help :P . Second, cooperation has long been a fundamental DB theme, especially in the mindsets of &quot;we are greater than the sum of our parts&quot; and &quot;united we stand.&quot; Third, I view Solars as solo dynamic powerhouses whose interests sometimes align in the same direction, who lead groups rather than participate jointly, compared to DBs (who are all &quot;brothers and sisters in the blood,&quot; even if extremely removed).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think anyone is suggesting giving DB themes to Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T12:32:28-07:00","id":205226,"title":"","content":"I think what many Sidereals want is Carousel from Logan's Run. Solar is getting ready for Essence 6, but by law he needs to pass a secret spiritual test, which endangers his life. There are legends of many who passed, including the heroes of the Primordial War. Since then, several Sidereals have passed, and a few Dragon-Blooded, but the core component is humility in the face of enlightenment, so Solars and Lunars usually don't. Maybe a few Lunars have, but every Solar commits ritual suicide during the test if they fail. Of their own free will. Every time. The Sidereals wouldn't lie about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T12:36:35-07:00","id":205233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205015#post205015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure about that, the tree we saw had three tiers of evocations on it. I'm also pretty sure that DBs being the second best at evocations doesn't mean access to higher circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but 3 tiers of Evocations doesn't necessarily mean &quot;access follows the three tiers of Sorcery.&quot; DBs being better at Evocations than Sidereals messes with that idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205015#post205015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would be really strange to have some evocation that can destroy a building and normally a celestial tier charm at least be accessible to terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would be strange at all. I think it would be rather appropriate - through their weapons and armor, DBs transcend their normal limits. On top of it, different Artifacts are going to have different Evocations - it's not like Sorcery, where a given spell has to be balanced against the inherent powers and native Charms of every Exalt type who has access to that Sorcery level.<br /> <br /> Also I'll point out that &quot;Celestial tier Charm&quot; doesn't have any meaning right now and even in the future there's been mentions that while DBs will still be individually the weakest, some DB Charms may be more powerful than Celestial or Solar Charms, just depending. I much prefer that to the rigidly-static power tiers of 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205217#post205217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone is suggesting giving DB themes to Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'm not sure what was desired from Solars being able to collaborate to the same/similar effectiveness as DBs can/should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T14:45:51-07:00","id":205352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205144#post205144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, really, I'd prefer to <i>not</i> be known as &quot;one of the guys who spends all his time bitching about Solars.&quot; I'd rather not be in a position where I feel I have to hold the line against Solars engulfing the entire damn game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, good luck protecting the game from its main characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T15:17:44-07:00","id":205395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205233#post205233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I'm not sure what was desired from Solars being able to collaborate to the same/similar effectiveness as DBs can/should.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant that teamwork in general, like in more than just the coordinated attack action part of the system, should be possible. Then DBs might not get co-operative charms by default, but they'd be theoretically more inclined to work together because a brotherhood of terrestrials is way way more common than a circle of Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T15:52:22-07:00","id":205414,"title":"","content":"Well is the default playstyle a circle of Solars or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:03:21-07:00","id":205421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205414#post205414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well is the default playstyle a circle of Solars or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? But in my experience most players forgo teamwork in exchange for making their characters personally awesome, particularly with Solars because that's kind of their thing. DBs on the other hand often need to band together to get stuff done so you might suffer and die for your pride, or agree to work together and live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:17:56-07:00","id":205426,"title":"","content":"If you don't want solars taking over the whole game then don't fucking use them. There's only 150 of the things running around, so the concept of a bunch of non-solars going the whole game without running into any is entirely plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:52:05-07:00","id":205495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205144#post205144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've come to the conclusion that a large part of the vitriol I direct at Solars is because I believe that, for the last two editions at least, this statement simply isn't true. And there's that part of me that keeps asking &quot;Well, if they cocked it up the <i>last</i> two editions...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what, at this point I honestly couldn't say how often the line stuck to my interpretation and how often it didn't! White Wolf game books have always had this issue where they're full of contradictions, reversals and tonal shifts because they're written by 40 different people and each line contains thousands of pages of material, so when talking about the material with other people it always ends up being kind of <i>Rashomon</i>. I can definitely think of situations where the line fishtailed sharply in the other direction, but overall without rereading everything all I can say is that that's the impression I got. I have been wrong before, though; since you usually <i>can't</i> take an entire White Wolf line as a single face-value piece, I tend to just glide over the dumb things I can't use.<br /> <br /> I will be interested to see what 3e does with this also!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T01:27:03-07:00","id":205815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204977#post204977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general structure of the Time of Tumult for established non-Solars with long memories is that the Solars are nuclear weapons, and the tension is in &quot;man, what do I do with all these Solars?&quot; because you know that they are vulnerable to manipulation and attack, but will eventually ripen into unimaginable power, and you have to decide how you want to deal with that. Do you ally with their enemies to put them down? Do you try to kill any who fuck with you, while otherwise leaving well enough alone? Do you wind them up, point them at something you want gone, and then stay out of it? Do you try to make friends and sell them on your own agenda, aware that you have to be careful because one day they may be too powerful for you to control?</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea represented here really irks me - solars have to be the best and greatest at pretty much everything, because otherwise the setting doesn't work - that it is the power of the Solars that makes their reemergence such a big deal. Sure, power is a big theme for Solars, but it tends to overshadow two others I consider even more important - virtue and legitimacy.<br /> <br /> The chosen of the Sun are the rightful leaders of the world, the true and right kings and queens of creation. Legitimacy isn't just about power - otherwise the Dragon-blooded would have <i>earned </i>it in full with the Usurpation. It isn't about how many charms you can throw around or what circle demons you can bind. We talked about fairy tales and fables, so let us consider their influence - there the protagonist is sometimes not the strongest or the smartest, but s/he is always with a good heart. This is how they earn their happy ending, not by some quirk of fate (even when fate is involved, it is not undeserved). Solars coming back would be a big deal even if they weren't any more powerful than Lunars or Sidereals, because of what they represent. They are the shining beacons of hope and virtue that contrast with the decaying, corrupt Empire. The rulers of old that come to claim their world from the pretenders. That makes their story much more compelling than &quot;they can be stronger than anyone else,&quot; because it gives them a place and a role no one else can match. The ruler sees them and unconsciously realizes s/he is sitting in a seat meant for someone else. The peasant working in the field, or the craftsman toiling in the shack sees them and his or her heart rises in awe - they are back, and the world is on the way to becoming right. Things will become what they should be.<br /> <br /> It isn't just about the role, though, it is about the narrative as well. The Unconquered Sun may be the strongest of the Incarna, but it is his virtues and leadership that define him, not his strength alone, that define him, and they are His chosen. It is for their lack of virtue and their loss of legitimacy that they were, in time overthrown - it is said that the one final rumor that convinced the Sidereals that their masters had lost the way was when they heard the Unconquered Sun turned away from his chosen, thus showing the ones at the time had lost his backing, thus their mandate to rule. And now, purified after the long exile, they return to a world that, in its current state, needs exactly exemplars of virtue to combat all the corruption and decay, the rightful rulers to forge the splintering world and subdue the claimants. That is the true power of the Solar Exalted imo - having them be the ones with the most power, coolest sword magic and all-around bestest skillz can actually obscure that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-23-2014, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T01:38:15-07:00","id":205818,"title":"","content":"Also, solars may be more powerful-- but with the elimination of the E6+ charms as a major theme and from what we've seen of the published solar charms inteh developer previews they're not like they were-- a Solar still NEEDS lunars and DB's and Sidereals, both because they can do stuff he can't, and because solars can no longer laugh off attacks by their foes. A bit off topic, but this is what makes me eager for this styesm, the hope that yeah, we'll now have mechanical support for the idea that making friends with the DB isn't just about getting a flunky, it's getting someone who is Important and will remain important no matter how powerful the solar gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T02:46:07-07:00","id":205857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205815#post205815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The chosen of the Sun are the rightful leaders of the world, the true and right kings and queens of creation. Legitimacy isn't just about power - otherwise the Dragon-blooded would have earned it in full with the Usurpation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that pretty much how the solars got it in the first place though? I mean, sure, they were endorsed as such by the gods, but the gods only had the right to do that because they had nicked it about a week before from the Primordials. <br /> <br /> So depending on your viewpoint on succession either the DBs claim to ruling creation is legitimate, or the Yozi's is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T04:20:53-07:00","id":205933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204959#post204959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is a reason for them to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like Bob, Exigent of Dan, god of Evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T04:23:56-07:00","id":205935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205818#post205818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, solars may be more powerful-- but with the elimination of the E6+ charms as a major theme and from what we've seen of the published solar charms inteh developer previews they're not like they were-- a Solar still NEEDS lunars and DB's and Sidereals, both because they can do stuff he can't, and because solars can no longer laugh off attacks by their foes. A bit off topic, but this is what makes me eager for this styesm, the hope that yeah, we'll now have mechanical support for the idea that making friends with the DB isn't just about getting a flunky, it's getting someone who is Important and will remain important no matter how powerful the solar gets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The solar's ability to just laugh off attacks or damage being reduced does mean that they will need help. No doubt tallented players (munchkins) will find a way to break the system. Exploit something in the DV system to make themselves mostly unhitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T05:32:46-07:00","id":205960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205815#post205815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This idea represented here really irks me - solars have to be the best and greatest at pretty much everything, because otherwise the setting doesn't work - that it is the power of the Solars that makes their reemergence such a big deal. Sure, power is a big theme for Solars, but it tends to overshadow two others I consider even more important - virtue and legitimacy.<br /> <br /> The chosen of the Sun are the rightful leaders of the world, the true and right kings and queens of creation. Legitimacy isn't just about power - otherwise the Dragon-blooded would have <i>earned </i>it in full with the Usurpation. It isn't about how many charms you can throw around or what circle demons you can bind. We talked about fairy tales and fables, so let us consider their influence - there the protagonist is sometimes not the strongest or the smartest, but s/he is always with a good heart. This is how they earn their happy ending, not by some quirk of fate (even when fate is involved, it is not undeserved). Solars coming back would be a big deal even if they weren't any more powerful than Lunars or Sidereals, because of what they represent. They are the shining beacons of hope and virtue that contrast with the decaying, corrupt Empire. The rulers of old that come to claim their world from the pretenders. That makes their story much more compelling than &quot;they can be stronger than anyone else,&quot; because it gives them a place and a role no one else can match. The ruler sees them and unconsciously realizes s/he is sitting in a seat meant for someone else. The peasant working in the field, or the craftsman toiling in the shack sees them and his or her heart rises in awe - they are back, and the world is on the way to becoming right. Things will become what they should be.<br /> <br /> It isn't just about the role, though, it is about the narrative as well. The Unconquered Sun may be the strongest of the Incarna, but it is his virtues and leadership that define him, not his strength alone, that define him, and they are His chosen. It is for their lack of virtue and their loss of legitimacy that they were, in time overthrown - it is said that the one final rumor that convinced the Sidereals that their masters had lost the way was when they heard the Unconquered Sun turned away from his chosen, thus showing the ones at the time had lost his backing, thus their mandate to rule. And now, purified after the long exile, they return to a world that, in its current state, needs exactly exemplars of virtue to combat all the corruption and decay, the rightful rulers to forge the splintering world and subdue the claimants. That is the true power of the Solar Exalted imo - having them be the ones with the most power, coolest sword magic and all-around bestest skillz can actually obscure that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree, sorry. The fact that the Solars are substantially stronger and can do things others can't is the #1 thing that makes their return so important. &quot;Legitimacy&quot; is definitely the wrong tack to take, because Exalted very self-consciously undermines the notion of legitimacy, and to make that the one reason the Solars' return matters, you would have to pump it up to a degree that I think would be unhealthy for the game.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Exalted is a game about realpolitik and harsh, ground-level maneuvering. It is not going to radically change the setting if you increase the number of Anathema by 50%, except <i>these</i> Anathema are good-hearted rightful rulers (implicitly casting everyone else as illegitimate and corrupt by default). That isn't <i>worth</i> anything in the setting without something to back it up<i>, </i>and again, to strengthen those themes to the point where it's useful you would have to throw out important, deliberate setting elements like &quot;The Solars' burgeoning corruption brought about the end of the Golden Age&quot; and &quot;The people with the best claim to being 'rightful rulers of the world' are the ones the Exalted murdered before history.&quot; Solars have a <i>thematic</i> of rejuvenating, fresh-faced righteousness, and if you're playing a Solar yourself the &quot;reclaiming your rightful throne&quot; thing is likely to be important to you, but these inform their role in the setting, and <i>especially</i> the way they relate to other characters, far less than you seem to be imagining.<br /> <br /> Like, okay, let's say the Solars are just on par with Lunars except with different power themes and a thematic of righteousness. As a Dragon-Blooded, I want them all dead, so this isn't really going to be any different to me than a bunch of new Lunars. If I'm a Sidereal, again this is basically the same situation I've been dealing with all along -- any protestations to the natural righteousness and legitimacy of Solars are going to wash over the people who <i>specifically</i> targeted the Solars for extinction due to their excesses (a move which comes off a lot worse if the Solars weren't stronger). If I'm a Lunar, I probably only care about this on a personal level and have an eye on how it will disrupt politics due to the influx of new players. Certainly I am not going to be that sympathetic to the idea that all these returning Solars are a big deal because they're more righteous and legitimate than I am. Trying to push this angle is actually much worse for non-Solars, I think, because the only way for the setting to make sense is to presume that those characters are intrinsically irrelevant in a post-Solar world, except as people for Solars to take the reins from.<br /> <br /> The context of the game is that the return of the Solars be a setting-defining event that everyone is reacting to, and for non-Solars the game involves figuring out how to exploit or secure yourself against this new upheaval. This cannot work if that's entirely dependent on the Solars legitimacy and pure hearts, because those things are neither especially important nor, crucially, are they <i>measurable</i> in the setting. Literally everybody has a tenable claim to legitimacy and people are generally going to favour whichever claim suits their biases and personal interests. The thing is, yes, there is an undertone and thematic of Solars as righteous, but the game is very explicitly questioning what righteousness and legitimacy are, and acknowledging that people do not tend to agree. People are not going to be able to look at Solars doing stuff, and then look at Lunars doing stuff, and say, &quot;Hmm, these Solars are definitely more virtuous and upstanding&quot;. Insofar as it comes up at all in-setting it's more like &quot;It says in this old book here (this book from the Golden Age ruled by Solars!) that Solars are the most righteous and upstanding, and we can perhaps extrapolate that from the properties of their patron.&quot; If a Solar rolls into your territory and recruits 5000 able-bodied workers to join her revolutionary army and then fucks off again, that is not worth much, and it's insult to injury if the setting is heavily pushing the notion that the Solar is in the right Because Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-23-2014, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T06:04:56-07:00","id":205977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205857#post205857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that pretty much how the solars got it in the first place though? I mean, sure, they were endorsed as such by the gods, but the gods only had the right to do that because they had nicked it about a week before from the Primordials.<br /> <br /> So depending on your viewpoint on succession either the DBs claim to ruling creation is legitimate, or the Yozi's is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the tack I have run with in my games previously.<br /> <br /> FWIW, though, 2e established in no uncertain terms (but like much of 2e, uncertain wisdom) that the Mandate of Heaven, the claim by which the Exalted had dominion over Creation, explicitly applied only to the Celestial Exalted. (This led to that line about gods having more innate respect for the most wretched street urchin--who might theoretically Exalt as a Celestial--than the greatest Dragon-Blood)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T06:41:57-07:00","id":206012,"title":"","content":"I can see some gods having that opinion - they are a bunch of jerks sometimes - but really that conclusion is just stupid even if the MoH <i>did</i> only apply to celestials. I mean It was dragonblooded who helped them throw of the Yoke of the primordials wasn't it? Bunch of ungrateful bastards. <br /> <br /> I think the original idea is a good one though. It gives the terrestrial gods an excuse to disobey them without heavenly reprisal which in turn gives the Immaculate Order a reason to start kicking heads in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T07:04:32-07:00","id":206044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205815#post205815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This idea represented here really irks me - solars have to be the best and greatest at pretty much everything, because otherwise the setting doesn't work - that it is the power of the Solars that makes their reemergence such a big deal. Sure, power is a big theme for Solars, but it tends to overshadow two others I consider even more important - virtue and legitimacy.<br /> <br /> The chosen of the Sun are the rightful leaders of the world, the true and right kings and queens of creation. Legitimacy isn't just about power - otherwise the Dragon-blooded would have <i>earned </i>it in full with the Usurpation. It isn't about how many charms you can throw around or what circle demons you can bind. We talked about fairy tales and fables, so let us consider their influence - there the protagonist is sometimes not the strongest or the smartest, but s/he is always with a good heart. This is how they earn their happy ending, not by some quirk of fate (even when fate is involved, it is not undeserved). Solars coming back would be a big deal even if they weren't any more powerful than Lunars or Sidereals, because of what they represent. They are the shining beacons of hope and virtue that contrast with the decaying, corrupt Empire. The rulers of old that come to claim their world from the pretenders. That makes their story much more compelling than &quot;they can be stronger than anyone else,&quot; because it gives them a place and a role no one else can match. The ruler sees them and unconsciously realizes s/he is sitting in a seat meant for someone else. The peasant working in the field, or the craftsman toiling in the shack sees them and his or her heart rises in awe - they are back, and the world is on the way to becoming right. Things will become what they should be.<br /> <br /> It isn't just about the role, though, it is about the narrative as well. The Unconquered Sun may be the strongest of the Incarna, but it is his virtues and leadership that define him, not his strength alone, that define him, and they are His chosen. It is for their lack of virtue and their loss of legitimacy that they were, in time overthrown - it is said that the one final rumor that convinced the Sidereals that their masters had lost the way was when they heard the Unconquered Sun turned away from his chosen, thus showing the ones at the time had lost his backing, thus their mandate to rule. And now, purified after the long exile, they return to a world that, in its current state, needs exactly exemplars of virtue to combat all the corruption and decay, the rightful rulers to forge the splintering world and subdue the claimants. That is the true power of the Solar Exalted imo - having them be the ones with the most power, coolest sword magic and all-around bestest skillz can actually obscure that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure which I find more appalling: the idea of the Solars as having an inherent moral high ground so that by definition anyone who opposes giving up all authority to them is evil and wrong, or the idea that these 150 people have created a world that cannot survive without them, so that even though they're all insane tyrants in the making everyone else has to either submit to them or die. The more the writers and the game emphasize how much &quot;Creation <i>needs</i> the Solars&quot;, the worse my opinion of Solars becomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T07:11:52-07:00","id":206052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205960#post205960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree, sorry. The fact that the Solars are substantially stronger and can do things others can't is the #1 thing that makes their return so important. &quot;Legitimacy&quot; is definitely the wrong tack to take, because Exalted very self-consciously undermines the notion of legitimacy, and to make that the one reason the Solars' return matters, you would have to pump it up to a degree that I think would be unhealthy for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we disagree, then. Having Solars being the uber-Exalted that must be the best at swordfighting, oratory, pickpocketing, interior decoration, interpretative dance and anything that exists because this they are Solars and this is their position in the world is something I find extremely off-putting and frankly unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I'm spoilering the rest because it is starting to get mostly off-topic for this thread. As for Evocations, I'd rather wait a bit more to see just <i>how </i>they are better than anyone else and then see if I like the <i>why.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[Realpolitik and harsh measures are only a part of the narrative, and often a sign of the compromises and the lessening of the world in its dark times. It is what Creation is used to about in the current age - after all, it is the Age of Sorrows. The interaction between the themes of what is and what should be is reflected in other conflicts as well - the rivalry between Mnemon and the Roseblack, for example. At the end of the day, it is not about legitimacy being right or wrong but what constitutes legitimacy and how it is derived. A ruler needs to be obeyed to rule - whether out of fear, force, tradition, love, or what have you.<br /> <br /> Let us presume there is no <i>huge </i> difference between Lunars and Solars in overall power - some are better in some things, other in others. I'd argue that it does not detract from Solars being such a big deal. The Solars' theme leans itself much better to leadership, and this makes them that much more dangerous to the Realm as they are much better at providing an alternative for people to accept and rally behind. If you are a Dragonblooded, you find out that these things are far, far more persuasive and dangerous in undermining your cause than the Lunar anathema ever were. A few words from them whip up a crowd from strangers who have spent their whole lives tilling the fields to rise up. With a simple admonition, their enemies, weak-hearted mortals that they are, lay down their arms and join them. They can act as wide-eyed idealists, leading if all the accumulated wisdom of how the world <i>should </i>work simply does not apply to them - and the thing is, they <i>make it work</i>. They do the things your ancestors never did... that they never could. The spirits and demons that you spent months bargaining with - and those your teachers told you can not be bargained with - bow down their heads and speak as if to their lords and masters. They challenge the authority and legitimacy of the Realm and the Dragonblooded like no other have, and can. To a prince of the Earth they are more than just a dangerous enemy. These supposed Anathema do everything that you were taught is right, and make little of the compromise you are taught must be made, and they still win. And at some point, in your heart of hearts, you start doubting.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are in just a big of a mess. Before the solars came back, Sidereals didn\u00b4t have an easy time either - a lot of gods, elementals and the like never quite forgave them for what they did and never quite gave them the support they used to have. Just look at Whitewall - several powerful gods went out and against all laws acted to become the seneschals of a city because they considered valued it as sacred to the UCS and its chosen. Still, the naysayers had no choice - what was done was done, and everyone had to live with the consequences. Except now they are back. The Solars had plenty of supporters and advocates in Heaven when they were supposedly gone for good - just how much support would they have now they have come back, so far with little of the insane hubris they used to have? How many of their old supporters can you turn back? How many of the fence-sitters can at most be persuaded to stay on the fence? And how many of your supporters - or at least those who stood behind you when the mighty Sun Kings were cast down - will stay on your side? All the things once accepted as truth - about who and what the Solars were, what they did and what had to be done are now reevaluated in the face of the Solars and their deeds. At the end of the day, even the most jaded Sidereal was once human, and even the most cynical once held a kernel of respect for the institutions and order they serve. At some level, no one can deny the magnetism of the Solar cause. Chejop can say he was right a millenia and a half ago and is still right now, but with all that happened since and the sight of the Sun-Chosen coming to the world, not everyone believes him. Ultimately, they will be judged by their own actions.<br /> <br /> My point is that Solar have a power that goes beyond their <i>personal </i>might, and that is one of the unique things about them - something that no other exalt, demon, Deathlord or whatever of Creation-shaking power has. They should be powerful, definitely, but it is how they interact with the world that makes them such a force. A Dragonblooded may awe you with their powers or inflame their passions, a Lunar can incite feelings inside you that you didn't even know existed, but when a Solar speaks, it is as if a<span style=\"color:#001320\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> voice came from the cloud, right in your heart, saying, &quot;This is my Son, whom I have chosen; listen to him.&quot;</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> @ Couch - it is not that an individual Solar will have the moral high ground by default, but that a protagonist doesn't necessarily HAVE to be the strongest, smartest and overall best. Yet of all exalted Solars have the tightest connection to the heroic virtues through what they represent via their connection to the UCS and what they tend to be exalted for. It is their theme - how a particular Solar will react is his or her own prerogative, but there should be some reason why they got UCS' attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-23-2014, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T07:18:19-07:00","id":206062,"title":"","content":"Creation needs the solars mostly because of the other solar-like things who popped up at around the same time. <br /> <br /> They're saving creation from themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:32:02-07:00","id":206216,"title":"","content":"Solars are not the &quot;leader Exalted&quot;. They are, in an abstract historical sense, the leaders <i>of</i> the Exalted, and leadership is one of their themes, but having the one defining Solar property that sets them apart be that they're super inspiring and everyone wants to follow them and do what they say would be straitjacketing. Making this the Solars' defining gimmick -- I mean to the point where it implies meaningful effects on the setting, which is what I'm hearing suggested -- also forces you to make other Exalted worse at it, in fact probably worse than they actually will be in 3e as it stands, so it has a narrowing effect on everybody else as well. For example, currently Lunars are pretty damn good at doing the Second Coming thing, so you'd have to really cut back on that ability in order to make the Solars' comparative edge big enough to singlehandedly justify the setting conceit that the Solars' return is a huge deal. The fact that <i>aesthetically</i> a Solar rabble-rouser tends to evoke liberation theology and divine revelation in a way that other splats don't is cheap coin in Creation.<br /> <br /> If a Solar swordsman isn't scarier than a Lunar swordsman by virtue of being a Solar, then no Solar whose gimmick is &quot;being a swordsman&quot; is more noteworthy than a Lunar simply by virtue of being an ancient returned king of the world. Probably less so as of RY768, because the Lunar is much more likely to be experienced and powerful. If there's one specific niche that makes the return of the Solars scary, then any Solar without that niche is an also-ran, which has a narrowing effect on what is meant to be the broadest splat in a game full of broad splats. The Revolutionary Prophet is a good meat-and-potatoes Solar concept, but almost none of the Solars I've seen, and none of the ones I've played, looked anything like that.<br /> <br /> The big question the Solars pose to those with a long view of history is: if left to their own devices, will they return the world to the heights of the First Age, or will they finally turn the world into the hellish place the Sidereals foresaw in the Prophecies of Gold and Darkness? This question requires a context: <i>why</i> was the First Age so wonderful at its heights? <i>Why</i> would the world in which the corrupt Solars were left unchecked be nightmarish and broken? Answering this question with &quot;because the Solars are chosen prophets of the Most High, and people eagerly flock to their banner&quot; does not give satisfying results, because it implies that the defining feature of the First Age was that everyone worked together in mutual love and friendship because of Solar leadership, and the corrupted age would be bad because, I guess, they would all go to war on one another or use their leadership ability to make people do bad things? It just doesn't work as well -- it sucks all the blood out of nations and armies until they feel like abstracted units with an unrest statistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-23-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:18:46-07:00","id":206277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=204890#post204890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sid becomes more and more distant, detached, and a Plutocrat.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Plutocrat? <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orthogals.files.wordpress.com/2014/02/words1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> (Sorry, couldn't help myself.)<br /> <br /> Anyway... to the topic at hand. Just for clarification, what are we discussing - Solar superiority or Solar<i>oid </i>superiority? (Beyond the specific context of Evocations I mean.) Because I'm okay with one of those things, but not the other. There's a certain sort of implicit moralizing that I really, <i>really</i> hope left the line with Neph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:44:49-07:00","id":206307,"title":"","content":"Man, this is a long thread. I couldn't more than skim it - it seems to have turned into a discusion about Solar suprmacy and the whole legitiomate leaders and stuff. So, my own, quick opinion about it...<br /> <br /> Yes, the fact that Solars are Better Than You IS annoying to high hell, and puts me off from playing them, but it's how the game works. The Solars are in no uncertain terms the <i>protagonists</i> of this thing, as can be seen in the fact that every other Exalted type is explicitly defined primarily for how it relates to the Solars, and the writers have hit that bell against our heads dozens of time. In Exalted, like in so much shonen anime, the secondary characters may be more interesting than the main character, but that isn't going to make the main character less the focus of the thing, and constantly hoping for Goku to fall off a bridge and drown so Piccolo can take the leading role is just going to bring your frustration and heartache. I've more or less made my peace with it, even if I'm not a fan of it. <br /> <br /> I draw the line at the whole &quot;legitimate king&quot; thing, though. I can deal with an entire splat of people who are more powerful than me and who could perform my party niche better than I do for half the XP I spent. If I <i>needed </i>to feel powerful and useful I would be playing M&amp;M, not Exalted. But if the ST also takes the view that they are not only more powerful, but outright <i>better </i>for the future than everyone and all the world loves them and it is only right and proper that they govern again (which is a thing I've seen), <i>that </i>is when I get the hell out of dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T11:11:10-07:00","id":206329,"title":"","content":"I feel as though phrasing it in terms of &quot;Solars are better than you&quot; is still providing an answer to the wrong question, because it misconstrues the meaning of other Exalted being differently powered, namely that they're around to do and be different things.<br /> <br /> It's like... look at Bureuacracy. In a system with a good way of representing bureuacracies and how the relevant Ability interfaces with them, with good hooks for Charms about them, a Solar has all kinds of ways to be amazing at running and harnessing a bureaucratic system, ways to make procedure go faster or to tie people up in precedents and regulations, the works.<br /> <br /> A Sidereal uses Bureaucracy to do things like destroy an organisation, end an argument, and pose a fairly lethal threat to spirits.<br /> <br /> I don't really see these people as competing in the same arena.<br /> <br /> The Solar still comes across as more powerful than the Sidereal because they're better at directing bureaucracies to do the kinds of things you'd use them for, but I think they're a bit hard-pressed to have an individual Charm as powerful as End Debate, and can't really use the Bureaucracy Ability to do anything like Terminal Sanction at all. End Debate and Terminal Sanction alone don't make the Sidereal a more powerful bureaucrat than the Solar, and even their place in the overall Bureaucracy cascade don't really help make the Sidereal much good at bureaucracy at all.<br /> <br /> But they're fairly good for doing the kinds of things that matter to the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't mean they're useless at running bureaucracies altogether; I'd say a big part of making a system that's fun for playing mortals (in which they can present meaningful challenges even for Solars) is that you also implicitly producing a system in which a playing an Exalt can be fun even if you're not a type who'd have Charms for doing that thing directly. A Sidereal with Bureaucracy 5 will still be good at actions and challenges based on that Ability even if they don't have Charms that do other things for it (they may also still have some degree of recourse to target number alteration).<br /> <br /> That's not to say that the absence of organisations that, implicitly or explicitly, could only exist if run with the level of expertise or complexity that only a Solar could manage is not meaningful to a Sidereal. Part of the idea of the Age of Sorrows is living in a world where the capacity for such a thing has not been present for a long time, with a meaningful detrimental effect. Part of the narrative premise of a bunch of Sidereals is that they saw that as a worthwhile sacrifice; the game should really try to sell one on the credibility of such a position, I think.<br /> <br /> But it's still a matter of how Sidereals respond to a problem that exists outside of themselves; it's still not quite an arena that they're competing for the same space in.<br /> <br /> Still, one of the areas that Sidereals <i>are</i> focused on is concerned with how they engage their response; they might not be able to run super-bureuacracies, but they do have certain of the necessary tools to alternately bring about that desired sacrifice of the Solars, or to guide or manipulate them into making such organisations, as suits the Exalt in question.<br /> <br /> That doesn't make the Sidereal equally powerful to the Solar, but it doesn't make them useless against them (or alongside them) either. Indeed, it's a dynamic and a tension that is directly informed by the idea of a disparity in their power.<br /> <br /> This is part of why it helps to view Exalts holistically.<br /> <br /> I think you get much the same deal with Evocations; mastery of powerful weapons isn't really a thing that's part of the Sidereals, even though they're affected by the presence or absence of people who can, and do have their own means of affecting that presence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T11:27:45-07:00","id":206341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205935#post205935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solar's ability to just laugh off attacks or damage being reduced does mean that they will need help. No doubt tallented players (munchkins) will find a way to break the system. Exploit something in the DV system to make themselves mostly unhitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single game system has mechanical exploits and optimized builds. Every single one. You can't get rid of them completely - what you can do is design a baseline system that doesn't already stack the deck in the offense vs defense game, etc. I'm sure there will be strong builds in 3e, but taking a different tack from 2e (cheap, easy perfects) will likely go a long way to make the game more fun to play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205815#post205815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This idea represented here really irks me - solars have to be the best and greatest at pretty much everything, because otherwise the setting doesn't work - that it is the power of the Solars that makes their reemergence such a big deal. Sure, power is a big theme for Solars, but it tends to overshadow two others I consider even more important - virtue and legitimacy.<br /> <br /> The chosen of the Sun are the rightful leaders of the world, the true and right kings and queens of creation. . . . They are the shining beacons of hope and virtue that contrast with the decaying, corrupt Empire. The rulers of old that come to claim their world from the pretenders . . . The peasant working in the field, or the craftsman toiling in the shack sees them and his or her heart rises in awe - they are back, and the world is on the way to becoming right. Things will become what they should be. . . And now, purified after the long exile, they return to a world that, in its current state, needs exactly exemplars of virtue to combat all the corruption and decay, the rightful rulers to forge the splintering world and subdue the claimants.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The returning Solars are all pure of heart and deed, and inspiring of hope and good times to come&quot; is <i>not not not not not a given for all Solars</i> and should not at all be a given either. If that's <i>your </i>Solar, cool, great. But making &quot;good guy righteousness turned up to 11&quot; a theme of Solars invalidates any concepts of grey morality Solars and Solar anti-heroes and that is just terrible. Holy fire is not a Good-aligned weapon, it's divine judgment against things deemed Unclean to Creation - a definition which, in some cases, may be rooted in ideas of &quot;that thing is icky and/or unnatural, so probably bad&quot; rather than them being Evil. Ghosts are mostly innocents - there's nothing morally wrong about being tied to your life and not wanting to move on, but to UCS he sees &quot;dead soul --&gt; not going to Lethe as programmed --&gt; bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sweeney Todd is a valid inspiration for a Solar, just as King Arthur might be - they explore different themes, but they also both represent standing up for ideals and exerting power to accomplish those ideals; Havish the Vanisher and Filial Wisdom are completely valid as Solars as Salina and Dace are (took me a while to think up a canon RY 765 Solar who's not doing-things-for-good-reasons-but-also-a-complete-ass).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-23-2014, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T11:30:26-07:00","id":206345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205815#post205815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now, purified after the long exile, they return to a world that, in its current state, needs exactly exemplars of virtue to combat all the corruption and decay, the rightful rulers to forge the splintering world and subdue the claimants.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of carrying on the off-topicness...<br /> <br /> Whenever I encounter a viewpoint like this, I am always interested in hearing how it squares with the likes of, say, Harvesh the Vanisher. Or any other Solar who doesn't radiate anything near what you've described. These are still legitimate Solar characters and would seem to serve as firm counterexamples to the narrative proposed, or suggestions that things are more complicated. This isn't meant to be argumentative or a dig: I have a genuine curiosity about how you reconcile your viewpoint with such Solars","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T14:45:04-07:00","id":206573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206216#post206216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big question the Solars pose to those with a long view of history is: if left to their own devices, will they return the world to the heights of the First Age, or will they finally turn the world into the hellish place the Sidereals foresaw in the Prophecies of Gold and Darkness? This question requires a context: <i>why</i> was the First Age so wonderful at its heights? <i>Why</i> would the world in which the corrupt Solars were left unchecked be nightmarish and broken?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a para-canon ending to the Second Age, the First Edition Core goes with <i>&quot;it slipped inch by inch into barbarism and darkness, until one last catacylsm blotted it out forever. Yet in its sunset, it was a splendid thing, and glorious were the deeds of the Exalted&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> I think that conveys, fairly well, that the Solars were not certain to be Second Age's demise or destroyers, nor, alone, to be its uplifting. Neither of Chejop Kejak's nightmare scenarios have to out.<br /> <br /> (The end, the catacylsm, could come from a number of directions).<br /> <br /> For some reason that's got lost.<br /> <br /> When this book says <i>&quot;the Lunar Exalted were the most powerful emissaries of the Exalted Court&quot;</i>, or <i>&quot;Commonly, Lunars were the consorts of the Solars ... it also reduced the competitive tension which occasionally arose between the Lunar and the Solar Exalted by granting them frequent contact and allowing them to share authority over the land they ruled&quot;</i> or <i>&quot;The Sidereals great insight into destiny was the star by which the Solars steered the ship of state&quot;</i> or <i>&quot;the Sidereal Exalted were far more talented at astrology and learning than any others&quot;</i> (comparing the Twilight Caste to the Sidereals), then this edition meant it.<br /> <br /> When discussing the First Age, it says <i>&quot;Some argue that the wisdom of the First Age is not gone, but merely, that the complex civilization that made the Age possible has passed away. Others contend that the world changed irrevocably when the Great Contagion struck and that, even if the lore of the lost First Age were reclaimed and put to use, it would mean little. So far, neither group is organized or determined enough to put their theories to the test.&quot;</i> There's an opportunity to hang this all on Solar magic and skill which was not taken here. Consciously, I think.<br /> <br /> The loss of the Solars was the catalyst for the end of the First Age. Not the only thing making it what is was, in both of its possible endings.<br /> <br /> The Second Edition seems to want the dilemma of the end of the First Age to go on forever. I don't think, reasonably, it can. It's a choice that shapes the world, not necessarily the question that keeps being asked.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean the Solars weren't worth suppressing or fighting for, by the Bronze and Gold factions - clearly they were.<br /> <br /> I see, optimistically, some hint of a return to this healthier attitude in how 3e developer has described &quot;Imagine the splendor of a First Age in which the Solars are surrounded not just by Sidereal viziers, Lunar compatriots and Dragon-Blooded honor guards, but whole hosts of majestic heroes and numinous champions, glorious, infernal and divine.&quot; What I'm talking about isn't exactly legitimacy and harmony over power, but it is the Age being more than the sum of the Solar Exalted, and the ways &quot;they&quot; could end the First Age also being more than the sum of them, while both being handily &quot;lost&quot; or &quot;solved&quot; by their deaths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206329#post206329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like... look at Bureuacracy. In a system with a good way of representing bureuacracies and how the relevant Ability interfaces with them, with good hooks for Charms about them, a Solar has all kinds of ways to be amazing at running and harnessing a bureaucratic system, ways to make procedure go faster or to tie people up in precedents and regulations, the works.<br /> A Sidereal uses Bureaucracy to do things like destroy an organisation, end an argument, and pose a fairly lethal threat to spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an aside to your main point, but made me think, with the Abyssals being destructive, the Lunars... not really focused in genre on building bureaucratic organisations, and the Dragonblooded less powerful, it was an interesting choice to focus the Sidereals Bureaucracy Ability on Endings, as the scalpel that removes to reshape the Heavenly Bureaucracy. It leaves Solars as the only Creation dwelling Celestial level group with a strong hand in creative bureaucratic magic.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this was informed more by a desire to shape the setting in certain ways, or by Bureaucracy having to be constrained to one Maiden and a decision being taken for bureaucratic Sidereals to have a certain feel and a certain intimidating &quot;hatchet man&quot; attitude to bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> For all that the setting as it is commits to this, the pairing of Endings with Bureaucracy being non-arbitrary, I'd be interested to see a version of Sidereals that allowed them to filter any Ability through any Maiden, for this reason. What does the Bureaucracy of Serenity look like? The Medicine of Journeys? I doubt this is on the cards in 3e though.<br /> <br /> But then, this is part of why Exigents are the most exciting development of 3e! Allowing these expressions of magic infused Ability to be explored while keeping the old specialities of the old Exalted and avoiding any setting disruption that would come by having Celestial size hosts of Celestial level Exalted appear on the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T15:47:47-07:00","id":206623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206573#post206573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When this book says <i>&quot;the Lunar Exalted were the most powerful emissaries of the Exalted Court&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes books just say dumb things. It's easy to get caught up in your subject matter and say something that doesn't make a lot of sense when pulled out of context.<br /> <br /> (I mean, not to pick a fight over that one line, but if you're going to hang your hat on that you're going to be disappointed. That quote is not and was never intended to be literally true, and if an author said otherwise they screwed up.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;the Sidereal Exalted were far more talented at astrology and learning than any others&quot;</i> (comparing the Twilight Caste to the Sidereals), then this edition meant it. </div> </div> </div>Astrology yes, learning no, and again, if you're going to focus on statements like that you're going to be disappointed.<br /> <br /> Obviously the First age was more than &quot;the Solars did everything forever on their own, the end&quot; and the story of the Second age is not &quot;the Solars arrive and change everything personally with no interaction with anyone else, the end.&quot;<br /> <br /> But as a general rule of thumb (keeping in mind that generalizations always miss something, of course), the mightiest emissaries of the Exalted were probably the Eclipse caste, and the Twilight caste are at least as good at scholarly learning as anyone else (it's a broad and ill-defined topic, so I'd want to hedge a bit; but saying that the Sidereals were &quot;far more talented&quot; is flat-out wrong); this is central to both their definitions. And those things are not even really central to the definitions of the Lunars or Sidereals -- the Lunars as powerful emissaries thing seems completely out-of-the-blue, to the extent that it would be just as true with the name of almost any other splat inserted. Sidereals, of course, are <i>wise</i>, and more knowledgeable in certain matters than anyone else -- even putting aside their obvious advantages in the second age -- but they're probably not eg. the very best magical or theoretical researchers outside of their specific fields.<br /> <br /> But again, I see statements like the ones you quoted as fundamentally unhealthy for the line -- those are bad quotes. You shouldn't say &quot;X is the very absolute best at Y, far more talented than anyone else&quot; unless it is <i>absolutely</i> essential to what they are. Even then, there's almost nothing where I would include the 'far more' qualifier, for anyone. That's basically saying &quot;nobody else can meaningfully touch this, fullstop.&quot; For astrology, maybe, but for <i>learning</i>? Don't be ridiculous. That's an author getting too caught up in excitedly expressing how wise the Sidereals are without considering the implications of their statement, or how learning is at least as important a concept for others.<br /> <br /> Even for Solars the books are usually pretty conservative about using lines like that. (Mostly it comes up with regard to crafting and gestalt prowess, which are both essential to the setting's history and therefore hard to hedge about.) But taking that caution and using it to say &quot;aha, it doesn't specifically say Twilights are the most learned Exalted! Here is a place where Sidereals can be better!&quot; is missing the point. You do that and first, the concept of gestalt Solar power and Solars as a whole as (overall) leaders in their fields will suffer a death of a thousand cuts as everyone gets defined as better than them at some core Solar thing, turning them into the jack-of-all-trades, master-of-none Exalted; and second, you'll end up cutting into more than just Solars, as each type of Exalted has to carefully write around the carelessly-broad &quot;nobody can come close to X at Y!&quot; statements made by everyone else.<br /> <br /> (Or, more likely, you'll end up with those statements becoming an empty joke as writers just ignore them -- certainly, while they have a number of unique and powerful effects to reflect their theme of supernatural wisdom, Sidereals do not have the &quot;best at learning overall&quot; reflected in their charms, and Lunars are neither unusually powerful nor particularly talented emissaries compared to other Exalted in either edition. This is because, thankfully, other writers wrote their subjects in whatever way was best for them and the overarching definition of the setting, not constantly worrying about how some writer carelessly wrote a line saying that Lunars NUMBAH ONE at emissary-ing or that whatever you have <i>doesn't even compare</i> to Sidereals at being learned.)<br /> <br /> It's a cheap and thoughtless way to make your subject look awesome at the expense of everyone else. That thinking was how we ended up with a list of &quot;greatest martial artists in Creation&quot; longer than your arm back in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-23-2014, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:05:19-07:00","id":206648,"title":"","content":"Being that the Lunar were not the better but the more POWERFUL means that they had a nice is that role that even the solar could not fill. You send the solar in and he carefully negotiates and there is long back and forth.<br /> <br /> You send the lunar in and the person on the other side &quot;Must have&quot; wants &quot;now now now&quot; what ever it is your offering. That or the Lunar can always take plan be and force them to sign it by using sheer force. Lunar social ability in some ways in 2e is as good or even can outstripe Solar.<br /> <br /> The Solar are very good scholars and the Twilight have their things but the Sidereal have in some ways the ability eek out a little bit ahead of the solar. This doesn't diminish the Solar scholar who can skill achieve many great things but the sidereal can learn faster, same with the air aspected dragon blood. These two might not be able to do as many grand things with their knowelge but they can obtain the same knowledge levels as the solar faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:06:27-07:00","id":206650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this was informed more by a desire to shape the setting in certain ways, or by Bureaucracy having to be constrained to one Maiden and a decision being taken for bureaucratic Sidereals to have a certain feel and a certain intimidating &quot;hatchet man&quot; attitude to bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like to think that the symbolism of the Constellations in general was based on the idea of a mysticism that was cynical rather than uplifting. It's most blatant with the Lovers, but it pops up all over. That popular idea about Solars, about how they're just too effective that people get to comfortable with them being around to run things, leading to disaster in the event of their sudden removal? That's how the Maidens interpret Bureaucracy; those sabotage Charms aren't about execution, they're about a preemptive strike. Just look at the Scripture of the Maiden's Promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:08:15-07:00","id":206651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206623#post206623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes books just say dumb things. It's easy to get caught up in your subject matter and say something that doesn't make a lot of sense when pulled out of context.<br /> <br /> (I mean, not to pick a fight over that one line, but if you're going to hang your hat on that you're going to be disappointed. That quote is not and was never intended to be literally true, and if an author said otherwise they screwed up.)<br /> <br /> Astrology yes, learning no, and again, if you're going to focus on statements like that you're going to be disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I'm not 100% sure whether you have missed the thrust of my post somewhat.<br /> <br /> I actually don't care about these skills specifically, or them being the best at them. I don't mind if those specific skills, or any human skills really were dropped. Sidereals and Lunars could well be best at no skill at all. I agree with your post about about the problems of trying to hedge out &quot;This Exalt is best at this skill&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's the attitude of Sidereals and Lunars being generally enormously competent and a massive asset that made the First Age what it was that I'm interested in, and the general agnosticism about how much the Solars made the First Age and threatened the world all on their own, that this, the first and strongest expression of the core game made. Regardless of whether they were ever the best at any skill in willy waving contests about who's the best in the universe or not, which really isn't important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:27:58-07:00","id":206668,"title":"","content":"Disregarding all other texts, I have had a few thoughts regarding the new Edition having an idea of Lunars possessing the role of being guardians of the Realm (as a matter of appointment and relationship and a suitable common application for their particular talents, rather than Guardianship being part of their makeup), and the idea that this meant there were occasions in the history of the Realm where the Lunars collectively held more political power than the Solars. At the very least for having a greater unity of purpose than contemporary Solars might have had.<br /> <br /> I do think the writing needs to strike a suitable balance between the power of Exalted based on what they are, and on what they've done. It doesn't quite need to be unambiguous, but maybe a bit acknowledged. The Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted, but the Dragon Blooded are still the rulers of Creation (and even though the return of the Solars shakes the status quo, that doesn't necessarily mean that the Terrestrials aren't coming through the Time of Tumult with a lot of their prestige intact). Solars might have Charms that convey the motif of being the mightiest swordfighter in the world, but the actual title goes to... well, maybe any number of people based on all kinds of criteria, but generally folks who've won lots of sword fights, so it's still up for grabs by other Exalted (in a manner that doesn't fall neatly into &quot;winning by cheating&quot; or even &quot;winning despite not being as good&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:37:12-07:00","id":206672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206648#post206648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being that the Lunar were not the better but the more POWERFUL means that they had a nice is that role that even the solar could not fill. You send the solar in and he carefully negotiates and there is long back and forth.<br /> <br /> You send the lunar in and the person on the other side &quot;Must have&quot; wants &quot;now now now&quot; what ever it is your offering. That or the Lunar can always take plan be and force them to sign it by using sheer force. Lunar social ability in some ways in 2e is as good or even can outstripe Solar.<br /> <br /> The Solar are very good scholars and the Twilight have their things but the Sidereal have in some ways the ability eek out a little bit ahead of the solar. This doesn't diminish the Solar scholar who can skill achieve many great things but the sidereal can learn faster, same with the air aspected dragon blood. These two might not be able to do as many grand things with their knowelge but they can obtain the same knowledge levels as the solar faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is, again, that if you look at it like that (as a game of trying to find niches that &quot;even a Solar could not fill&quot; inside of areas a Solar would normally be presumed competent at) you risk turning Solars into the jack-of-all-trade, master-of-none Exalted as everything important gets claimed by someone else.<br /> <br /> Obviously a Sidereal or a Lunar can do things a Solar can't (there's no Solar charm quite like Efficient Secretary Technique, for instance); but in terms of overarching themes, I don't feel you can give Sidereals a generic &quot;Sidereals can learn faster than Solars&quot; statement without cutting too deeply into the Twilight caste -- and it would only take a few cuts like that to turn Twilights from masterful scholars to generic jack-of-all-trade scholars.<br /> <br /> Especially when your other example is that Lunars are as good or better than Solars at <i>social ability</i>, which is, uh. Look. Solar preeminence is the central conceit of the game. That doesn't mean that other people don't sometimes get better charms or specific tricks that exceed Solars, but in general the idea is that Solars are overwhelming in raw power or skill within their areas, and at straightforward expressions through those things; other Exalted define themselves according to more specific overarching narratives that are deliberately set up to be tangential to the Solar one -- and to each other -- in terms of their overall direction. It is this overall direction that gives you your broad area of competence as a Sidereal or a Lunar, not bits you carve off of the Solar Exalted. If you want to be the overall best scholar or emissary or whatever, you're probably best off with a Solar; if you want to be a mysterious sage of the stars, a hidden adviser or a secretive old master, you might be better off with a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> You'll have specific Sidereal charms to help you play a learned and wise character in your own unique Sidereal way, but the best ones (the ones, like Efficient Secretary Technique, that do things Solars don't) will generally have a unique Sidereal flavor. Efficient Secretary Technique is a Sidereal charm not because Jenna Moran said &quot;I'm going to make Sidereals even better at learning than Solars,&quot; it's a Sidereal charm because it operates via a weird cheaty mechanism that doesn't really make sense for anyone else, with broad efficient power at what it does but unusual limitations related to the Sidereal thematic (it doesn't just make the statement that Sidereals are wise, it makes the statement that they are wise in a specific unique Sidereal <i>way</i>.) So what you won't see is Solars getting a learning charm that learns at speed X, and then Sidereals getting a learning charm that just learns at speed X + 1 because lol let's give Sidereals the niche of learning faster.<br /> <br /> You're not entirely wrong in that Lunar emissaries are (notionally, at least) good at having a versatile skillset being able to switch tracks quickly -- especially from negotiation to violence -- but if you're talking &quot;best at raw social force&quot;, no. That's not part of how Lunars are defined anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:51:38-07:00","id":206683,"title":"","content":"This line about Lunars being &quot;the most powerful emissaries of the Exalted courts&quot; is interesting to look at in the context of early 1st Edition (possibly prior to the core coming out, but it certainly influenced it), where Lunars were conceived of as the &quot;insane and inimical allies of the Fair Folk,&quot; who had gone into exile beyond the edges of Creation. Kind of taking the role of &quot;emissaries&quot; to an extreme in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 07-23-2014, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T21:03:39-07:00","id":206753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206341#post206341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweeney Todd is a valid inspiration for a Solar</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that it's exactly germane, but he's almost a perfect template for an Abyssal now that I think about it - just replace &quot;shipped off to Australia&quot; with &quot;ganked in a back alley&quot; and you've got your whole story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T06:24:00-07:00","id":206981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206672#post206672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is, again, that if you look at it like that (as a game of trying to find niches that &quot;even a Solar could not fill&quot; inside of areas a Solar would normally be presumed competent at) you risk turning Solars into the jack-of-all-trade, master-of-none Exalted as everything important gets claimed by someone else.<br /> <br /> Obviously a Sidereal or a Lunar can do things a Solar can't (there's no Solar charm quite like Efficient Secretary Technique, for instance); but in terms of overarching themes, I don't feel you can give Sidereals a generic &quot;Sidereals can learn faster than Solars&quot; statement without cutting too deeply into the Twilight caste -- and it would only take a few cuts like that to turn Twilights from masterful scholars to generic jack-of-all-trade scholars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Air aspected Dragon Bloods already do this and as far as I know there is no solar charm for accelerating learning speed in your self. There is a war charm that let's you accelerating training an army, but that is about it. Are you saying that Twilight caste are marginalized by Air Aspect Dragon Bloods? The fact is that as scholars each and every Exalted has their own thing that they do differetly with their scholarly persuits. Solars can do far more powerful things with there scholarly pursuit with their wyld shapeing that other exalted can't. No mater how much a Dragon Blood pours over tomes he simply CANNOT do this. Every exalt type has a Niche within certain fields of their ability that the others do not fill as well. Solars do great things, Dragon Bloods learn things faster seeming to pull the knowelge in from the air it's self. The fact that each of them can do things the others do not does not diminish one or the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206672#post206672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when your other example is that Lunars are as good or better than Solars at <i>social ability</i>, which is, uh. Look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never meant this. I said in some aspects of social ability Lunar are better not in all aspects. Solar do things their way which is a very good, and unique way. It acheives it's results at it's pace, with it's own tools. Lunar have their own tools. One of those tools let's them ensure that they play to the primal desires in others. Making them lust for either the product you are selling, or for the diplomat sen to them who is willing to trade a few days of sex with them (which you want oh so badly) for your signature on the peace treaty. Solar are fare more refined about how they go about things. Their work is much more clean, crisp, and without loopholes. Being the most powerful does not mean being the best, or even being better at something. It means you can brute force your way though it with little to no control.<br /> <br /> In all just because other exalted are either better at, a single aspect of an ability does not marginalize the others. Dragon Blood Learn faster, does not suddenly make an Air aspect the superior for using Lore. It simply means the Air aspect learns faster. the Solar still does more with his lore than the air aspect in being able to shape the wyld, transfer essence or will, or virtue channels to others. The Solar still has very solar things he can do with his lore that the Air Aspect can't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T06:24:06-07:00","id":206982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206753#post206753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that it's exactly germane, but he's almost a perfect template for an Abyssal now that I think about it - just replace &quot;shipped off to Australia&quot; with &quot;ganked in a back alley&quot; and you've got your whole story.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kinda falls into the idea that a single media character can inspire a plethora of Exalt types, depending on what parts of the character you are most inspired by and emphasize. Being a nasty revanchist git who murders his way to his ultimate foe isn't the sole purview of Abyssals after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T07:09:41-07:00","id":207033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206981#post206981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air aspected Dragon Bloods already do this and as far as I know there is no solar charm for accelerating learning speed in your self. There is a war charm that let's you accelerating training an army, but that is about it. Are you saying that Twilight caste are marginalized by Air Aspect Dragon Bloods?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I think concluding that there can be no Twilight Charm that enables learning at that sort of speed, because Air Aspects are &quot;the fast-learning Exalts,&quot; would be unwarranted.<br /> <br /> You can look at powers like Elemental Bolt or various bender-style Dragon-Blood powers and understand why Solars don't get them - elemental manipulation is not their thing. Solars don't generally get Charms to create a swarm of entangling, poisonous vines, or to shape the battlefield with tornadoes or spontaneous bulwarks of earth. These tasks are not in line with their themes - the closest they're likely to come is a Survival Charm to mitigate nearby hazards or construct shelter, and even then it's going to fall closer to &quot;angelic miracle&quot; than &quot;elemental manipulator.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, is there any particular reason that &quot;read and absorb the contents of this book at super-speed&quot; is outside the Solar paradigm? Well, no - that's an application of peerless mastery at scholarship, which is... kind of the Twilight's bag. That seems like the kind of thing a Solar absolutely could develop Charms to do, even if there aren't any published. (Which may not even be true - Harmonious Academic Methodology will let you buy a dot of Lore after a five-hour training montage.)<br /> <br /> The point is that you can't look at Charm lists and conclude that any specific thing they don't have a Charm for is necessarily someone else's bailiwick - that pretty literally misses the forest for the trees. Solar Charms derive from the overall Solar theme of &quot;surpassing excellence at all human endeavors,&quot; and their hypothetical Charm space has to be interpreted in a way that supports that thematic notion. The place where the other Exalted stand distinct is when they pursue something that <i>isn't</i> what we'd generally think of as a human endeavor, like &quot;become a primal shapeshifting monster,&quot; or &quot;command the elements,&quot; or &quot;weave the skein of Fate from the palace of the gods.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T07:34:16-07:00","id":207062,"title":"","content":"I agree with irked. Hopefully there will be enough charms in each ability for this edition that we won't randomly get holes in the solar charmset which are oddly filled by other exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T07:36:10-07:00","id":207065,"title":"","content":"That's what homebrew charms are for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T07:43:13-07:00","id":207070,"title":"","content":"Homebrew is great and everything, but if given the choice I'd rather not have to boost up DB charms to solar level, I find it difficult to get the balance right sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T08:23:52-07:00","id":207106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207033#post207033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, is there any particular reason that &quot;read and absorb the contents of this book at super-speed&quot; is outside the Solar paradigm? Well, no - that's an application of peerless mastery at scholarship, which is... kind of the Twilight's bag. That seems like the kind of thing a Solar absolutely could develop Charms to do, even if there aren't any published. (Which may not even be true - Harmonious Academic Methodology will let you buy a dot of Lore after a five-hour training montage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>and this charm exist, but is in Linguistics not in Lore<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T08:39:29-07:00","id":207127,"title":"","content":"Gayo,<br /> <br /> While I deeply respect your views on Exalted, I find I must disagree with your disagreement about the role of, basically, ethics in a game of Exalted. However, I do fully agree that the only way to handle these issues is starting from a point where the Solars are the most powerful Exalts. <br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted <i>are</i> Kings. They may not deserve it, but that's <i>what they are</i>. (Note: It's not necessarily <i>who</i> they are.) And yes, those Kings fell, and fell horribly, to the point that they <i>lost</i> the Mandate of Heaven (in a very Chinese sense). However, <i>unlike</i> the Chinese sense of the term, legitimacy was not conferred on their successors in the Shogunate or, worse, the Scarlet Empress. This is noted by the Ministry of Heaven's regard (or lack of it) for those successor states. Note: Being a King doesn't make you good (or evil). It makes you in charge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, the Solar Exalted are returning. Should everyone bend over for them? <i>Hell no</i>. Because while being Kings is in their Exaltation, does that make them <i>right? </i>Emphatically, <i>no</i>. This goes all the way back to Euthyphro where it is asked, &quot;Is something good because the gods will it?&quot; The answer in almost all Western (classical) ethical systems is no, because the alternative is arbitrary.<br /> <br /> I fully agree that everyone's reactions to the Solars is, 'How do I benefit from them?' But that's <i>their</i> reaction. What is the <i>Solar's </i>reaction? You have a human being who is basically given <i>phenomenal cosmic power</i>, and one of the core questions asked in the game, narratively speaking, is, &quot;What will the Solars do with their power?&quot; They're given little-to-no-guidance or <i>limits</i> on their power. So what do they use it for?<br /> <br /> I think this is what's behind the 'humanizing' aspects of Solars in 3E. What does it mean to be human? Are you defined by your limitations? Your actions? Your desires? All? None? With the Solars, you take away the limitations of being human... and nothing else. (Lunars increasingly lose their human shapes, Sidereals lose their Freedom, etc.) What happens? Is a 'human being without limits' still capable of doing human beings, or do you lose your humanity when you lose the limitations of humanity? Note that the setting and rules don't answer the question; they ask the players to answer it for their characters.<br /> <br /> These are all fascinating questions, and <i>should</i> be explored in a Solar game. I wish I could quote the 1E core book, but I'm fairly certain this is exactly what's called out.<br /> <br /> Now, this doesn't mean that they're 'good'. They can repeat the mistakes of the First Age. But that's not a guarantee. The Great Prophecy summarized several possibilities, and the Sidereals in their hubris and risk-aversion decided on the 'safer' option. If you reduce the Solar to 'most powerful splat' without tying it to ethical dilemmas, you just made a mockery of the pivotal event in Creation's history, the Usurpation. But that also doesn't mean that the Solars have some sort of <i>untainted</i> legitimacy that means people should not just do what they say, but be happy about it.<br /> <br /> With all respect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T08:39:45-07:00","id":207128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206672#post206672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] turning Solars into the jack-of-all-trade, master-of-none Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep repeating this phrase, but it occurs to me that their current status of Jack-of all-Trades, Undisputed-Master-of-Frickin'-EVERYTHING is arguably no less boring, and at <i>least</i> as problematic. I mean, to use an earlier example: why <i>can't</i> Sidereals be better than Solars at learning? Surely there's enough nuance to Solars that they could still be a viable choice of protagonist without hammering so hard on the Better Than You nail? (And if not, that too seems like a problem that needs addressing.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206982#post206982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kinda falls into the idea that a single media character can inspire a plethora of Exalt types, depending on what parts of the character you are most inspired by and emphasize. Being a nasty revanchist git who murders his way to his ultimate foe isn't the sole purview of Abyssals after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTrue enough.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Although the concept does lend itself particularly well to Abyssals.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T08:50:09-07:00","id":207139,"title":"","content":"The trick there is that solars as a whole are masters of everything, but an individual solar is not. So it's more Jack of All Trades Masters of Any They Put Their Minds To.<br /> <br /> A solar may go his entire life without learning a particular skill just because it bores the pants off him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:09:27-07:00","id":207214,"title":"","content":"That's really not much of a trick, considering that we're speaking of splats rather than characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:36:55-07:00","id":207241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206573#post206573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a para-canon ending to the Second Age, the First Edition Core goes with <i>&quot;it slipped inch by inch into barbarism and darkness, until one last catacylsm blotted it out forever. Yet in its sunset, it was a splendid thing, and glorious were the deeds of the Exalted&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> I think that conveys, fairly well, that the Solars were not certain to be Second Age's demise or destroyers, nor, alone, to be its uplifting. Neither of Chejop Kejak's nightmare scenarios have to out.<br /> <br /> (The end, the catacylsm, could come from a number of directions).<br /> <br /> For some reason that's got lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is important for presenting the setting to the players, because it sets the tone without straitjacketing everybody's games. But the people in the setting have not read the book. The driving conflict that the Solars create in the Second Age is absolutely tied to what they did in the First Age, and that defines how anyone in Creation with even a hearsay notion of the first Age and Usurpation relates to them. It's not literally about recreating the First Age's highs or lows, it's about the fact that the people who were responsible for those things are back, and so those things are now on the table again after a thousand years where everyone assumed they were gone forever. The fact that the game itself does not go out of its way to instruct you to make this the climactic dilemma of the Second Age does not mean that it isn't the defining dilemma of the return of the Solars, so much as it means that there is a lot going on and the return of the Solars might not (though also might) singlehandedly steer the Second Age to its conclusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207127#post207127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gayo,<br /> <br /> While I deeply respect your views on Exalted, I find I must disagree with your disagreement about the role of, basically, ethics in a game of Exalted. However, I do fully agree that the only way to handle these issues is starting from a point where the Solars are the most powerful Exalts.<br /> [snip because long]</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can meet a consensus there, yeah. I agree with most of this completely. For what it's worth, I respect that the game plays the moral cynicism with a light enough hand that you can basically just ignore it and everything still works properly. I think it's important to keep the bleak and cynical aspects within convenient reach of those who want them there, which means being careful not to make changes that damage them, but it's also important that you be able to play the Solar narrative (or, really, anyone else's) in totally straight and positive way without the game hassling you about it every step of the way. To a great extent I think this requires a light touch with detail, which is one of the reasons 2e had issues with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:45:13-07:00","id":207248,"title":"","content":"My point was that Solars have unfettered choice in their competencies. Being Masters of All might make the splat as a whole sound boring, but you aren't playing the splat as a whole, are you?<br /> <br /> You're taking the average of a splat with no real core theme, coming out with a homogeneous blob, and then throwing out the whole concept as boring. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:09:38-07:00","id":207284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207128#post207128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Although the concept does lend itself particularly well to Abyssals.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely, some media characters fit one role or another perfectly with minimal editing, my point being that with some editing, you could put them in another splat and not really notice a huge behavioral difference. And I'll say this too: I'm biased. :P I might be running a game for a friend whose Solar character is at least quite inspired by Sweeney Todd (killer barber, but more assassin, less killer-oriented-at-revenge). And certainly the concept does lend itself to Abyssals. I just don't like implications of &quot;Sweeney Todd as a Solar? You're just Doing It Wrong!&quot; Which, for what it's worth, I wasn't really getting from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T12:58:22-07:00","id":207431,"title":"","content":"Second ed does have the solar legitimacy thing down pretty well, don't they have crazy authority over the gods? Almost none of them know it of course but if anyone told them they have the authority to alter the prayer calendar not because they're the IO and will punch your face but because they're the boss? Or am I misremembering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T13:06:41-07:00","id":207433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207431#post207431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second ed does have the solar legitimacy thing down pretty well, don't they have crazy authority over the gods? Almost none of them know it of course but if anyone told them they have the authority to alter the prayer calendar not because they're the IO and will punch your face but because they're the boss? Or am I misremembering?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so? Maybe Way Back When, the Solar Deliberative had that authority through the Mandate of Heaven and maybe the Hierophant could alter the prayer calendar, but the Solar Deliberative doesn't exist anymore and in all likelihood will never exist again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T13:28:34-07:00","id":207471,"title":"","content":"I don't recall the Solar Exalted having any special dominion over the prayer calendar, given that IIRC it's a matter of the Immaculates saying, &quot;Faithful believers, next Saturn's Day will be the observance of Jack, god of the field. Several of our Dragon-Blooded bretheren will be present to ensure that proper formalities are observed, and to act as proper intermediaries. Previous announcements that we would be celebrating the loyal service of Bob, god of the nearby river, on that day have been found to be in error, although we would like to clarify that this does not necessarily connect with our poor fishing over the last season. Please be sure that your offerings are proper to the station of Jack, and that you remember your place as he remembers his and we ours. Failure to follow these strictures may result in remedial reincarnation.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...that went on longer than intended. The point is that as far as I know, the Solars would more or less be doing the exact same thing, although probably more easily and with more oomph, and possibly more charisma and intimidation to bring to bear as appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-24-2014, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T13:34:44-07:00","id":207476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=206650#post206650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like to think that the symbolism of the Constellations in general was based on the idea of a mysticism that was cynical rather than uplifting. It's most blatant with the Lovers, but it pops up all over. That popular idea about Solars, about how they're just too effective that people get to comfortable with them being around to run things, leading to disaster in the event of their sudden removal? That's how the Maidens interpret Bureaucracy; those sabotage Charms aren't about execution, they're about a preemptive strike. Just look at the Scripture of the Maiden's Promise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say &quot;unromantic, or professional, (yet compassionate and capable of joy)&quot; rather than cynical (and of course, yes, Serenity shows these contrasts best) but I don't basically disagree. <br /> <br /> (They are not big, certainly, on the power of the enthusiasm of the enthusiastic, the love of lovers, the virtue of the virtuous, and the optimism of the optimistic to infectiously break free from their bearers and remake the people and the world.)<br /> <br /> I think that's a great insight into the Scripture and the Charms. I don't know if I would say that is all we can know about the Maidens' collective attitude to Bureaucracy - we can also see their attitude in their decision to tie their chosen more firmly to the Celestial Bureaucracy than any of the other Exalted, and the endurance of the Bureau of Fate. <br /> <br /> It is what stern, vigilant Endings would see in Bureaucracy - she'd see the potential for it to become a means by which things fall to a close, and how the power of bringing endings through Bureaucracy can forstall and hasten that bringing to a close. The Maidens have vastly different personalities. <br /> <br /> Yet could the Maidens have chosen for Bureaucracy to fall in the House of any other Maiden? Did they choose, if they did choose, with the knowledge of what the Sidereals must be and must do? That's a religious question for Sidereals, I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:05:27-07:00","id":207624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207248#post207248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that Solars have unfettered choice in their competencies. Being Masters of All might make the splat as a whole sound boring, but you aren't playing the splat as a whole, are you?<br /> <br /> You're taking the average of a splat with no real core theme, coming out with a homogeneous blob, and then throwing out the whole concept as boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly - but no more so than the Masters-of-None argument to which I was responding.<br /> <br /> (For the record, I have no dog in this fight. Just passing by, and tossing in my two cents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:47:12-07:00","id":207702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207128#post207128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You keep repeating this phrase, but it occurs to me that their current status of Jack-of all-Trades, Undisputed-Master-of-Frickin'-EVERYTHING is arguably no less boring, and at <i>least</i> as problematic. I mean, to use an earlier example: why <i>can't</i> Sidereals be better than Solars at learning? Surely there's enough nuance to Solars that they could still be a viable choice of protagonist without hammering so hard on the Better Than You nail? (And if not, that too seems like a problem that needs addressing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The question in this case, I think, is, &quot;So what are the Solars?&quot;<br /> <br /> Right now, Solars have a very clear core theme: surpassing excellence at human endeavor (or some similar phrasing and concept). They have other, secondary themes (sunlight, for instance), but this is the one that drives their place in the setting, the logic of their Charms, etc. It's the first court of appeal when pulling together an idea for a new Solar power: &quot;Does this express surpassing excellence at a human endeavor?&quot; While we <i>could</i> make them protagonists without a clear narrative theme, it wouldn't exactly be an improvement to do so, right?<br /> <br /> So. Suppose we slice off, for the sake of argument, &quot;The Air Aspects are the fast-reading Exalts; Solars don't get fast-reading magic.&quot; Suppose we slice off a dozen other areas of human excellence and silo them in the other Exalts: &quot;Solars can't provoke desire, fear, or other raw emotions as well as Lunars. Solars can't teach people as fast or as thoroughly as Sidereals.&quot; Whatever.<br /> <br /> We still need a core theme for the Solars, and &quot;Surpassing excellence at an unpredictable grab-bag of human endeavors&quot; sure ain't gonna cut it. What do we replace it with?<br /> <br /> (There are answers that could be given to this question - others have suggested, for instance, &quot;Leadership.&quot; And the Solars could have been made the Leadership Exalted, sure - at the cost of making the default play splat out-of-theme for anyone who doesn't want to play a god-king. What answer do you give that's simple enough to understand, without pigeonholing the default character types? Because that's the advantage of &quot;Surpassing excellence at human endeavor&quot;: it's easy to get across, and it enables basically every human-ish larger-than-life heroic archetype. Superman? Odysseus? Achilles? Gilgamesh? King Arthur? King Solomon? Hercules? Sherlock Holmes? Enzio? Sun Tzu? Easy to translate to Solars, and with powers that say, &quot;Yes, you <i>are</i> the embodiment of the swordsman/the trickster/the detective/the king/the scholar/the strongman/the general/the <i>whatever men can be</i>.&quot; That's a powerful thing, when trying to get someone interested in the game, and it's a thing arguably worth preserving.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:08:39-07:00","id":207732,"title":"","content":"I like the &quot;Surpassing excellence at human endeavor&quot;, because it allows other splats to be &quot;better&quot; in a non-human way.<br /> Solars are fast learners that can read and teach at amazing levels.. Sure, but a Sidereal can take on the destiny of a warrior and just know how to fight while wearing that destiny - he never &quot;learnt&quot; the skill, and it might go away if he doesn't pretend in the right way, but it is an instant thing vs the solar learning things faster... (as a poor example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/37-dionysus","name":"Dionysus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar37_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:17:33-07:00","id":207740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207128#post207128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep repeating this phrase, but it occurs to me that their current status of Jack-of all-Trades, Undisputed-Master-of-Frickin'-EVERYTHING is arguably no less boring, and at <i>least</i> as problematic. I mean, to use an earlier example:<b> why <i>can't</i> Sidereals be better than Solars at learning?</b> Surely there's enough nuance to Solars that they could still be a viable choice of protagonist without hammering so hard on the Better Than You nail? (And if not, that too seems like a problem that needs addressing.)[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>they arent the best at learning, but the have the best libraries in Creation<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:36:51-07:00","id":207791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207732#post207732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the &quot;Surpassing excellence at human endeavor&quot;, because it allows other splats to be &quot;better&quot; in a non-human way.<br /> Solars are fast learners that can read and teach at amazing levels.. Sure, but a Sidereal can take on the destiny of a warrior and just know how to fight while wearing that destiny - he never &quot;learnt&quot; the skill, and it might go away if he doesn't pretend in the right way, but it is an instant thing vs the solar learning things faster... (as a poor example)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think that's a bad example at all. The Sidereal is not better at soldiering, or better at learning to soldier, but he is better at <i>stealing the fate of a soldier</i> - because that's not anything like a thing humans do, and so it's not a thing Solars do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:08:47-07:00","id":207913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207732#post207732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the &quot;Surpassing excellence at human endeavor&quot;, because it allows other splats to be &quot;better&quot; in a non-human way.<br /> Solars are fast learners that can read and teach at amazing levels.. Sure, but a Sidereal can take on the destiny of a warrior and just know how to fight while wearing that destiny - he never &quot;learnt&quot; the skill, and it might go away if he doesn't pretend in the right way, but it is an instant thing vs the solar learning things faster... (as a poor example)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I think this might be the crux of all the &quot;I hate solars&quot; sentiment. In my experience when people build a character, they tend to think in terms of board archetypes. &quot;I am a great general who wants to lead her nation to greatness&quot; &quot;I am a shrewd diplomat to wants to establish peace through a complex web of inter-dependent trade&quot; &quot;I am a cunning rogue who want to make a fast buck&quot;, etc etc.<br /> <br /> The problem here is twofold: First, Solars were specifically made with these archetypes in mind. They are intended to be the very best at these things, and to perform at them better than anyone else, as is their nature as the &quot;exemplary human skill&quot; Exalted.<br /> <br /> Secondly, and more importantly, people have a favored Exalt-type that is NOT a Solar, but will still try to make them fit in to a playstyle that they were not designed for. A Sidereal for example is not meant to be a great general, a shrewd diplomat or a cunning rogue. They can certainly have a go at it, but Sidereals are intended to be (among other things) the &quot;men in black&quot; Exalted. They are the tacticians and strategists, the behind the scenes manipulators and the spies and assassins. Trying to force them to fill a roll that they aren't intended to fulfill will end up being unsatisfying because their charmset and thematics are build around the sideways and indirect approach, thanks to the fact that Fate and the Maidens who run it are very much sideways and indirect things/gods. As a result of their favorite Exalt not being able to satisfactorily full the role that they've chosen, they tend to view Solars with animosity and start demanding that their favorite Exalt type be brought in to parity with the Solars, all the while failing to realize that they're trying to make a square peg fill a round hole.<br /> <br /> In short, the classic archetypes are reserved for Solars, because the classic archetypes are prime examples of exemplary human skill, which is a core theme of the Solar Exalted. Trying to force a Sidereal a Lunar or a Dragon-Blooded in to these roles is possible, but since you are trying to work out of your native themes, you are going to be much more limited and have a harder time getting the results you wanted, and will be left feeling unsatisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 07-25-2014, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T23:47:23-07:00","id":207962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=205495#post205495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been wrong before, though; since you usually <i>can't</i> take an entire White Wolf line as a single face-value piece, I tend to just glide over the dumb things I can't use.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'd much rather break a bottle over the head of the dumb things, shove the broken glass in their face, drown it in the toilet and bury it in a shallow grave by the side of the Interstate.<br /> <br /> ...you may be more patient and forgiving than I am.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207913#post207913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, the classic archetypes are reserved for Solars, because the classic archetypes are prime examples of exemplary human skill, which is a core theme of the Solar Exalted. Trying to force a Sidereal a Lunar or a Dragon-Blooded in to these roles is possible, but since you are trying to work out of your native themes, you are going to be much more limited and have a harder time getting the results you wanted, and will be left feeling unsatisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><i>Anti-life justifies my hate...anti-life justifies my hate...</i></span><br /> <br /> Jay...I find the concept of UNIVERSAL ARCHETYPES to be the sole and exclusive dominion of Solars to be...<i>problematic</i>, let's say. Particularly for a roleplaying game. Because, ya'know, of the whole <i>universal</i> aspect there...&quot;There's nothing new under the sun,&quot; hah, sort of thing?<br /> <br /> I mean, it seems like you're basically arguing that doing <i>anything ever</i> with non-Solars is &quot;trying to make them fit a playstyle there weren't designed for&quot; because damn near everything, if not actually everything, can potentially fall under the auspicious of these classical archetypes you're cordoning off exclusively for Solars.<br /> <br /> I mean, you want to talk about why people dislike Solars...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:10:48-07:00","id":207969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207962#post207962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jay...I find the concept of UNIVERSAL ARCHETYPES to be the sole and exclusive dominion of Solars to be...<i>problematic</i>, let's say. Particularly for a roleplaying game. Because, ya'know, of the whole <i>universal</i> aspect there...&quot;There's nothing new under the sun,&quot; hah, sort of thing?<br /> <br /> I mean, it seems like you're basically arguing that doing <i>anything ever</i> with non-Solars is &quot;trying to make them fit a playstyle there weren't designed for&quot; because damn near everything, if not actually everything, can potentially fall under the auspicious of these classical archetypes you're cordoning off exclusively for Solars.<br /> <br /> I mean, you want to talk about why people dislike Solars...</div> </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;classic&quot; not &quot;universal&quot;. To invoke DnD for a second, &quot;The Fighter&quot; &quot;The Wizard&quot; &quot;The Rogue&quot; &quot;The Cleric&quot; and &quot;The Bard&quot; are all archetypes that map perfectly to the Dawn, Twilight, Night, Zenith and Eclipse Caste. They are Achilles, Merlin, Robin Hood, Orpheus, and Odysseus, Iconic representations of specific narrative archetypes. &quot;The Barbarian&quot; and &quot;The Sorcerer&quot; are more focused and specialized variants of those archetypes, and relate to Lunars (Full Moon) and Sidereals (Chosen of Secrets), respectively.<br /> <br /> Saying that Solars have exclusive rights to ALL archetypes is stupid and wrong, which is exactly why I didn't say it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:54:42-07:00","id":207986,"title":"","content":"I suspect Coik's problem is to do with the fact that Solars are <i>also</i> better at being &quot;The Barbarian&quot; and &quot;The Sorcerer&quot; - although truth be told I'm not sure how you'd relate Sorcerers and Siddies to begin with, Sorcerers being all about mastering internal potential and all.<br /> <br /> (Now that I think about it, hasn't Conan been listed in the books as a source of inspiration for Solars at least once? Or am I just mis-attributing something I read on the old forums?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:03:35-07:00","id":207989,"title":"","content":"I never got why Siddies were supposed to be &quot;the sorcerer&quot; because they don't even get the top rung. Sorcery has <i>always</i> been the solars' thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:45:22-07:00","id":208009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207128#post207128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep repeating this phrase, but it occurs to me that their current status of Jack-of all-Trades, Undisputed-Master-of-Frickin'-EVERYTHING is arguably no less boring, and at <i>least</i> as problematic. I mean, to use an earlier example: why <i>can't</i> Sidereals be better than Solars at learning? Surely there's enough nuance to Solars that they could still be a viable choice of protagonist without hammering so hard on the Better Than You nail? (And if not, that too seems like a problem that needs addressing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars aren't masters at everything, but they are masters at everything <i>Solar</i>, which encompasses every field of human endeavor and most of the basic archetypes for purely human heroes. They are not necessarily entirely peerless at everything in those fields (like I said, Sidereals might be able to match Solars at learning in certain ways, and have powers that exceed them in others), but the basic premise of the game is that Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted, and that this might is expressed in the basic thematics of their 25 abilities and 5 castes.<br /> <br /> Therefore, while your Sidereal might be wiser in certain ways, or more knowledgeable about certain things, you're not going to be better at generalized learning than the Twilight caste; and the areas where Sidereals (or other splats) do things Solars don't will generally be by going outside the bounds of humanity or by exploring specific concepts unique to themselves.<br /> <br /> The nuance and depth any individual Lore-focused Twilight caste character has is going to come from their personal story, background, and goals, combined with the way that their powers burn these things onto the world; but their definition <i>as a Twilight</i> is that they bring a level of scholarship to the world that it has not seen since the fall of the First Age. That's the core definition of what they are, in the same way that Sidereals are astrologers and advisers and martial-artists; it doesn't mean that those Twilights are the only supernaturally-talented scholars, or that there's nobody capable of competing with them, or that Sidereals can't have tricks they don't, but it means that no, none of the Exalted are going to be overall better than them at the broadly-defined field of &quot;learning.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're talking about this as though they're MMoRPG classes, like you can nerf Twilights <i>a bit</i> at this and they'll still be viable, or as if scholarship is just a number on a sheet that can be moved around a bit. That's not what splats are for. They tell specific stories, and the Twilight story is fundamentally about being the greatest scholar. You can still beat them at that (just like you can beat Dawn who strives to be the greatest swordsman), but...<br /> <br /> Let me use the Dawn as an example, because I think that's clearer. If you wanted to beat the Invincible Sword Princess using another splat, what would you do? How would that story go? I mean, there's lots of ways. and it's certainly not impossible to just beat her at her own game -- but I think that the most logical path, for any non-Solar, is going to at some point involve leveraging their talents at things other than swordsmanship. You can build a Lunar who can beat the Invincible Sword Princess at a swordfight, but if you don't involve some thematically uniquely Lunar power in that fight, you're fighting with one hand tied behind your back, so you're going to be at a disadvantage. That isn't (just) because the Invincible Sword Princess is the best at swording -- it's because, while you can make an utterly lethal Lunar swordsman, the overall thrust of the Lunar charmset isn't <i>about</i> swording and doesn't really contain trees that are purely focused on that, so if you, say, took a bunch of strength and dexterity charms and used them only for swords (and ignored all parts of the trees that don't apply to swords) you're not going to be using them at full capacity.<br /> <br /> Which is a roundabout way of saying that, more than just their power or preeminence -- if you want to describe the overarching design and thematics of each splat, you shouldn't focus on comparisons with Solars at a Solar narrative, because nobody's charmset but Solars tells purely Solar narratives. You can make a lethal Lunar swordsman or a learned Sidereal scholar (and both those things overlap heavily with the core of their narratives, so they're going to be very good at it), but thematically and magically, a Lunar is more than just a simple swordsman and a Sidereal is more than just a simple scholar; they may have some charms that help a lot at those things, but the overarching thrust of their charmsets is slightly different from that, whereas the Solar charmset expresses those concepts squarely.<br /> <br /> That is why Sidereals cannot be better than Solars at learning. The Secrets caste knows a lot of things (in some ways, more than a Twilight, even before you start to talk about the setting's default state), but their overarching definition is aimed at a subtly different target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-25-2014, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:46:40-07:00","id":208010,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207702#post207702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Suppose we slice off, for the sake of argument, &quot;The Air Aspects are the fast-reading Exalts; Solars don't get fast-reading magic.&quot; Suppose we slice off a dozen other areas of human excellence and silo them in the other Exalts: &quot;Solars can't provoke desire, fear, or other raw emotions as well as Lunars. Solars can't teach people as fast or as thoroughly as Sidereals.&quot; Whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't an amazing idea. <br /> <br /> However sitting down and writing Solar magic to be able to mean that they are the best at every trick isn't necessary either really. That would be a bad idea which would leave them a flavourless balance of mush who might have more advantage over other Exalted than they should have for the game to make sense and feel right.<br /> <br /> The Solars should only get the tricks the writers are inspired to give them, at a strength balanced with how powerful they are generally supposed to be which should generally leave them stronger than others in a specifically Solar feeling way that cleaves to their inspirations. That might mean they might not have the fastest &quot;fast learning&quot; Charm, for an example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207732#post207732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the &quot;Surpassing excellence at human endeavor&quot;, because it allows other splats to be &quot;better&quot; in a non-human way.<br /> Solars are fast learners that can read and teach at amazing levels.. Sure, but a Sidereal can take on the destiny of a warrior and just know how to fight while wearing that destiny - he never &quot;learnt&quot; the skill, and it might go away if he doesn't pretend in the right way, but it is an instant thing vs the solar learning things faster... (as a poor example)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a pretty cool example, but I would say that <br /> <br /> a) generally Sidereals get more distinctive approaches, that are allowed to be more overtly sorcerous and follows particular patterns, to make them powerful at goals within their ability because having less overlap when possible makes them feel more unique. Not always possible though, and making them feel extremely competent, cool people who are have abilities that are like human but more is much more important than &quot;zero overlap&quot;.<br /> <br /> b) learning to take on the destiny of a warrior in this way is a cool, powerful expression of human ability to learn and understand, fuelled by effort, experience and Ability prerequistites. It's not cheating or stealing and he's not a character we're to understand as &quot;faking it&quot; and deserving a comeupance.<br /> <br /> If we can't deal with the Sidereal learning to be a great soldier (perhaps not as strong as a Solar) through his own ability magic without viewing it as some kind of cheating, I think it will be hard to deal with the possibility of an Exigent character who picks up say, Ten Sheaves themed expressions of her ability, becomes as comparably strong at it a Solar and regularly bests Solars (even perhaps the best Solar) at that ability. <br /> <br /> If we were then approaching that character through the mindset that she was cheating rather than that she was an awesome warrior uplifted through a force quite different to that which picks up Solars, then we'd be unnecessarily putting a cynical slant on things that would wreck our enjoyment by making us feel a character who fairly was supreme... wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T02:09:11-07:00","id":208020,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing, though: it is perfectly viable to build those other archetypes as other types of Exalts. Most of them will approach them through the lens of their themes, some can't quite cover all of those archetypes without approaching them in odd ways. The fact that all of these Exalts have weaknesses and things they can't do makes them all interesting.<br /> <br /> The exception is Solars. Solars can do everything, and they can do it better than anyone else. The only things they can't do aren't important because they have different, usually better ways of doing anything those things enable you to do. They don't need to be able to shapeshift because they have better, faster ways of doing almost anything you would use shapeshifting in order to do. They don't need to be able to manipulate Fate because they can already manipulate people and groups to do what they want much more easily than having to work around the restrictions of Fate manipulation. In a game where everyone else is made interesting by their restrictions as much as their powers, Solars are the guys without any restrictions. As a result they're boring at the same time as they take away from everyone else by making it Doing It Wrong to build a Lunar out to become a skilled swordsman because nope, being skilled isn't using your powers effectively and together with your mundane prowess, it's having Solar powers. Everyone else's powers aren't real skills, they're ways of cheating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","user":"Couch","date":". 07-25-2014, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:05:17-07:00","id":208060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208010#post208010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is a pretty cool example, but I would say that<br /> <br /> b) learning to take on the destiny of a warrior in this way is a cool, powerful expression of human ability to learn and understand, fuelled by effort, experience and Ability prerequistites. It's not cheating or stealing and he's not a character we're to understand as &quot;faking it&quot; and deserving a comeupance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wanted to jump in on this point.<br /> - The Solar's excellence is in &quot;learning how to fight as a man, but surpasses the ability to fight as a man&quot; - ie, he picks up a sword, learns that the pointy end goes in the enemy, and practices (even if only for a short time).<br /> - The Siderial learns how to take other destinys (or some other such thing). Something that is literally impossible for humans to do. The Siddie has learnt something awesome, but the method is something outside of human endeavor - Siddies are the &quot;men behind the scenes&quot;, they learn how to pull the strings, open the doors that humans never get to.<br /> <br /> Same thing could be applied to Lunars. I always took them to be the &quot;attribute exalted&quot;: They change themselves to be inhuman so that they can excel. So in a raw test of strength, the Solar will loose out to a Lunar - because no matter how strong a human can get, there are monsters out there that can beat them without breaking a sweat. A human vs an elephant - the elephant can lift more (until the human tries to apply human ingenuity... then they can win) Same with any kind of survival - sure you can hold your breath for an incredible amount of time, but the Lunar can damn well breath water like a fish!<br /> <br /> That is why i dont quite understand all this kerfuffle about solars vs other exalts. Solars are the best at human excellence - If you can imagine a human doing something, take it to 11 for a Solar. But the other exalts, they do INHUMAN things - Lunars change to take on traits of the natural and supernatural world, Siderials cheat destiny, DragonBloods manipulate elements and enhance others around them. Alchemicals are machines. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/37-dionysus","name":"Dionysus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar37_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:10:48-07:00","id":208069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208020#post208020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, though: it is perfectly viable to build those other archetypes as other types of Exalts. Most of them will approach them through the lens of their themes, some can't quite cover all of those archetypes without approaching them in odd ways. The fact that all of these Exalts have weaknesses and things they can't do makes them all interesting.<br /> <br /> The exception is Solars. Solars can do everything, and they can do it better than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the thing - Solars CANT do everything. They can only do things that a human could do, but do it at an incredible level. And more importantly, a single solar can not to everything... The restrictions of a solar are internal - they are humans turned up to 11, so all their problems are human problems.<br /> <br /> If you want to beat a Lunar, or Siddie, or whatever, you throw a problem at them that is &quot;outside scope&quot; for their powers.<br /> If you want to beat a Solar, you find their human flaw and exploit that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone else's powers aren't real skills, they're ways of cheating. </div> </div> </div>Actually, thats sorta the point... a Lunar's power isn't skill - its natural ability - strength, speed, endurance etc... same with the others. They are &quot;powers&quot;, not skills. While the Solars are explicitly about skills.<br /> <br /> If you want a character that is all about surviving, enduring, travelling, becoming anything and everywhere - be a Lunar as a solar cannot compete.<br /> If you want to know the future, know the &quot;cheat codes&quot;, know the hidden secrets, be a &quot;secret agent&quot; - be a Siderial<br /> If you want to control the elements, be part of an ass-kicking brotherhood - be a Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":37,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/37-dionysus","user":"Dionysus","date":".  additional thoughts... 07-25-2014, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/37-dionysus","name":"Dionysus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar37_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:24:05-07:00","id":208091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208069#post208069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, thats sorta the point... a Lunar's power isn't skill - its natural ability - strength, speed, endurance etc... same with the others. They are &quot;powers&quot;, not skills. While the Solars are explicitly about skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Dragonblooded using Essence to make throwing knives out of fire is using powers to make up for a lack of skills, Solars using Essence to make throwing knives out of golden fire is a pure expression of their skills. Got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:30:16-07:00","id":208094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208091#post208091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Dragonblooded using Essence to make throwing knives out of fire is using powers to make up for a lack of skills, Solars using Essence to make throwing knives out of golden fire is a pure expression of their skills. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah.. some of those solar powers are &quot;cheat&quot; powers.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/37-dionysus","name":"Dionysus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar37_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:46:34-07:00","id":208102,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the concept that Solar powers are really nothing but expressions of their pure skills and not just magic like everyone else's magic is bullshit. You won the lottery, you got a chunk of Essence shoved into your soul and now you're Superman. Own up to it, don't pretend you're Batman doing his mundane guy thing and beating up all those losers who have to rely on superpowers, not like you with your pure expressions of human skill. You're not Batman in any sense other than that the writers love you and will make sure you're always the favorite to win. Which they do in Exalted by giving you all the powers of Superman, but without any of the things that make Superman a likable character. And with nothing like Kryptonite because having weaknesses is for dweebs who have to cheat.<br /> <br /> Basically what I'm saying is that Solars are simultaneously everything wrong with Superman and everything wrong with Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:47:14-07:00","id":208103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208060#post208060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wanted to jump in on this point.<br /> - The Solar's excellence is in &quot;learning how to fight as a man, but surpasses the ability to fight as a man&quot; - ie, he picks up a sword, learns that the pointy end goes in the enemy, and practices (even if only for a short time).<br /> - The Siderial learns how to take other destinys (or some other such thing). Something that is literally impossible for humans to do. The Siddie has learnt something awesome, but the method is something outside of human endeavor - Siddies are the &quot;men behind the scenes&quot;, they learn how to pull the strings, open the doors that humans never get to.<br /> <br /> Same thing could be applied to Lunars. I always took them to be the &quot;attribute exalted&quot;: They change themselves to be inhuman so that they can excel. So in a raw test of strength, the Solar will loose out to a Lunar - because no matter how strong a human can get, there are monsters out there that can beat them without breaking a sweat. A human vs an elephant - the elephant can lift more (until the human tries to apply human ingenuity... then they can win) Same with any kind of survival - sure you can hold your breath for an incredible amount of time, but the Lunar can damn well breath water like a fish!<br /> <br /> That is why i dont quite understand all this kerfuffle about solars vs other exalts. Solars are the best at human excellence - If you can imagine a human doing something, take it to 11 for a Solar. But the other exalts, they do INHUMAN things - Lunars change to take on traits of the natural and supernatural world, Siderials cheat destiny, DragonBloods manipulate elements and enhance others around them. Alchemicals are machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in our world mastery of destiny is inhuman. Although in Exalted's world mortals can learn thaumaturgy with an astrological bent - prediction, etc.<br /> <br /> The other Exalted learn to do feats which are not really human, as such. But they use human effort, will and persistance to fairly win these powers, and they use these powers in the pursuit of human goals and excellence. <br /> <br /> The non-Solar Exalts are a lot like Solar sorcerors or mortal thaumaturges (or masters of evocations?) that way - they're learning these arcane powers which aren't human, really, but they're using human will, drive, persistence, ability and intelligence to master them, and they're learning them so that they can achieve human goals and what humans would regard as mighty deeds that will change the world.<br /> <br /> Re: powers and skills and magic, the difference between a power and skill and magic to me (which might be different from everyone else's mental definition), is that a power isn't learned, it doesn't involve effort and knowledge and the mind, it isn't won. So in that sense Sidereal and Lunar powers are absolutely *not* powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:55:04-07:00","id":208105,"title":"","content":"I think maybe part of the problem here is that the previous edition was broken, but had people saying the same things. Like when a supposedly challenging circle of immaculate essence 5 DBs god soloed by the Dawn while everyone else watches, or when a night caste ninja knocked out you and your whole lunar circle without effort. Then you see on the forums &quot;of course that happened, Solars are the most powerful!&quot;. When really there should be some doubt as to the outcome of that fight and if one night caste wants to capture four Lunars at once he'd better pull out all the stops and even then might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:44:42-07:00","id":208148,"title":"","content":"Instead of going round and round rehashing the same arguments over and over again and theorycrafting, why don't we try and give examples from real campaigns.<br /> <br /> Now, we have played several mixed campaigns with a majority of the PC's being solars.<br /> <br /> I played a social Chosen of Serenity in a party with a social Solar. Vastly different play-experience from the solar. The Serenity was a whole lot better at behind the scenes manipulation than the Solar could ever be. She could build up or tear down support without ever being known while the Solar always needed to be seen. It was also much, much easier on the xp to be competent in important area's (information gathering, infiltration, combat) while not losing your social focus. Oh, and having access to Yu-Shan and it's recources is also a major gamechanger. I certainly did not feel underpowered.<br /> <br /> I had a similar experience with a Pretty Kitty social Lunar. Again, in raw mass-influencing social mojo, the Solar has the edge, no question. But in smaller scale situations, and especially if subtlety and deniability were even remotely required, send in the Lunar. Also, similar to the sidereal, it was much cheaper to be competent in other area's as well as the social arena. I was having a different experience, which I felt I could not have with a Solar. I was not weaker than the Solars and the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded, while definately not having the same powerlevel as the Celestials, especially in combat, bring plenty of other, unique things to the table that the Anathema by their very nature cannot. I certainly had fun playing one in a Solar party, though yes, you will feel weaker if some niche-protection is not observed. But even then, the fact that you're simply not an anathema, though not as easily quantifiable as the strenth of your charm-set or shapeshifting, is a pretty big advantage.<br /> <br /> In our current party we have a Full Moon Lunar combat wombat. He has other strengths than my Dawn Invincible Sword Princess. He is more invested in protecting others, taking the blows and regerating and slowly grinding oponents down than the quick win. I have the edge in a straight one on one fight against him (not a guaranteed win though in 2.5), but hey, he is built to be the big guy/bear protecting everybody else and he is certainly better at that then my character (or any solar can be, really).<br /> <br /> We also briefly had an Alchemical at the table. If he went for his specialised load-outs he could compete with the Solars in combat or in the sneaky stealthy scout department. It definately looked like a different play-experience, but I did not get see much of it, so can't fully say how they compare or where their strenths really lie in comparison to Solars.<br /> <br /> TL/DR: Play to your splat's strengths and your character will not be weaker than your friend's solar (if you use the same xp &amp; advancement tables). You are probably much broader in capabilties, thanks to shapeshifting/fate stuff/arrays for the same xp. Solars really can't do everything at once in actual play. Even then, Solar's are not very subtle in most areas, being golden, shiny leadertypes, while Lunars and Sidereals certainly can be. Play to the splat's strengths and you'll be just fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:49:00-07:00","id":208154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208103#post208103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The non-Solar Exalts are a lot like Solar sorcerors or mortal thaumaturges (or masters of evocations?) that way - they're learning these arcane powers which aren't human, really, but they're using human will, drive, persistence, ability and intelligence to master them, and they're learning them so that they can achieve human goals and what humans would regard as mighty deeds that will change the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>totally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/37-dionysus","name":"Dionysus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar37_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T05:54:14-07:00","id":208204,"title":"","content":"Interestingly enough, they only invented Kryptonite to justify <i>radio show</i> Superman being unable to save the day when his voice-actor was indisposed, on vacation, et cetera. The idea was then ported over into the comics. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T06:44:54-07:00","id":208244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207989#post207989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got why Siddies were supposed to be &quot;the sorcerer&quot; because they don't even get the top rung. Sorcery has <i>always</i> been the solars' thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a several different people use this argument. Here's the thing though, Sids are the sorerous archtype because they don't actually need Sorcery (at least in terms of Exalted's mechanics) to get spell-like effects.<br /> <br /> The confusion is that the kind of magic Exalted calls Sorcery is different from the magic that the archtypical sorcerer uses. In D&amp;D, the big difference between a sorcerer and a wizard is that wizards learn spells whereas sorcerers are born with them and use them as innate magic. In the same way, Sidereal charms/astrology can summon elementals, banish demons, magically heal, and create magical disguises. Sidereals can't use exalted's sorcery to summon a 3rd Cicle demon, but they could make a go at it with their charms. They could use sorcery to caste a giant flaming bird at someone, but it would be cheaper to load a lit candle into their powerbow and shoot that. So no, Sids aren't as good at using Exalted's version of sorcery as Solars. Compared to other splats, though, this shortcoming affects them the least since their native charms can, in part, bridge the gap.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:35:48-07:00","id":208292,"title":"","content":"Going back to 1E Lunars and Abyssals, I think part of the problem was that nearly all their powers were &quot;like Solars, but a little bit worse&quot;. It wasn't until Sidereals &amp; Alchemicals that the rules actually backed up the idea of &quot;good in a different way&quot;, rather than &quot;sub-Solar&quot;. If you were a Lunar, you were strong-armed into taking Deadly Beastman Transformation, because it was the only thing you could do better than a Solar (including shapeshifting into other people!)<br /> <br /> And then the 2E Manuals did the same thing again by botching Sidereals and Abyssals. I'd wager one of the reasons Infernals was so popular was that again, it did &quot;You're as good as a Solar, in a novel and interesting way.&quot; rather than &quot;You're worse than a Solar, deal.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:40:28-07:00","id":208299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207969#post207969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said &quot;classic&quot; not &quot;universal&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of this discussion I consider the difference to be largely semantical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To invoke DnD for a second, &quot;The Fighter&quot; &quot;The Wizard&quot; &quot;The Rogue&quot; &quot;The Cleric&quot; and &quot;The Bard&quot; are all archetypes that map perfectly to the Dawn, Twilight, Night, Zenith and Eclipse Caste. </div> </div> </div>The problem is still the same...I mean, that's the thing about them being <i>archetypes</i>. They're general, and you can pretty easily argue any character into them. That's why my D&amp;D 5e intro set has Fighters, Wizards, Clerics and Rogues as the class options instead of Wu-Jen or Bladesingers...they're non-specific enough that any adventurer concept you can come up with can be molded to them without too much trouble.<br /> <br /> And, well...Barbarians are really just Fighters. Sorcerers are really just Wizards. I don't feel dropping synonyms and calling them distinct character identities really works, because then you're pretty much just right back to saying that any non-Solar doing anything ever is doing it wrong, because Solars already have all design space reserved for them by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:52:07-07:00","id":208313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208292#post208292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then the 2E Manuals did the same thing again by botching Sidereals and Abyssals. I'd wager one of the reasons Infernals was so popular was that again, it did &quot;You're as good as a Solar, in a novel and interesting way.&quot; rather than &quot;You're worse than a Solar, deal.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh let's not just stop there. Lunar Charms have too-high prereqs and too-high costs, implemented as a sort of balance because they could throw Solar-level-ish PDs and social effects. Not to mention they have no real theme. DB mechanics were a huge mess until TCA errata'd them, much like Sidereals. And it was why GSPs were so popular: for years and years, Solars were the only splat with a really working Charmset <i>and </i>free reign of choice for gameplay (the Abyssal book saying you're Doing It Wrong if you don't fit a certain play style, the punishment being Resonance; Lunars having no themes, and the rest having awful mechanics). Plus you had stratified power tiers and a mindset of &quot;if Solars are the best and if Solars have the most functional mechanics, why play anything else?&quot; So it was natural that people would get tired of playing Solars, when each new splatbook was bad, and when GSPs came out they were on the Solar power level but felt completely different, hence the popularity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:21:38-07:00","id":208353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208010#post208010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't an amazing idea.<br /> <br /> However sitting down and writing Solar magic to be able to mean that they are the best at every trick isn't necessary either really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying they should be the best at every trick. I'm saying they should be the best at every field of human endeavor. That doesn't mean you have to literally read through every Charm of every other Exalt type and add one to all of the numerical effects - again, no one thinks Solars should have Even More Efficient Secretary as a Charm. But it does mean that you run into problems when you want to parse, say, learning, and conclude, &quot;Oh, these other Exalts will always be <i>faster</i>,&quot; or whatever. &quot;Can read fast&quot; is a pretty straightforward application of being the Bestest Scholar Ever; that makes it an unlikely nail to hang someone else's hat on.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want, say, a Fire-Aspect or Abyssal Charm where you burn down a library and absorb the knowledge as the books go up in smoke - well, okay! Solars aren't going to have that, because that's not really about <i>learning</i>, it's about your connection to elemental fire or to destruction. (One might quibble whether this is an appropriate Charm for either of those splats, but that's not really my major point.) Perhaps that's a means by which you could end up with the effect of absorbing information faster, but it's not because they're the Learning Exalts more than Solars are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:34:39-07:00","id":208366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207962#post207962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jay...I find the concept of UNIVERSAL ARCHETYPES to be the sole and exclusive dominion of Solars to be...<i>problematic</i>, let's say. Particularly for a roleplaying game. Because, ya'know, of the whole <i>universal</i> aspect there...&quot;There's nothing new under the sun,&quot; hah, sort of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Universal&quot; and &quot;classic&quot; aren't really the same thing at all here, though - particularly because, if I'm reading Jay correctly, he means &quot;classic&quot; specifically in the sense of &quot;classic heroic archetypes,&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> So, for instance, &quot;The Vampire&quot; is not a classic heroic archetype - and it's an archetype that Abyssals can/should do better than Solars. (And you could really break that down into a number of different archetypes - the seductive life-stealer, the creature of the night, the father of the undead, the walking infection, and so on.) &quot;The Monster&quot; is not a classic heroic archetype, and it's one that Lunars and Infernals both do better (albeit in very different ways). &quot;The Titan&quot; is Infernal property. &quot;The Elemental&quot; belongs to the Dragon-Blooded. &quot;The Shapeshifter&quot; is the Lunars'. &quot;The Agent of the Gods&quot; is for Sidereals. Again, each of these subdivides, and I'm not providing an all-encompassing list - but the point is that these are <i>different</i> archetypes, and ones where the other splats tell the story better (and in a different way!) than Solars can.<br /> <br /> These are also narrower archetypes, yes. And they're primarily means- rather than ends-focused, yes - they do not outperform Solars, in general, at accomplishing tasks of raw power. That's why the Solars are the default player splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:38:52-07:00","id":208368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208148#post208148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of going round and round rehashing the same arguments over and over again and theorycrafting, why don't we try and give examples from real campaigns.<br /> <br /> TL/DR: Play to your splat's strengths and your character will not be weaker than your friend's solar (if you use the same xp &amp; advancement tables). You are probably much broader in capabilties, thanks to shapeshifting/fate stuff/arrays for the same xp. Solars really can't do everything at once in actual play. Even then, Solar's are not very subtle in most areas, being golden, shiny leadertypes, while Lunars and Sidereals certainly can be. Play to the splat's strengths and you'll be just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about this. Being a subtle manipulator should totally be a solar thing, same with a big beefy bodyguard. It seems to me more that effects that solars should have but don't have written. <br /> <br /> Playing non solar splats shouldn't be about &quot;oh hey if I do this maybe I can equal a solar.&quot; It should be about using your restrictions to be interesting. For instance if you need to convince some lord about something a solar could slip into his room while he was sleeping and whisper it into his mind, or just convince him of it outright with an epic speech. A lunar might have to kill somebody close to him, take their form and tell him from a source he trusts, or a DB would probably have to bend over backwards because non of his magic directly applies here. It's fun to do that sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:51:05-07:00","id":208455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208353#post208353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you want, say, a Fire-Aspect or Abyssal Charm where you burn down a library and absorb the knowledge as the books go up in smoke - well, okay! Solars aren't going to have that, because that's not really about <i>learning</i>, it's about your connection to elemental fire or to destruction. (One might quibble whether this is an appropriate Charm for either of those splats, but that's not really my major point.) Perhaps that's a means by which you could end up with the effect of absorbing information faster, but it's not because they're the Learning Exalts more than Solars are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm.... Yeah, you could have something like that<br /> <br /> &quot;The Dragon-blooded learns to control the essence of his intellect and thirst for knowledge channeling fire essence into a work of knowledge made from flammable materials. <br /> <br /> While she commits essence it burns with smoking fire and is hot to the touch, but is not consumed by flame and does not give off any heat.<br /> <br /> Her mind moves with the speed of flame, seeing and absorbing patterns of information in the smoke and flame, learning the information at an increased rate&quot;<br /> <br /> Exactly as you say, that's not really being &quot;better at learning&quot; as you say. What it is an effortful learned skillful piece of magic that is rooted in learning, involves the power of the mind and involves control and integration and functionally allows the character to learn, faster.<br /> <br /> If she were just able to burn books just because (without learning or understanding the magic that led to it) and magically the knowledge pops into her head, that probably would not quite &quot;fit&quot; as a Dragonblooded Charm, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:55:45-07:00","id":208469,"title":"","content":"Those are some cool Charm ideas I'll have to steal. Abyssal Lore/Linguistics (burn the books and breathe in the smoke gives you the knowledge from in the books - fits the destruction theme) or DB Presence/Socialize (hard to hammer that into a particular Fire Aspect Ability).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:12:27-07:00","id":208487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208469#post208469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are some cool Charm ideas I'll have to steal. Abyssal Lore/Linguistics (burn the books and breathe in the smoke gives you the knowledge from in the books - fits the destruction theme) or DB Presence/Socialize (hard to hammer that into a particular Fire Aspect Ability).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be a Fire Aspect Ability particularly; you could make it a Fire Aspect Lore/Linguistics Charm (as we're told in the 3e DB preview that Abilities will have Charms for different elements)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:15:32-07:00","id":208488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208487#post208487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as we're told in the 3e DB preview that Abilities will have Charms for different elements</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Elemental keyword? In any case, cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208105#post208105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe part of the problem here is that the previous edition was broken, but had people saying the same things. Like when a supposedly challenging circle of immaculate essence 5 DBs god soloed by the Dawn while everyone else watches, or when a night caste ninja knocked out you and your whole lunar circle without effort. Then you see on the forums &quot;of course that happened, Solars are the most powerful!&quot;. When really there should be some doubt as to the outcome of that fight and if one night caste wants to capture four Lunars at once he'd better pull out all the stops and even then might not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the statements about 3e are that a Dawn picking a fight with a Sworn Brotherhood of DBs is either going to want a really good plan or backup, and certainly should not expect to win as a default, or even get away without some injuries. Which sounds great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-25-2014, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:01:45-07:00","id":208534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208488#post208488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the Elemental keyword? In any case, cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemme quote. From the 3e DB preview PDF:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actual conversation we had (paraphrased):<br /> \u201cIt\u2019s always kind of sucked that if you wanted to play an Air<br /> Aspect swordsman, all your Charms were fire magic, and you<br /> couldn\u2019t do wind-slashes or anything like that, and came off as<br /> kind of a wannabe Fire Aspect.\u201d<br /> \u201cWell, there was Dragon-Graced Blade and Dragon-Graced<br /> Arrow and stuff, but that was just one Charm, and you can only<br /> use that format for kind of generic effects, not highly-specific<br /> ones like a long-range cutting wind slash. Long-range cutting<br /> wind doesn\u2019t translate to say, Wood. And getting a mix of el-<br /> ementally influenced Charms into the various Abilities would<br /> require more wordcount being allocated into the Charmset\u2026<br /> you couldn\u2019t do that with a Charms chapter the size of the pre-<br /> vious ones.\u201d<br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d<br /> \u201cWait, hold on, what am I saying? We\u2019re the ones who get to<br /> decide how big the chapters are now.\u201d<br /> Dragon-Blooded in Exalted Third Edition will still use Abil-<br /> ity-based Charms, but we\u2019re going to expand their elemental<br /> palette beyond what First or Second Edition could do, so that<br /> Abilities are not only encompassed by a single element. Ele-<br /> mental influence will usually predominate in an Ability\u2014Sail<br /> will obviously be strongly water-influenced, and Archery by<br /> Wood\u2014but Third Edition Dragon-Blooded will display more<br /> elemental diversity in their magic, pointing to their unity as<br /> a Terrestrial host, and providing a greater array of character<br /> style options. Botanical Crafts techniques, flame-omen Occult<br /> Charms, Brawl attacks with fists like granite, aquatic mobility<br /> Athletics Charms, and other elemental fusions will all be pos-<br /> sible in Exalted Third Edition. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:31:57-07:00","id":208564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208366#post208366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for instance, &quot;The Vampire&quot; is not a classic heroic archetype - and it's an archetype that Abyssals can/should do better than Solars. (And you could really break that down into a number of different archetypes - the seductive life-stealer, the creature of the night, the father of the undead, the walking infection, and so on.) &quot;The Monster&quot; is not a classic heroic archetype, and it's one that Lunars and Infernals both do better (albeit in very different ways). &quot;The Titan&quot; is Infernal property. &quot;The Elemental&quot; belongs to the Dragon-Blooded. &quot;The Shapeshifter&quot; is the Lunars'. &quot;The Agent of the Gods&quot; is for Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>These archetypes do not preclude the basics. In fact, the way Exalted is set up, they <i>can't </i>preclude the basics, because Abyssals and Sidereals and whatnot still have Ability Charms, and more importantly, they're all still humans and heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:49:48-07:00","id":208578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208534#post208534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lemme quote. From the 3e DB preview PDF:<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a lot better than before and makes a lot more sense than before and removes yet another layer of power that weakened the dragon blood. The out of aspect tax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T13:06:09-07:00","id":208587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208564#post208564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These archetypes do not preclude the basics. In fact, the way Exalted is set up, they <i>can't </i>preclude the basics, because Abyssals and Sidereals and whatnot still have Ability Charms, and more importantly, they're all still humans and heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>but still, a Solar cant play a Vampire, Zombie or things related to undeath, you need either the Abyssal or Liminal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T13:11:55-07:00","id":208591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208587#post208587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but still, a Solar cant play a Vampire, Zombie or things related to undeath, you need either the Abyssal or Liminal</div> </div> </div> </div>True, a Solar can't play to vampire themes - but a Lunar certainly can. They do it differently than Abyssals do, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T13:43:11-07:00","id":208609,"title":"","content":"but an Abyssal cant play the minotaur, harpy, chimera. Also i cant think of one now but im sure ther are many others undead archetypes than an Abyssac can play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 07-25-2014, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T13:54:17-07:00","id":208638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208020#post208020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, though: it is perfectly viable to build those other archetypes as other types of Exalts. Most of them will approach them through the lens of their themes, some can't quite cover all of those archetypes without approaching them in odd ways. The fact that all of these Exalts have weaknesses and things they can't do makes them all interesting.<br /> <br /> The exception is Solars. Solars can do everything, and they can do it better than anyone else. The only things they can't do aren't important because they have different, usually better ways of doing anything those things enable you to do. They don't need to be able to shapeshift because they have better, faster ways of doing almost anything you would use shapeshifting in order to do. They don't need to be able to manipulate Fate because they can already manipulate people and groups to do what they want much more easily than having to work around the restrictions of Fate manipulation. In a game where everyone else is made interesting by their restrictions as much as their powers, Solars are the guys without any restrictions. As a result they're boring at the same time as they take away from everyone else by making it Doing It Wrong to build a Lunar out to become a skilled swordsman because nope, being skilled isn't using your powers effectively and together with your mundane prowess, it's having Solar powers. Everyone else's powers aren't real skills, they're ways of cheating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noooo.<br /> <br /> I mean, sort of. If your goal when building a non-Solar character is &quot;be obviously better than an equally-experienced Melee-focused Solar at swordsmanship in a white-room fight&quot;, you've set an uphill battle for yourself. Solars are defined as the mightiest of the Exalted, and challenging the mightiest of the Exalted at the core of what they do is going to be hard mode at the best of times.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean you're Doing It Wrong to build a Lunar swordsman, for a wide variety of reasons. First, most obviously, &quot;be better than a Solar&quot; is not the purpose of the game. A Lunar swordsman will be terrifyingly skilled, and the fact that the Solar charmset is somewhat more suitable for building a mighty swordsman doesn't change that unless you define your entire character concept around beating Solars at sword fights. Even <i>then</i>, the fact that you're at a bit of a disadvantage is not a bad thing; Solars are supposed to be overwhelming, yes, but that also makes them good challenges. You've just set a difficult goal for yourself, that's all.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, though, your thematic, as a Lunar, gives you other capabilities beyond just skill at a sword, even if your character concept is &quot;Lunar swordsman&quot; and you invest everything in the Lunar charms that make you good at swording. (This isn't true for Solars -- an all-Melee Solar is going to be pure Melee. I mean, they can use Melee weapons other than swords, but that's about it.) You are a master of shapeshifting. You have impossibly-good strength and dexterity, and an entire array of related capabilities stemming from those. You have... whatever Lunar thematics give you beyond that. (Yes, yes, I know.) If you completely, deliberately ignore all these things, yes, you're at a disadvantage, because it means that when you climbed the Lunar Dexterity tree you were probably buying prerequisite charms that let you do other non-sword related feats of dexterity and then <i>not using them</i>. I mean, duh, that's going to put you at a disadvantage? As a Lunar, you can use the same charms you use to swordfight in order to fight barehanded or with ranged weapons. You don't have to (you're also very good with a sword, sure), but that's part of your capabilities, and if you want to discuss how you measure up to a Solar you have to include it; if you refuse to include it then you're going to look worse.<br /> <br /> Likewise, you don't have to use your shapeshifting (and can still be very good without it), but... if you remove your shapeshifting, you don't get to then compare yourself to a Solar and say &quot;hey, why does it look like something is missing?&quot; Because, well, <i>yes</i>, something is missing in that case.<br /> <br /> The way I've described it before is to picture the array of Solar capabilities as a chessboard. Solars developing their abilities cover each square one at a time, putting a little square piece of paper on each one to mark them as claimed. Lunars (or other splats) instead place oddly-shaped pieces of paper on the board, half-covering (from a Solar perspective) unusual assortments of squares at once. You can still get things that make you very very good with a sword, but the way you expand over that range of capabilities means that it's not your core <i>thing</i> the way it is for some Dawns. Conversely, a Dawn has to pay a lot more to get the combination of mobility, stealth, and varied combat tactics that a Lunar can get very cheaply and easily; the straightforward way they expand their abilities doesn't let them compete well with Lunars at the particular suite of skills we might call &quot;being a Lunar.&quot; They can't shapeshift, yes, but that's not irrelevant fluff the way you're dismissing it -- Lunars, by advancing their shapeshifting abilities, get to improve at combat, stealth, mobility, and a variety of other things all at once. A Dawn who wanted to keep up with a Lunar at that would need to spread themselves over three or four different abilities, which would cost them a lot more. (Dawns like that still exist, but it would be their entire character concept, whereas the Lunar can be &quot;master shapeshifter&quot; and get really good at all those things while still having a lot left over to invest in other areas.)<br /> <br /> Basically, different splats grow in different ways, which means that they're more suitable for some concepts than others, even if they can still be really good at stuff that isn't directly part of their core concept.<br /> <br /> As far as the whole &quot;everyone else's powers aren't real skills&quot; goes -- well, sort of. They're skills, but they're skills at eg. being a Sidereal or being a Lunar, which involves some concepts that are more than just &quot;really good at a sword&quot; or &quot;really good at studying.&quot; If you want to be able to advance through a charm tree and take nothing but &quot;really good at swording&quot; charms, you should play a Solar, because that's part of their concept. You should only play a Lunar if you want to be really good at being a <i>Lunar</i> -- which can include eg. a concept like &quot;Lunar swordsman&quot;, but the 'Lunar' part of that definition means you get a variety of powers that go beyond just supernatural skill with a sword, and that in really tough fights with people like Solars, you have to leverage those other powers to operate at full capacity. If you don't want those, don't play a Lunar? I mean, what you're saying amounts to either &quot;I want to play a Lunar, but with no unique Lunar abilities, just supernaturally keen swordsmanship skill&quot; or &quot;I want to play a Lunar, and keep all the unique Lunar abilities, while being as good at supernaturally keen swordsmanship skill as a sword-focused Solar.&quot; Even aside from the Solar preeminence thing, that doesn't make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-25-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:25:45-07:00","id":208684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208020#post208020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only things they can't do aren't important because they have different, usually better ways of doing anything those things enable you to do. They don't need to be able to shapeshift because they have better, faster ways of doing almost anything you would use shapeshifting in order to do. They don't need to be able to manipulate Fate because they can already manipulate people and groups to do what they want much more easily than having to work around the restrictions of Fate manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bad way of looking at it. I would absolutely disagree that Solars have consistently <i>better</i> ways of accomplishing certain goals compared to shapeshifting, full stop. Partially because shapeshifting is built-in functionality that requires no additional XP investment to be an incredible toolkit. A Lunar can purchase zero &quot;be better at shapeshifting&quot; Knacks (to use the 2e terminology) and still be able to eat a mouse and then a hawk and then a rhino and use all of those forms to their fullest. For a Solar to be as quiet and unobtrusive as a mouse, or as dangerous and powerful as a rhino, or to fly and be sharp-sighted like a hawk, they need to invest in quite different sets of Charms, and those are just three examples. This is just at a baseline, before the Lunar adds their own Charms to those forms.<br /> <br /> Holden had quite a good quote about this, archived on Chancel Aleph:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's the First Age. To settle a bet, Luna and another Luna that she has spun off, gotten drunk with, and started betting against, call all 300 Solars and all 300 Lunars to assemble in a great big god damned field. Around the edge of this field are 600 identical castles, each guarded by well-trained mortal soldiers. At the center of each castle is a MacGuffin.<br /> Each Solar and each Lunar is assigned a different castle. They have one night to sneak into this castle, retrieve the MacGuffin, and sneak back out. In doing so, they may incapacitate no more than three guards and may not cause the general alarm to be raised. Whichever group of Exalts has the most MacGuffins come morning wins.<br /> The Lunars are going to win this contest. They are going to win it easily, because all of them have the wherewithal to make a decent go at this. The Solars who can do it, will do it much more easily, but there are plenty of them who have like Stealth 0, Larceny 0, and whose only option is to head in like Popeye on a Spinach bender.<br /> This does not make them better than Solars. It does not even make them better at stealth infiltration than Solars. It just makes them Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm getting at, why it's sometimes true but often not to say that Solars have tools to be better infiltrators than Lunars. Sure they do, and especially in a white-room scenario that doesn't consider XP. But more practically, they don't, <i>unless they choose to</i>. If they choose to, yes, they'll be better infiltrators (expressed in a different way) but not all of them will choose to.<br /> <br /> Discussing Fate manipulation is tricky, since so many of the mechanics for it have been absolutely overpriced, useless, horribly implemented, or a combination of those 3, and it's hard to imagine them implemented well - Astrology sucked in 1e just as bad as in 2e. But if you flat-out look at Solar vs Sidereal Charms, there have been a lot of comments about the closed Charmset putting effects there that work in weird ways - those weird ways letting them be more effective than Solar Charms in some way, with the balance idea being cost, or the closed set itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208069#post208069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to beat a Solar, you find their human flaw and exploit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. More like you exploit the holes in their competencies, because nobody can be good at everything, and the way they express their power (through Abilities, and in a relatively direct, human-like manner) is, of a necessity, quite a bit more narrow than those who express power through Attributes, or through Abilities but in a weird or inhuman way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-25-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:51:37-07:00","id":208724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208638#post208638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I've described it before is to picture the array of Solar capabilities as a chessboard. Solars developing their abilities cover each square one at a time, putting a little square piece of paper on each one to mark them as claimed. Lunars (or other splats) instead place oddly-shaped pieces of paper on the board, half-covering (from a Solar perspective) unusual assortments of squares at once. You can still get things that make you very very good with a sword, but the way you expand over that range of capabilities means that it's not your core <i>thing</i> the way it is for some Dawns. Conversely, a Dawn has to pay a lot more to get the combination of mobility, stealth, and varied combat tactics that a Lunar can get very cheaply and easily; the straightforward way they expand their abilities doesn't let them compete well with Lunars at the particular suite of skills we might call &quot;being a Lunar.&quot; They can't shapeshift, yes, but that's not irrelevant fluff the way you're dismissing it -- Lunars, by advancing their shapeshifting abilities, get to improve at combat, stealth, mobility, and a variety of other things all at once. A Dawn who wanted to keep up with a Lunar at that would need to spread themselves over three or four different abilities, which would cost them a lot more. (Dawns like that still exist, but it would be their entire character concept, whereas the Lunar can be &quot;master shapeshifter&quot; and get really good at all those things while still having a lot left over to invest in other areas.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this about the combinations is important - it's really important that other splats patterns of buying Charms doesn't just *feel* like &quot;Oh, forced inefficient multiclassing... in combinations no one wants that doesn't match up to the character concepts this splat sells&quot; or &quot;Solars get more ability to specialise. sadface.&quot;... where you just feel like buying Lunar close combat Charms is the equivalent of being forced to be a weaker Solar who is forced to split exp between Melee and Brawl, particularly due to the fact this multi skilling is horribly suboptimal in Exalted.<br /> <br /> It should *ideally* feel like your splat's options for specialisation are as efficient (to get to broad goals that humans would want to get to), and desirable, just different in shape from purely ability focused lenses. Or more likely, given Ex's power hierarchy, that they at least *could* be and it is a deliberate decision where they aren't (not just clunky design).<br /> <br /> That's the ideal, I think. It seems difficult to achieve when being Ability oriented is built into the base of the system, compared to games with freeform Aspects and stuff.<br /> <br /> Basically a lot of this is about salesmanship and packaging powers together which will generally be desirable together - powers that help achieve the broad goals that a character with the prerequisite is generally going to care about and desire (e.g. lots of winning close combat fights, winning arguments, etc. powers together and stuff like that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:51:33-07:00","id":208860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208724#post208724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think this about the combinations is important - it's really important that other splats patterns of buying Charms doesn't just *feel* like &quot;Oh, forced inefficient multiclassing... in combinations no one wants that doesn't match up to the character concepts this splat sells&quot; or &quot;Solars get more ability to specialise. sadface.&quot;... where you just feel like buying Lunar close combat Charms is the equivalent of being forced to be a weaker Solar who is forced to split exp between Melee and Brawl, particularly due to the fact this multi skilling is horribly suboptimal in Exalted.<br /> <br /> It should *ideally* feel like your splat's options for specialisation are as efficient (to get to broad goals that humans would want to get to), and desirable, just different in shape from purely ability focused lenses. Or more likely, given Ex's power hierarchy, that they at least *could* be and it is a deliberate decision where they aren't (not just clunky design).<br /> <br /> That's the ideal, I think. It seems difficult to achieve when being Ability oriented is built into the base of the system, compared to games with freeform Aspects and stuff.<br /> <br /> Basically a lot of this is about salesmanship and packaging powers together which will generally be desirable together - powers that help achieve the broad goals that a character with the prerequisite is generally going to care about and desire (e.g. lots of winning close combat fights, winning arguments, etc. powers together and stuff like that).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars in particular have had a lot of problems with that.<br /> <br /> 1e Lunars were very one-note; they did one thing and nothing else.<br /> <br /> 2e Lunars separated shapeshifting out of the charmset, then made large portions of the charmset just copy-pastes of Solar stuff, encouraging players to basically view them as weaker Solars that can shapeshift as their secondary thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:47:22-07:00","id":208907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208469#post208469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are some cool Charm ideas I'll have to steal. Abyssal Lore/Linguistics (burn the books and breathe in the smoke gives you the knowledge from in the books - fits the destruction theme) or DB Presence/Socialize (hard to hammer that into a particular Fire Aspect Ability).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oHLw2lyLnA8\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I'm going to smoke you.&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T01:02:59-07:00","id":209190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=208366#post208366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Universal&quot; and &quot;classic&quot; aren't really the same thing at all here, though - particularly because, if I'm reading Jay correctly, he means &quot;classic&quot; specifically in the sense of &quot;classic heroic archetypes,&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> So, for instance, &quot;The Vampire&quot; is not a classic heroic archetype - and it's an archetype that Abyssals can/should do better than Solars. (And you could really break that down into a number of different archetypes - the seductive life-stealer, the creature of the night, the father of the undead, the walking infection, and so on.) &quot;The Monster&quot; is not a classic heroic archetype, and it's one that Lunars and Infernals both do better (albeit in very different ways). &quot;The Titan&quot; is Infernal property. &quot;The Elemental&quot; belongs to the Dragon-Blooded. &quot;The Shapeshifter&quot; is the Lunars'. &quot;The Agent of the Gods&quot; is for Sidereals. Again, each of these subdivides, and I'm not providing an all-encompassing list - but the point is that these are <i>different</i> archetypes, and ones where the other splats tell the story better (and in a different way!) than Solars can.<br /> <br /> These are also narrower archetypes, yes. And they're primarily means- rather than ends-focused, yes - they do not outperform Solars, in general, at accomplishing tasks of raw power. That's why the Solars are the default player splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I think it also has something to do with how people think Solars have no theme, because the themes they do have (the heroic archetypes/exemplary human skill) are broad enough and so widely used that often people don't even recognize them as distinct themes anymore, they just assume something to the effect of &quot;all characters fall in to one of these categories&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T04:22:16-07:00","id":209262,"title":"","content":"I like the phrasing used in that &quot;What is Exalted&quot; thing Holden put together, where the Solars are about &quot;unbound excellence and holy might&quot;, the latter of which I take to mean they carry a visual motif implying a certain level of righteousness in their persona and actions, in the fairly typical imagery. It is, however, just a visual convention (and maybe occasionally a slight bias in how their powers incline them to act, in terms of either mechanism or feedback rewards), rather than value judgement on the Solars, or implication that no Solar ever had doubts or moral dilemmas. (This is also why one can talk about Infernals having blasphemous might without it necessarily reflecting on their character; they're not necessarily bad, their powers just work in a freaky fashion and visuals that people might be inclined to view as transgressive).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:48:57-07:00","id":210585,"title":"","content":"To add to what I said above, an example of how you can use shapeshifting to help you as a Lunar swordsman. Let's say you have a Solar adversary -- someone totally and completely invested in swordsmanship.<br /> <br /> You attack him, trying to swordfight him to the death. Since he's the ultimate master of the sword, he's winning. Your shapeshifting allows you to turn into a bird and fly away.<br /> <br /> Well that's not a very fun way to use shapeshifting, right? But here's the thing. As a bird, you keep stalking him. The next day, resuming human form, you attack him again. He wins and you're forced to retreat a second time. Solars really are bullshit, aren't they?<br /> <br /> This repeats six times. On the seventh time -- whether by luck, or because you've been studying his strategies the whole time, or because you chose a perfect time to attack, or because you were using your faster recovery to wear him out, whatever -- you get the upper hand. Realizing he's going to lose, he throws down his sword and tries to run the way you did the past six times.<br /> <br /> You turn into a huge wolf, chase him down, and eat him. The end. The Solar may have beaten you six out of seven fights, but you survived and ultimately won by fighting as a Lunar. You don't need to use shapeshifting in combat directly in order to do that. That's an example of how a Lunar swordsman fights, at least against really dangerous opponents like Solars. Note that the overarching story still has you beating him as a swordsman, even if it's in the context of a Lunar swordsman using Lunar tricks to support it -- you fought him for seven days, but despite his vast skill he could never kill you because you were cunning and slippery and tough, and on the seventh day you killed him. You wouldn't have been able to do that if you weren't also really really good with your sword.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I'm aware that in 2e you wouldn't be able to do that because you'd probably be formlocked, but I'm talking in terms of the broad concept for how splats' themes interact -- obviously Lunars have had issues.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:15:05-07:00","id":210606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=210585#post210585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add to what I said above, an example of how you can use shapeshifting to help you as a Lunar swordsman. Let's say you have a Solar adversary -- someone totally and completely invested in swordsmanship.<br /> <br /> You attack him, trying to swordfight him to the death. Since he's the ultimate master of the sword, he's winning. Your shapeshifting allows you to turn into a bird and fly away.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Or</i>, you use your Dexterity and Strength Charms, which aren't about swordfighting but sure <i>help</i>, and so you have a cool swordfight which you may or may not win, depending on a number of factors, including but not limited to location, superior strategy, various social actions, and luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:32:32-07:00","id":210612,"title":"","content":"A solar can become a great swordsman. A lunar can become really really good at killing things with a sword. Therein lies the key difference, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:38:44-07:00","id":210668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=210606#post210606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Or</i>, you use your Dexterity and Strength Charms, which aren't about swordfighting but sure <i>help</i>, and so you have a cool swordfight which you may or may not win, depending on a number of factors, including but not limited to location, superior strategy, various social actions, and luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you totally can. You might even win. You can totally make a Lunar swordsman and be really skilled with a sword, and you can totally leverage your awesome dexterity and strength to that end.<br /> <br /> But like I said above, the issue is that if you do that, and try to fight a Solar as a Lunar without using your shapeshifting (or other completely-unique Lunar powers) to get a any benefit at all in any form, you're going to be at a disadvantage that goes beyond just &quot;Solars too stronk&quot;, because you've deliberately chosen to ignore one of your most powerful capabilities. There's nothing <i>wrong</i> with that -- sometimes it can be cool to fight with one arm tied behind your back and still win -- but you don't get to then complain &quot;that fight was totally bullshit, the Solar was better than me at swordfighting even though I invested everything in charms I thought would make me better at it!&quot; Because... you haven't. The power to shapeshift is yours even if you're choosing not use it, and that's part of your overarching design.<br /> <br /> If you play a Lunar, and try to fight a Solar, relying solely on the way your Dexterity and Strength charms can help you attack and defend with a sword in a natural human fashion, and nothing else? You will be at a significant disadvantage. You have <i>chosen</i> to place yourself at a significant disadvantage by foregoing what's intended to be one of your biggest strengths. That can be a cool and exciting thing to do, and you still have a chance of winning, but... you're not going to be as strong as the Lunar who cleverly tries to find ways to use shapeshifting to get an advantage at every opportunity. How could you be?<br /> <br /> (Remember, Lunars are not just &quot;the attribute Exalted, who are the best at everything that falls under an Attribute&quot;, because doing so ultimately just turns them into Silver Solars, doing mostly the same things as Solars but with slightly different justification. Shapeshifting, and themes related to it, are built into their entire design from the ground up; and there will probably be other unique themes introduced and explored in 3e. If you just want to be the strongest man in the world and don't care about anything else, I would hesitate before recommending Lunars, because they have a lot of other things built into them that are core to their design, too.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=210612#post210612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar can become a great swordsman. A lunar can become really really good at killing things with a sword. Therein lies the key difference, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a Lunar can become a great swordsman, too; remember that we're talking matters of degrees here. Lunars lack specific sword-focused charms, but that's not necessarily an impediment, and their strength and dexterity <i>do</i> help them to become a great swordsman. If you're a Lunar and have Melee 5, MA 5, and have mastered a secret CMA sword style, which you use with your sword's evocations and your own Strength and Dexterity charms, I don't know what else to call you.<br /> <br /> My objection is purely to the people who look at that character, refuse to consider the advantages of shapeshifting or the other &quot;inhuman&quot; effects of Lunar charms, and then say &quot;...but overall, I'm not quite as good as it as the Solar who does the same thing! <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wkrLwPtEQ9c\" target=\"_blank\">That's not fair!</a>&quot; Well, yes, when you lopped all those bits off you sort of ensured it, didn't you? Lunars are designed to tell different stories than Solars, which means that the game is going to try and make your Lunar swordsman look, feel, and play as distinctly as possible from the Solar swordsman, <i>especially</i> by encouraging you to use things that are outside the Solar theme. If you don't like that unique Lunar story... why are you playing a Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-27-2016, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:47:24-07:00","id":210695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=210612#post210612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar can become a great swordsman. A lunar can become really really good at killing things with a sword. Therein lies the key difference, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit of an aside here, but -- It's not really useful to speak in absolute terms rather than relative ones, because &quot;ridiculously amazing&quot; is the baseline for Exalted. If you have 8-11 dice in swording people, you are already a great swordsman before you buy a single charm or technique. If you're an Exalt whose theme is &quot;great swordsman&quot; you were probably already a great swordsman as a mortal!<br /> <br /> I mean, this has limited practical relevance when you're fighting &quot;all my charms are in Melee&quot; Solar Timmy, but that isn't the measure of whether or not your character is a great swordsman. You can outfight a hundred people and end up standing on a huge pile of bodies, you can keep from getting wet in a storm by cutting the raindrops in half before they hit you, you can split stone without pitting your blade by striking it in exactly the right place. You're a fuckin' great swordsman!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T01:05:53-07:00","id":210956,"title":"","content":"It's a good example of how a Lunar *might* proceed, I wouldn't take it over literally as that being the only way the Lunar could triumph - there's some space between &quot;Using only Strength and Dexterity Charms which aren't shapeshifting based in a fight&quot; and &quot;Using shapeshifting only to run away from fights&quot;, where you use Strength and Dexterity Charms and shapeshifting of a sort that makes you stronger and physically and mentally faster and sharper and tougher all together to win the fight, in the fight without ever running away, without needing to lose like, 6 out of 7 times and flee or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T01:35:29-07:00","id":210964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=210668#post210668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, a Lunar can become a great swordsman, too</div> </div> </div> </div>That was sort of my point. There's no real difference between the end results, but a solar gets there through unparalleled skill with a sword, whereas a lunar gets there through unparalleled might whilst <i>holding</i> a sword. A solar surpasses a mortal swordsman by doing things they could not. A lunar surpasses a mortal swordsman by doing things they could <i>much, much harder</i>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T02:27:10-07:00","id":211001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=210668#post210668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, Lunars are not just &quot;the attribute Exalted, who are the best at everything that falls under an Attribute&quot;, because doing so ultimately just turns them into Silver Solars, doing mostly the same things as Solars but with slightly different justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>From where I'm standing, it looks like you're the one invoking Silver Solars, what with Lunar Charms somehow not being &quot;completely-unique Lunar powers&quot; and only allowing you to... &quot;attack and defend [...] in a natural human fashion.&quot;<br /> Is that really what you expect of the splat-specific Charms of the crazy shapeshifting god-monster-heroes?<br /> But I guess that's not pertinent.<br /> <br /> Look, it's like this: if EX3 is anything like advertised, Solars being &quot;the mightiest&quot; will not translate to sheer numerical superiority, and, more importantly, Lunar Charms will confer certain advantages Solar Charms <i>don't </i>(like, say, Hella Snakes Prana). And vice versa, of course.<br /> Point is, Lunars are more than turning into animals, even if turning into animals can be a powerful advantage (if you have the right shapes, and know when to use them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:38:43-07:00","id":211669,"title":"","content":"By a D&amp;D analogy, the central question becomes, from the perspective of the core rulebook, are the other Exalted supposed to be the other classes? Or are they the creatures from the Monster Manual (who then have dedicated supplements to allow you to play)?<br /> <br /> If they other Exalted are supposed to be the other classes, then Solars having foremost competence at all human endeavors is a problem. &quot;Solars are better at being fighters than members of the fighter class are at being fighters!&quot; is a problem.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the Sidereals are mind flayers and the Dragon-Blooded are the beholders and the Lunars are the werewolves, it doesn't matter that the Solars are the best fighters, thieves, wizards, and clerics. &quot;Solars are better at being fighters than mind flayers are at being fighters!&quot; is not a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:47:54-07:00","id":211677,"title":"","content":"From the perspective of the core rulebook and nothing else, Solars are the only Exalt type who have detailed chargen rules and a list of powers that can be played as comprehensive without really limiting any character concepts or options, while all other Exalts are presented as sample statblocks in the Antagonists section. Make of that what you will. (Maybe I'm being too literalist, but).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:52:17-07:00","id":211682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=211677#post211677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of the core rulebook and nothing else, Solars are the only Exalt type who have detailed chargen rules and a list of powers that can be played as comprehensive without really limiting any character concepts or options, while all other Exalts are presented as sample statblocks in the Antagonists section. Make of that what you will. (Maybe I'm being too literalist, but).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this, maybe more than the other two editions, is true. Solars are the PCs, the other splats are like playing an all troll game or all drow game or something. Not prohibited but not really what it's designed for. That's what it kind of feels to me anyway, if you've got a concept you've got a solar, and also maybe another type of exalt, but solar always works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:54:06-07:00","id":211683,"title":"","content":"Also I'm not complaining either, without the BS of the previous editions I'd like not to have to choose between cool concept and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:05:21-07:00","id":211687,"title":"","content":"Well, that's not entirely true. Solar doesn't <i>always</i> work (if you really want to play a political bureaucrat game in Heaven and basically be James Bond piping in all over Creation, you'll be hard-pressed to find a better fit than Sidereals; if you want to play a literal shapeshifter, well, Lunars duh). The Exalted game rules are written with an assumption that other types will come out, so it's not exactly like D&amp;D releasing Savage Species years and years after the core rules come out (D&amp;D always felt like it added that stuff for book sales, rather than planning to release them from the start; Exalted probably always intended to release at least DBs and Sidereals as playable splats in 1e - Lunars weren't planned in long-term advance and hence that book was so damn bad).<br /> <br /> I also feel like the core conceit of the game (&quot;after 2000 years, the Solars have returned in force&quot;) is a sudden jarring to the world that breaks centuries-old stalemates: suddenly the Wyld Hunt is wholly inadequate to hunt down so many Anathema, suddenly the Lunars have more breathing room with attention diverted elsewhere; suddenly stable satrapies start to revolt as honey-tongued prophets and shining generals incite rebellion. The Solars have stories to tell, but simply their return opens up avenues for so many other stories that would be much harder to tell in, say, RY 520.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=211683#post211683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">without the BS of the previous editions I'd like not to have to choose between cool concept and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously amen to that. When you have strict power tiers and pretty much all splats except Solaroids have broken mechanics, it's really hard to figure out a convincing reason not to play a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:44:08-07:00","id":211752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=211669#post211669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By a D&amp;D analogy, the central question becomes, from the perspective of the core rulebook, are the other Exalted supposed to be the other classes? Or are they the creatures from the Monster Manual (who then have dedicated supplements to allow you to play)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a false dichotomy. From the perspective of the corebook, they're all NPCs: allies, rivals, lovers, end-bosses, and random jerks you sword at to show how cool you are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T16:08:07-07:00","id":211771,"title":"","content":"Well unlike previous editions I can be a solar forest warrior in green jade armor with a green jade bow that turns sticks into arrows as their drawn on the bowstring, and fire out a thorny cascade supplemented with solar archery. You could also be an awesome solar agent of heaven, employed by the gold faction with a fate stealing starmetal daiklave. It's just so easy to adapt any concept to being a solar unless it's hyper specific. Which again, is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}